// נוצר אוטומטית מ-sims-src/ ע"י tools/build-sims.js. לא לערוך כאן.
const SIM_SETS = {"p0rc1":{"id":"p0rc1","tier":0,"type":"rc","title":"Surviving the Antarctic Winter","text":["Winter in Antarctica is one of the hardest seasons on Earth. For months the sun hardly rises, the temperature can fall below minus 40 degrees Celsius, and strong winds blow across the ice. Most animals leave long before winter arrives. Emperor penguins, however, stay. In fact, this is when they raise their young.","Part of the answer lies in their bodies. A penguin has a thick layer of fat under its skin, which keeps heat inside. Its feathers are short and grow very close together, and they overlap like the tiles on a roof, so cold air and water cannot easily reach the skin. In the legs, warm blood that flows down to the feet heats the cold blood coming back up, so very little heat escapes through the feet.","Still, a good body alone is not enough in the worst storms. For this reason, emperor penguins depend on one another. In bad weather, thousands of birds stand close together in a group called a huddle. Inside the huddle, the temperature can rise above 20 degrees. The birds at the edge are much colder, but the group moves slowly all the time. As a result, each penguin gets turns both in the warm center and at the cold edge.","This teamwork is especially important for the fathers. After the female lays her single egg, she walks back to the sea to feed, and the male holds the egg on his feet under a warm fold of skin. For about two months he eats nothing. Without the shared heat of the huddle, few fathers would have enough energy to keep the egg safe until the chick hatches."],"qs":[{"q":"The passage mainly discusses","o":["why most animals leave Antarctica in winter","how penguin chicks are fed by their parents","how emperor penguins survive the Antarctic winter","the dangers of strong winds on the Antarctic ice"],"a":2,"ex":"כל הקטע עוסק בדרכים שבהן פינגווין הקיסר שורד את החורף: הגוף שלו (פסקה 2), הקבוצה הצפופה (פסקה 3) והאב ששומר על הביצה (פסקה 4). זה שרוב בעלי החיים עוזבים מוזכר רק במשפט אחד בפסקה 1.","w":[["survive","לשרוד"],["mainly","בעיקר"]]},{"q":"According to the second paragraph, a penguin's feathers help it by","o":["keeping cold air and water away from its skin","storing extra fat for the long winter","warming the blood that flows down to its feet","helping it swim faster in the cold sea"],"a":0,"ex":"בפסקה 2 כתוב שהנוצות צפופות ומונחות זו על זו כמו רעפים, ולכן אוויר קר ומים לא מגיעים בקלות לעור. השומן והדם ברגליים הם דרכים אחרות לשמור על חום, לא תפקיד של הנוצות.","w":[["feather","נוצה"],["reach","להגיע ל..."]]},{"q":"In the second paragraph, the word 'they' in 'they overlap like the tiles on a roof' refers to","o":["the tiles","the penguins","the layers of fat","the feathers"],"a":3,"ex":"המשפט אומר שהנוצות קצרות וצפופות «and they overlap», כלומר הנוצות הן שמונחות זו על זו. הרעפים (tiles) הם רק הדימוי שבא אחרי «like», לא הנושא של המשפט.","w":[["overlap","לחפוף, להיות מונח זה על זה"],["like","כמו"]]},{"q":"The main purpose of the last paragraph is to","o":["describe how young chicks learn to swim","explain why the huddle matters so much to the fathers","show that females care less about the egg than males","compare emperor penguins with other kinds of penguins"],"a":1,"ex":"הפסקה האחרונה פותחת ב«especially important for the fathers» ומסבירה שהאב לא אוכל חודשיים, ובלי החום של הקבוצה לא היה לו כוח לשמור על הביצה. הקטע לא אומר שהנקבה פחות אכפתית: היא פשוט הולכת לים כדי לאכול.","w":[["especially","במיוחד"],["purpose","מטרה"]]},{"q":"According to the third paragraph, the penguins at the edge of the huddle","o":["keep the center warm for the others all winter","are usually the strongest fathers","later get a turn in the warm center","leave the group to look for food"],"a":2,"ex":"בפסקה 3 כתוב שהקבוצה זזה כל הזמן, ולכן «As a result» כל פינגווין מקבל תור במרכז החם ותור בקצה הקר. האפשרות הראשונה סותרת את זה, כי אף אחד לא נשאר בקצה כל החורף.","w":[["as a result","כתוצאה מכך"],["edge","קצה, שוליים"],["turn","תור"]]}]},"p0rc2":{"id":"p0rc2","tier":0,"type":"rc","title":"Lungs of the City","text":["Today, almost every large city has public parks where anyone can walk, play or rest for free. For most of history, however, this was not the case. The large green spaces inside cities usually belonged to royal families and nobles, who used them for hunting or private walks. Ordinary people could enter them only on special days, if at all.","The situation began to change in the nineteenth century, when factories drew millions of people from villages into cities. Workers lived in small, crowded homes, and the air was thick with smoke. Diseases spread quickly, especially in the poorest areas. Some reformers began to call for open green spaces, which they described as the 'lungs' of the city. They believed that fresh air, trees and sunlight would make workers healthier and calmer.","One of the first parks built with public money for all citizens opened in 1847 in Birkenhead, near Liverpool, England. A few years later, a young American named Frederick Law Olmsted visited it. He was deeply impressed that rich and poor people walked along the same paths. Back home, he helped design Central Park in New York, which became a model for many other cities.","Not everyone, however, benefited equally. In New York, about 1,600 people, many of them poor, had to leave their homes to make room for Central Park. In addition, early parks had strict rules: visitors could not play ball on the grass or make noise. Over time, these rules became more relaxed, and parks added playgrounds and sports fields. Even so, the basic idea has stayed the same: a city needs places where nature is open to everyone."],"qs":[{"q":"Which of the following is the best title for the passage?","o":["How Public Parks Came to Cities","The Life of Frederick Law Olmsted","Why Factories Moved to the Countryside","The Strict Rules of Central Park"],"a":0,"ex":"הקטע מספר איך פארקים ציבוריים נוצרו בערים: מגנים פרטיים של משפחות מלוכה, דרך הרפורמות במאה ה-19, ועד הפארקים הראשונים. אולמסטד והחוקים הנוקשים הם רק חלק מהסיפור, ובקטע אנשים עברו מהכפרים לערים, לא ההפך.","w":[["public","ציבורי"],["title","כותרת"]]},{"q":"According to the second paragraph, reformers wanted open green spaces because they believed that","o":["parks would bring new factories to the city","rich families should open their gardens on special days","doctors needed more room to treat sick workers","fresh air and sunlight would improve workers' health"],"a":3,"ex":"בסוף פסקה 2 כתוב שהם האמינו שאוויר צח, עצים ואור שמש יהפכו את הפועלים לבריאים ורגועים יותר. הימים המיוחדים מוזכרים בפסקה 1, ושם מדובר במה שהיה לפני השינוי.","w":[["reformer","מתקן חברתי, איש רפורמה"],["believe","להאמין"]]},{"q":"According to the third paragraph, what impressed Olmsted in Birkenhead?","o":["The park was larger than any park in America.","Rich and poor people used the same paths.","The park had been designed by a famous American.","Workers were not allowed to enter the park."],"a":1,"ex":"בפסקה 3 כתוב שהוא התרשם מאוד מכך שעשירים ועניים הלכו באותם שבילים. האפשרות האחרונה הפוכה: הפארק נבנה בשביל כל האזרחים.","w":[["impressed","מתרשם, מלא הערכה"],["design","לתכנן, לעצב"]]},{"q":"In the last paragraph, the phrase 'became more relaxed' means that the rules became","o":["more famous","more confusing","less strict","less popular"],"a":2,"ex":"לפני כן כתוב שהחוקים היו נוקשים (strict): אסור לשחק בכדור ואסור לעשות רעש. «Over time» הם נעשו «relaxed», כלומר פחות נוקשים, ולכן אפשר היה להוסיף מגרשי משחקים וספורט.","w":[["relaxed","רגוע; (חוק) מקל, פחות נוקשה"],["strict","קפדני, נוקשה"]]},{"q":"The main purpose of the last paragraph is to","o":["point out some problems of the early parks and how they changed","explain why Olmsted moved back to England","prove that the early parks made workers healthier and calmer than before","describe how playgrounds and sports fields are built"],"a":0,"ex":"הפסקה פותחת ב«Not everyone, however, benefited equally» ומביאה בעיות: אנשים שפונו מבתיהם וחוקים נוקשים, ואחר כך מתארת איך החוקים התרככו. היא לא מוכיחה שהפארקים שיפרו את הבריאות, זו רק האמונה של הרפורמים בפסקה 2.","w":[["however","עם זאת, אולם"],["in addition","בנוסף"],["even so","למרות זאת, ובכל זאת"]]}]},"p0rc3":{"id":"p0rc3","tier":0,"type":"rc","title":"Why Do We Yawn?","text":["Almost everyone yawns several times a day, usually when they feel tired or bored. People are not the only ones who do it. Dogs, cats, monkeys, birds and even some fish open their mouths wide in a similar way. Although yawning is so common, scientists still do not fully understand why it happens.","For many years, the most popular explanation was that a yawn brings extra oxygen into the body. When we are tired, the idea went, we breathe slowly, so the body needs one deep breath to wake it up. However, experiments did not support this explanation. In one study, people breathed air with more oxygen than usual, yet they yawned just as often as before.","Today, many researchers believe that yawning helps to cool the brain. A deep yawn pulls cool air into the mouth and nose, which may lower the temperature of the blood flowing to the head. A slightly cooler brain may work better, which could explain why we often yawn when we are trying to stay awake. Supporting this idea, studies have found that people tend to yawn less when the air around them is very hot, since hot air cannot cool the brain.","Yawning has another strange feature: it spreads. Simply seeing or hearing someone yawn often makes us yawn too. People also catch yawns more easily from family and close friends than from strangers. Chimpanzees and dogs can catch yawns as well, but children under the age of four, who are still learning how others feel, rarely do. For this reason, some scientists think that catching a yawn may be connected to our ability to understand other people's feelings."],"qs":[{"q":"The passage mainly discusses","o":["the reasons people feel tired during the day","how dogs and chimpanzees learn from humans","an experiment that proved the oxygen explanation","different ideas about why people and animals yawn"],"a":3,"ex":"הקטע מציג כמה הסברים לפיהוק: חמצן (פסקה 2), קירור המוח (פסקה 3) והקשר להבנת רגשות (פסקה 4). הניסוי בפסקה 2 דווקא לא תמך בהסבר של החמצן, כך שהאפשרות השלישית הפוכה.","w":[["yawn","לפהק; פיהוק"],["explanation","הסבר"]]},{"q":"According to the second paragraph, when people in one study breathed air with more oxygen, they","o":["stopped yawning completely","yawned just as often as before","felt much more tired than before","yawned more often than before"],"a":1,"ex":"בסוף פסקה 2 כתוב «yet they yawned just as often as before», כלומר הם פיהקו באותה תדירות כמו קודם. לכן הניסוי לא תמך ברעיון שפיהוק נועד להכניס חמצן.","w":[["yet","ובכל זאת, אך"],["as... as","...כמו (באותה מידה)"]]},{"q":"In the second paragraph, the word 'it' in 'to wake it up' refers to","o":["the body","one deep breath","the idea","the oxygen"],"a":0,"ex":"לפי ההסבר הישן, כשאנחנו עייפים הגוף צריך נשימה עמוקה אחת כדי «להעיר אותו», כלומר להעיר את הגוף. הנשימה העמוקה היא הדבר שמעיר, לא מה שמתעורר.","w":[["breath","נשימה"],["wake up","להתעורר; להעיר"]]},{"q":"It can be inferred from the third paragraph that a person sitting in a very hot room would probably","o":["need more oxygen than usual","yawn more often than usual","feel more awake than usual","yawn less often than usual"],"a":3,"ex":"בפסקה 3 כתוב שאנשים נוטים לפהק פחות כשהאוויר סביבם חם מאוד, כי אוויר חם לא מקרר את המוח. «more often» הפוך ממה שכתוב.","w":[["infer","להסיק"],["tend to","לנטות ל..."],["since","מכיוון ש..."]]},{"q":"Why does the writer mention children under the age of four in the last paragraph?","o":["To show that young children yawn more often than adults do","To support a link between catching yawns and understanding others","To explain why young children need more sleep than adults","To prove that dogs understand feelings better than children"],"a":1,"ex":"ילדים מתחת לגיל ארבע, שעוד לומדים להבין מה אחרים מרגישים, כמעט לא «נדבקים» בפיהוק. «For this reason» המדענים חושבים שהדבקות בפיהוק קשורה ליכולת להבין רגשות של אחרים. הקטע לא אומר שילדים מפהקים יותר.","w":[["rarely","לעיתים רחוקות"],["for this reason","מסיבה זו"],["ability","יכולת"]]}]},"p1rc1":{"id":"p1rc1","tier":1,"type":"rc","title":"From Running Machine to Safety Bicycle","text":["In 1817, a German official named Karl Drais introduced a strange wooden vehicle that he called a \"running machine.\" It had two wheels in a line and a seat, but no pedals; riders pushed it forward with their feet. Drais may have hoped to replace horses, which had become costly to feed after several poor harvests. It was briefly fashionable, yet it was soon dismissed as a toy for wealthy young men.","The next major step came in France in the 1860s, when pedals were attached directly to the front wheel. This design, nicknamed the \"boneshaker,\" allowed riders to lift their feet off the ground, but its iron-rimmed wooden wheels made every bump painful. Because each turn of the pedals turned the front wheel only once, the only way to go faster was to make that wheel larger. By the 1870s, this logic had produced the \"high-wheeler,\" whose front wheel could be as tall as an adult. Fast but unstable, it could throw its rider over the handlebars after hitting a single stone.","The solution arrived in 1885 with the \"safety bicycle,\" designed in England. Its two wheels were roughly the same size, and the rider's pedals moved a chain that drove the rear wheel. Because the chain connected a large gear to a smaller one, a single turn of the pedals could turn the wheel several times, so speed no longer depended on wheel size. A few years later, air-filled rubber tires replaced solid ones, making the ride far smoother. The basic shape of the bicycle has hardly changed since then.","The safety bicycle did more than make cycling less dangerous. As mass production lowered prices, millions of ordinary workers could afford a cheap means of travel for the first time. Women in particular embraced it: the bicycle gave them a freedom of movement they had rarely enjoyed, and it even encouraged changes in fashion, since long, heavy skirts were difficult to ride in."],"qs":[{"q":"Which of the following is the best title for the passage?","o":["Karl Drais and the End of the Horse","Why Cycling Is Safer Than Riding a Horse","How the Bicycle Developed into Its Modern Form","The Bicycle's Influence on Women's Fashion"],"a":2,"ex":"הקטע עובר שלב אחר שלב: מכונת הריצה בלי דוושות, ה-boneshaker, ה-high-wheeler, ולבסוף ה-safety bicycle שהצורה שלו כמעט לא השתנתה מאז. האופנה של נשים מוזכרת רק בסוף הפסקה האחרונה, ולכן היא לא כותרת לכל הקטע.","w":[["develop","להתפתח, לפתח"],["introduce","להציג, להכניס (המצאה)"]]},{"q":"According to paragraph 2, bicycle makers in the 1870s built very large front wheels in order to","o":["make the bicycle go faster","make the ride more comfortable","prevent riders from falling off","lower the price of the bicycle"],"a":0,"ex":"בפסקה 2 כתוב שכל סיבוב של הדוושות סובב את הגלגל הקדמי רק פעם אחת, ולכן «the only way to go faster» היה להגדיל את הגלגל. הגלגל הגדול דווקא הגביר את הסכנה ליפול, ולא מנע אותה.","w":[["in order to","כדי ל... (+פועל)"],["attach","לחבר, להצמיד"]]},{"q":"In paragraph 4, the word \"embraced\" (in \"Women in particular embraced it\") is closest in meaning to","o":["strongly criticized","eagerly adopted","carefully repaired","hardly noticed"],"a":1,"ex":"«embrace» כאן = לאמץ בהתלהבות. ההמשך מסביר שהאופניים נתנו לנשים חופש תנועה ואפילו שינו את האופנה, כלומר הן אהבו אותם והשתמשו בהם. «strongly criticized» הפוך לגמרי למה שמתואר.","w":[["embrace","לאמץ (בהתלהבות); לחבק"],["in particular","במיוחד, בפרט"]]},{"q":"According to paragraph 3, the safety bicycle did not need a giant front wheel because","o":["its rubber tires made the whole bicycle lighter","its frame was built from a lighter metal","it was designed mainly for short city trips","its gears made the wheel turn faster than the pedals"],"a":3,"ex":"בפסקה 3 כתוב שהשרשרת חיברה גלגל שיניים גדול לקטן, ולכן סיבוב אחד של הדוושות סובב את הגלגל כמה פעמים, «so speed no longer depended on wheel size». כלומר הגלגל מסתובב מהר יותר מהדוושות, ואין צורך בגלגל ענק. הצמיגים מוזכרים כשיפור בנוחות, לא כסיבה לגודל הגלגל.","w":[["gear","גלגל שיניים"],["depend on","להיות תלוי ב..."],["no longer","כבר לא"]]},{"q":"The main purpose of the last paragraph is to","o":["describe the effects of the safety bicycle on society","explain how bicycles were mass-produced in factories","show that cycling remained dangerous for women","compare the prices of different early bicycles"],"a":0,"ex":"הפסקה נפתחת ב-«did more than make cycling less dangerous» ומתארת מה האופניים שינו בחברה: פועלים יכלו להרשות לעצמם תחבורה, ונשים קיבלו חופש תנועה. ייצור המוני מוזכר רק כסיבה לירידת המחירים, לא כנושא הפסקה.","w":[["mass production","ייצור המוני"],["afford","להרשות לעצמו (כספית)"]]}]},"p1rc2":{"id":"p1rc2","tier":1,"type":"rc","title":"Living on Almost Nothing","text":["In many deserts, rain falls only a few times a year, and the hot sun can dry the ground within hours. Even so, these regions are far from empty. Thousands of plant species have adapted to such harsh conditions, and they have done so in surprisingly different ways. Broadly speaking, desert plants follow one of three strategies: they store water, they reduce the amount of water they lose, or they avoid the dry season altogether.","The best-known water storers are cacti. Their thick stems contain spongy tissue that swells after a rainstorm and slowly shrinks as the stored water is used. Many cacti also have shallow roots that spread widely just beneath the surface, allowing them to collect rainwater quickly before it evaporates. Their spines, which are actually modified leaves, protect this precious supply from thirsty animals and also shade the stem from the sun.","Other plants concentrate on saving water. Ordinary leaves lose a great deal of moisture through tiny openings called stomata, which plants must open in order to take in carbon dioxide. Many desert species keep these openings closed during the heat of the day and open them only at night, when the air is cooler and more humid. They store the carbon dioxide they absorb in the dark and use it for photosynthesis once the sun rises. Some shrubs go even further, dropping their leaves completely during long dry periods and growing new ones after it rains.","The third group does not attempt to survive the drought at all. Certain desert flowers spend most of their lives as seeds buried in the soil, sometimes for several years. When enough rain finally falls, they sprout, bloom and produce new seeds within a few weeks, before the ground dries out again. To a visitor, a desert suddenly covered in flowers may seem like a rare miracle; in fact, it is the result of a carefully timed survival plan."],"qs":[{"q":"The passage mainly discusses","o":["why deserts receive so little rain","how desert animals find water to drink during the long dry season","the life cycle of the cactus","different ways in which plants survive in dry places"],"a":3,"ex":"בפסקה 1 הקטע מציג שלוש אסטרטגיות (לאגור מים, לחסוך במים, להימנע מעונת היובש), וכל אחת מהפסקאות הבאות מסבירה אחת מהן. הקקטוס הוא רק הדוגמה של פסקה 2, ולכן «the life cycle of the cactus» צר מדי.","w":[["survive","לשרוד"],["adapt","להסתגל"]]},{"q":"According to paragraph 2, the shallow roots of many cacti help them to","o":["reach water deep under the ground","collect rainwater before it disappears","protect the stem from thirsty animals","shade the plant from the sun"],"a":1,"ex":"בפסקה 2 כתוב שהשורשים הרדודים מתפרשים ממש מתחת לפני הקרקע ואוספים את מי הגשם מהר, «before it evaporates». הגנה מבעלי חיים וצל הם התפקיד של הקוצים, לא של השורשים.","w":[["shallow","רדוד"],["evaporate","להתאדות"],["beneath","מתחת ל..."]]},{"q":"In paragraph 3, the word \"They\" (in \"They store the carbon dioxide they absorb in the dark\") refers to","o":["ordinary leaves","the tiny openings","many desert species","long dry periods"],"a":2,"ex":"המשפט הקודם מדבר על «Many desert species» שסוגרות את הפתחים ביום ופותחות אותם בלילה, והן אלה שאוגרות את הפחמן הדו-חמצני ומשתמשות בו בבוקר. הפתחים (stomata) רק מכניסים את הגז, הם לא אוגרים אותו.","w":[["absorb","לספוג, לקלוט"],["store","לאגור, לאחסן"]]},{"q":"It can be inferred from paragraph 3 that many desert plants open their stomata at night because","o":["less water is lost when the air is cool and humid","carbon dioxide can only be found in the air at night","photosynthesis can take place only in the dark","strong sunlight damages the openings"],"a":0,"ex":"לפי פסקה 3, דרך הפתחים יוצאת הרבה לחות, והצמחים פותחים אותם רק בלילה, «when the air is cooler and more humid». מכאן שבלילה הם מאבדים פחות מים. «only in the dark» לא נכון, כי כתוב שהפוטוסינתזה מתבצעת «once the sun rises».","w":[["humid","לח"],["moisture","לחות"]]},{"q":"Why does the author describe a desert covered in flowers as \"the result of a carefully timed survival plan\"?","o":["to suggest that tourists should visit deserts only after it rains","to explain why desert flowers live for many years as adult plants","to show that the sudden bloom is an adaptation rather than a lucky accident","to argue that desert flowers are less common than cacti"],"a":2,"ex":"המחבר מנגיד בין מה שנראה למבקר («a rare miracle») לבין מה שקורה באמת («in fact»): הזרעים מחכים לגשם ומספיקים לפרוח לפני שהאדמה מתייבשת, כלומר זו הסתגלות. הצמחים האלה חיים שנים כזרעים, לא כצמחים בוגרים.","w":[["in fact","למעשה, בעצם"],["rather than","במקום, ולא"],["sprout","לנבוט"]]}]},"p1rc3":{"id":"p1rc3","tier":1,"type":"rc","title":"Larks, Owls and the Body Clock","text":["Some people wake up full of energy before sunrise, while others struggle to think clearly until late morning and feel most alert after dark. Scientists call these differences chronotypes. Most people fall somewhere in the middle, but a significant minority are clearly \"larks\" (early birds) or \"owls\" (night owls). For a long time, such preferences were treated as a matter of discipline; owls, in particular, were often seen as lazy. Research now suggests that the picture is far more complicated.","Every person has an internal clock, located in a small region of the brain, that runs on a cycle of roughly 24 hours. This clock controls when we feel sleepy, when body temperature rises and when certain hormones are released. Morning light resets it each day, keeping it in step with the world around us. However, the clock does not run at exactly the same speed in everyone. In people whose cycle is slightly longer than 24 hours, the clock tends to drift later, which pushes them toward an owl pattern.","Genes play an important part in these differences. Large studies have identified dozens of genetic variants that are linked to being a morning or an evening person. Age matters as well. Teenagers typically shift toward later sleep times, a change that reaches its peak at around the age of twenty and then gradually reverses. Many older adults, in contrast, find themselves waking up earlier than they would like.","These findings have practical implications. Because most schools and workplaces start early, owls are often forced to function at a time when their bodies are not ready, a mismatch sometimes described as \"social jet lag.\" Some researchers argue that later school start times could improve teenagers' learning and mood, and several school districts that tried this approach reported encouraging results. Understanding chronotypes, therefore, may help societies design schedules that suit more people."],"qs":[{"q":"Which of the following is the best title for the passage?","o":["How to Become a Morning Person","Why People Differ in Their Daily Rhythms","The Dangers of Jet Lag for Travelers","Why Teenagers Need Less Sleep"],"a":1,"ex":"הקטע מסביר למה יש «ציפורי בוקר» ו«ינשופי לילה»: השעון הפנימי, גנים וגיל, ומה המשמעות לבתי ספר ולעבודה. «jet lag» מופיע רק כשם לחוסר ההתאמה בפסקה האחרונה, לא כנושא של טיסות.","w":[["differ","להיות שונה"],["alert","ערני"]]},{"q":"According to paragraph 2, a person is more likely to be a night owl if","o":["he or she is exposed to a lot of morning light","his or her body temperature stays the same all day","his or her internal clock is located in a different part of the brain","his or her internal cycle is a little longer than 24 hours"],"a":3,"ex":"בפסקה 2 כתוב שאצל מי שהמחזור שלו «slightly longer than 24 hours» השעון נוטה לזוז מאוחר יותר, וזה דוחף אותו לדפוס של ינשוף. אור בוקר דווקא מכוון את השעון כל יום, ולא הופך אדם לינשוף.","w":[["slightly","מעט, במידה קטנה"],["tend to","נוטה ל..."],["drift","להיסחף, לזוז לאט"]]},{"q":"In paragraph 2, the word \"it\" (in \"Morning light resets it each day\") refers to","o":["the internal clock","a small region of the brain","body temperature","the world around us"],"a":0,"ex":"המשפט הקודם מתאר את השעון הפנימי ומה הוא שולט בו, ואור הבוקר «resets it», כלומר מכוון מחדש את השעון כדי שיתאים לעולם. «a small region of the brain» מפתה, אבל זה רק המקום שבו השעון נמצא, ואזור במוח לא «מכוונים מחדש».","w":[["reset","לאפס, לכוון מחדש"],["in step with","מתואם עם, בקצב אחד עם"]]},{"q":"It can be inferred from paragraph 3 that, compared with a typical sixty-year-old, a typical twenty-year-old","o":["has fewer genetic variants linked to sleep","wakes up earlier in the morning","tends to prefer later sleep times","is less affected by morning light"],"a":2,"ex":"לפי פסקה 3, המעבר לשעות שינה מאוחרות מגיע לשיא בערך בגיל עשרים, ואילו מבוגרים רבים מתעוררים מוקדם. לכן בן עשרים נוטה לשעות מאוחרות יותר. «wakes up earlier» מתאר דווקא את המבוגרים.","w":[["in contrast","לעומת זאת"],["peak","שיא"],["gradually","בהדרגה"]]},{"q":"The main purpose of the last paragraph is to","o":["prove that later school start times always improve grades","explain why research on chronotypes matters for how schedules are planned","describe the effects of long flights on sleep","argue that owls work less hard than larks"],"a":1,"ex":"הפסקה פותחת ב-«practical implications» ומסבירה שלוח זמנים מוקדם פוגע בינשופים, ולכן הבנת הכרונוטיפים יכולה לעזור לתכנן שעות שמתאימות ליותר אנשים («therefore»). «always improve grades» קיצוני מדי: כתוב רק «encouraging results».","w":[["therefore","לכן"],["implication","השלכה, משמעות"],["mismatch","חוסר התאמה"]]}]},"p2rc1":{"id":"p2rc1","tier":2,"type":"rc","title":"The Last Keepers: What Automation Changed at the Lighthouse","text":["For centuries, a lighthouse depended on the people who lived inside it. Keepers climbed the tower each evening to light the lamp, trimmed wicks and polished lenses so that the beam would remain visible far out at sea, and kept watch through storms that might last for days. The work was lonely and demanding, and the families who shared it often lived on rocky islands that could be cut off from the mainland for weeks. Yet for generations few people imagined that the light could be kept burning in any other way.","That assumption began to change in the twentieth century. Electric lamps that switched on automatically at dusk, together with backup generators and, later, sensors that reported faults by radio, made a permanent human presence increasingly unnecessary. Maritime authorities, which had long struggled with the expense of staffing remote stations, seized the opportunity. One by one, lighthouses were converted, and by the end of the century the profession of keeper had virtually disappeared in most countries.","The gains were considerable. Automated lights proved at least as reliable as their predecessors, and the money saved could be spent on other aids to navigation. Moreover, satellite positioning soon allowed ships to determine their location with an accuracy that no beam of light could match. Critics nevertheless argued that something had been lost. Keepers had done far more than tend a lamp: they recorded the weather, spotted vessels in distress and sometimes rowed out to rescue survivors. A machine could keep the light burning, but it could not notice that a fishing boat had failed to return.","Today, many towers stand empty, and their future is uncertain. Since they are no longer essential to navigation, governments are often reluctant to pay for their upkeep, and some have been sold to private owners or local trusts. Several have been turned into museums or guesthouses, where visitors can glimpse the isolated life that keepers once led. Such projects preserve the buildings, but they also raise a question: whether a lighthouse that guides no one is still a lighthouse, or merely a monument to one."],"qs":[{"q":"Which of the following is the best title for the passage?","o":["The Lonely Life of Island Families","How Satellite Navigation Replaced the Lighthouse","Lighthouses Without Keepers: Gains and Losses","Why Automated Lights Proved Unreliable at Sea"],"a":2,"ex":"הקטע מתאר את המעבר למגדלורים אוטומטיים (פסקה 2), את הרווחים ואת מה שאבד (פסקה 3) ואת מה שקרה למגדלים אחר כך (פסקה 4). חיי המשפחות הם רק פסקה 1, ולפי הקטע האורות האוטומטיים דווקא אמינים לפחות כמו הקודמים.","w":[["keeper","שומר (מגדלור)"],["automated","אוטומטי"]]},{"q":"According to the second paragraph, maritime authorities were quick to adopt automation because","o":["staffing distant lighthouses had long been expensive","keepers had begun to refuse work on remote islands","electric lamps gave a brighter beam than older ones","satellite positioning had made lighthouses less important"],"a":0,"ex":"בפסקה 2 כתוב שהרשויות «had long struggled with the expense of staffing remote stations», כלומר החזקת אנשים בתחנות מרוחקות עלתה הרבה כסף, ולכן הן ניצלו את ההזדמנות. הלוויינים מוזכרים רק בפסקה 3, ואין בקטע טענה שהשומרים סירבו לעבוד.","w":[["expense","הוצאה, עלות"],["seize","לתפוס, לנצל (הזדמנות)"],["remote","מרוחק"]]},{"q":"In the third paragraph, the word 'tend' could best be replaced by","o":["switch off","design","replace","look after"],"a":3,"ex":"«tend a lamp» = לטפל במנורה ולדאוג לה. המשפט אומר שהשומרים עשו הרבה יותר מטיפול במנורה. «replace» (להחליף) מפתה, אבל הקטע מתאר תחזוקה יומיומית ולא החלפה של המנורה.","w":[["tend","לטפל ב..., לדאוג ל..."],["look after","לטפל, להשגיח"]]},{"q":"The third paragraph mainly serves to","o":["prove that automated lights were less reliable than keepers","weigh the benefits of automation against the keepers' other duties","explain how ships use satellites to determine their position","show that keepers themselves opposed the automation of lighthouses"],"a":1,"ex":"הפסקה פותחת ברווחים (אמינות, חיסכון, לוויינים) ואז עוברת ב-«nevertheless» למה שאבד: השומרים גם תיעדו מזג אוויר והצילו ניצולים, ומכונה לא יכולה לעשות את זה. את הביקורת השמיעו «critics», לא השומרים עצמם, והאורות האוטומטיים אמינים לפחות כמו הקודמים.","w":[["nevertheless","למרות זאת, אף על פי כן"],["predecessor","קודם (מי שהיה לפני)"],["in distress","במצוקה"]]},{"q":"It can be inferred from the last paragraph that converting lighthouses into museums or guesthouses","o":["has made them essential to navigation once again","is opposed by most of the local trusts that own them","preserves the towers but not the role they were built for","costs governments more than employing keepers once did"],"a":2,"ex":"כתוב שהפרויקטים האלה «preserve the buildings», אבל מעלים שאלה אם מגדלור «that guides no one» הוא עדיין מגדלור. כלומר המבנה נשמר, אבל הוא כבר לא מנחה ספינות. הקטע אומר שהמגדלים כבר לא חיוניים לניווט, ולא שהם חזרו להיות חיוניים.","w":[["preserve","לשמר"],["reluctant","מסרב, לא ששׂ"],["merely","רק, לא יותר מ..."]]}]},"p2rc2":{"id":"p2rc2","tier":2,"type":"rc","title":"Singing Over the Traffic","text":["For a songbird, a song is far more than decoration. Males use it to defend a territory and to attract a mate, and females often judge a potential partner by the quality of his performance. A song works, however, only if it is heard. In cities, where traffic, construction and air conditioners produce a constant low-frequency roar, that simple requirement has become surprisingly difficult to meet, and researchers have spent the past two decades examining how birds respond.","The most widely documented change concerns pitch. In a number of species, including great tits and blackbirds, urban populations sing at higher frequencies than their relatives in nearby forests. Because most city noise is concentrated at low frequencies, higher notes are less likely to be masked by it. Some birds also sing louder, a tendency known as the Lombard effect, which humans display as well when they raise their voices in a crowded room. Others shift their timing, beginning their dawn chorus earlier, before the morning traffic builds up, or even singing at night.","Whether these adjustments are learned or inherited remains a matter of debate. Young songbirds acquire their songs by listening to adults, so a preference for higher notes could spread through a population without any genetic change. On the other hand, birds whose voices happen to carry better may raise more chicks, and over many generations such an advantage could alter the population itself. Evidence for both processes has been found, and they are not mutually exclusive.","The adjustments are not without cost. Higher notes may not travel as far as lower ones, and in some species females appear to prefer deeper songs, which are often produced by larger, healthier males. A bird that sings high in order to be heard may thus be heard as a less attractive partner. Moreover, singing louder or longer demands energy that could otherwise be spent searching for food. For these reasons, some ecologists warn that the birds' remarkable flexibility should not be taken as proof that noise is harmless, and that quieter roads and vehicles may still be needed."],"qs":[{"q":"The main purpose of the passage is to","o":["argue that birds living in cities are healthier than those in forests","describe how city noise is changing birdsong, and at what cost","explain how young songbirds learn their songs from adult birds","show that only humans and birds raise their voices in noisy places"],"a":1,"ex":"הקטע מתאר איך ציפורים בעיר משנות את השירה בגלל הרעש (פסקה 2), מתלבט מאיפה השינוי מגיע (פסקה 3) ומסביר מה הוא עולה להן (פסקה 4). הלמידה מהמבוגרים היא רק פרט מפסקה 3, והקטע לא משווה את הבריאות של ציפורי עיר וציפורי יער.","w":[["alter","לשנות"],["urban","עירוני"]]},{"q":"According to the second paragraph, singing at a higher pitch helps city birds because","o":["high notes travel further through city streets than low ones","females in cities prefer high-pitched songs","traffic noise is quieter early in the morning","low-frequency city noise is less likely to cover their songs"],"a":3,"ex":"בפסקה 2 כתוב שרוב הרעש בעיר נמצא בתדרים נמוכים, ולכן צלילים גבוהים «less likely to be masked», כלומר פחות מוסתרים על ידו. התשובה הראשונה הפוכה: לפי פסקה 4, צלילים גבוהים אולי דווקא לא מגיעים רחוק כמו נמוכים. הבוקר המוקדם קשור לתזמון, לא לגובה הצליל.","w":[["pitch","גובה צליל"],["mask","להסתיר, לכסות"],["frequency","תדר; תדירות"]]},{"q":"In the third paragraph, 'they' in 'they are not mutually exclusive' refers to","o":["learning from adults and change through inheritance","young songbirds and the adults they learn from","birds whose voices carry better in the city","the higher notes preferred by city populations"],"a":0,"ex":"«they» מתייחס ל-«both processes» שבאותו משפט: למידה מהמבוגרים ושינוי תורשתי לאורך דורות. «not mutually exclusive» = אחד לא מבטל את השני, שניהם יכולים לקרות יחד. הציפורים עם הקול שנשמע טוב הן רק חלק מהסבר אחד.","w":[["mutually exclusive","סותרים זה את זה, לא יכולים להתקיים יחד"],["inherit","לרשת (בתורשה)"],["on the other hand","מצד שני"]]},{"q":"It can be inferred from the fourth paragraph that a city bird that sings at a higher pitch","o":["is probably smaller and weaker than birds that sing at a lower pitch","spends less energy than a bird that sings louder","may be heard more easily but find it harder to attract a mate","learned its song from birds living in nearby forests"],"a":2,"ex":"כתוב שציפור ששרה גבוה כדי שישמעו אותה «may thus be heard as a less attractive partner», כי אצל חלק מהמינים הנקבות מעדיפות שירה עמוקה. התשובה הראשונה מלכודת: הקטע אומר שהשירה העמוקה באה לרוב מזכרים גדולים, אבל לא שמי ששר גבוה בעיר הוא באמת קטן או חלש, אלא רק שהוא נשמע פחות מושך.","w":[["thus","לפיכך, כך"],["attractive","מושך"],["infer","להסיק"]]},{"q":"The last sentence of the passage suggests that some ecologists","o":["believe that reducing noise may still be necessary","believe that urban birds will soon stop singing altogether","fear that quieter road surfaces would harm city wildlife","regard the birds' flexibility as proof that city noise does no harm"],"a":0,"ex":"האקולוגים מזהירים שאסור לראות בגמישות של הציפורים הוכחה שהרעש לא מזיק, ושייתכן שעדיין צריך כבישים ורכבים שקטים יותר. כלומר ייתכן שעדיין צריך להפחית את הרעש. התשובה האחרונה היא בדיוק ההפך ממה שהם אומרים.","w":[["flexibility","גמישות"],["remarkable","יוצא דופן, מרשים"],["adapt","להסתגל"]]}]},"p2rc3":{"id":"p2rc3","tier":2,"type":"rc","title":"Reading a Restless Mountain","text":["Hundreds of millions of people live within reach of a potentially active volcano, and for them the question of when it will next erupt is far from academic. Unlike earthquakes, which strike with almost no warning, eruptions are usually preceded by signs of unrest, sometimes for weeks or months. The challenge for volcanologists is therefore not detecting these signals, which modern instruments do remarkably well, but interpreting them.","Scientists rely on several kinds of evidence. Networks of seismometers record the small earthquakes produced as magma forces its way through rock beneath the surface. Satellites and GPS stations measure ground deformation: a volcano may swell by a few centimeters as magma accumulates in a chamber below it. Instruments that sample the gases escaping from vents provide a further clue, since a rise in sulfur dioxide, for example, can indicate that fresh magma is approaching the surface. Each method has its limitations, but taken together they allow observers to build a picture of what is happening underground.","Even so, that picture is often ambiguous. Magma that rises toward the surface may simply stall and cool, so a volcano can show every sign of unrest and then fall quiet again. Conversely, some eruptions have begun after only brief or faint warnings. Moreover, each volcano behaves differently, and many have not erupted since instruments were installed near them, so researchers have no record of how they behaved before their last eruption. A pattern that preceded an eruption at one mountain may therefore mean little at another.","For these reasons, volcanologists rarely issue precise predictions. Instead, they speak in terms of probabilities and alert levels, which help authorities decide when to restrict access or order evacuations. Such decisions are difficult: an evacuation that turns out to be unnecessary costs money and may make residents less willing to leave the next time, whereas a delayed one can cost lives. Improved computer models and longer records may narrow the uncertainty, but few experts expect it to disappear entirely."],"qs":[{"q":"The main idea of the passage is that","o":["modern instruments now allow scientists to predict eruptions precisely","people who live near volcanoes are usually unwilling to evacuate","eruptions, unlike earthquakes, almost never give any warning","volcanoes give warning signs, but these are hard to interpret reliably"],"a":3,"ex":"כבר בפסקה 1 כתוב שהקושי הוא לא לגלות את הסימנים אלא לפרש אותם, ושאר הקטע מסביר למה. התשובה השלישית הפוכה: דווקא רעידות אדמה מגיעות כמעט בלי אזהרה, והתפרצויות בדרך כלל כן מקדימות סימנים. גם התשובה הראשונה הפוכה: המדענים כמעט לא נותנים תחזיות מדויקות.","w":[["interpret","לפרש"],["unlike","בניגוד ל..."],["precede","להקדים, לבוא לפני"]]},{"q":"According to the second paragraph, the ground around a volcano may rise slightly when","o":["gases escape from vents near its summit","magma builds up in a chamber beneath it","small earthquakes break the rock below it","the surface cools after a period of unrest"],"a":1,"ex":"בפסקה 2: הר געש עשוי «swell» (להתנפח) בכמה סנטימטרים «as magma accumulates in a chamber below it», כלומר כשמאגמה מצטברת מתחתיו. הגזים ורעידות האדמה הקטנות הם סימנים אחרים שמוזכרים באותה פסקה, אבל לא הם הסיבה להתנפחות.","w":[["accumulate","להצטבר"],["deformation","עיוות, שינוי צורה"],["swell","להתנפח"]]},{"q":"In the third paragraph, the word 'stall' could best be replaced by","o":["speed up","stop moving","break out","grow hotter"],"a":1,"ex":"מאגמה שעולה עלולה «stall and cool», כלומר להיעצר ולהתקרר, ולכן ההר נרגע בלי להתפרץ. «break out» (לפרוץ) הוא כמעט ההפך: אם המאגמה הייתה פורצת, הייתה התפרצות.","w":[["stall","להיתקע, להיעצר"],["ambiguous","דו-משמעי, לא ברור"]]},{"q":"The third paragraph mainly serves to","o":["explain why signs of unrest are an unreliable guide to eruptions","describe the instruments used to detect rising magma","argue that most eruptions begin without any warning signs at all","show that all volcanoes behave alike before they erupt"],"a":0,"ex":"הפסקה נותנת שלוש סיבות לכך שהתמונה לא חד-משמעית: מאגמה יכולה להיעצר, יש התפרצויות עם אזהרה חלשה, ולכל הר געש התנהגות משלו. היא אומרת «some eruptions», לא רוב ההתפרצויות, ואומרת שכל הר מתנהג אחרת, לא שכולם דומים.","w":[["conversely","ובאופן הפוך, מנגד"],["even so","למרות זאת, ובכל זאת"],["unrest","אי-שקט, פעילות"]]},{"q":"It can be inferred from the last paragraph that an evacuation which proves unnecessary","o":["shows that the alert level had been set correctly","is usually the result of faulty instruments","is seldom ordered by the authorities","may make a later evacuation harder to carry out"],"a":3,"ex":"כתוב שפינוי מיותר עלול לגרום לתושבים «less willing to leave the next time», כלומר בפעם הבאה יהיה קשה יותר לפנות אותם. הקטע לא תולה פינויים מיותרים במכשירים תקולים, אלא בכך שהסימנים עצמם לא ברורים.","w":[["evacuation","פינוי"],["whereas","בעוד ש..., ואילו"],["willing","מוכן, מסכים"]]}]},"p3rc1":{"id":"p3rc1","tier":3,"type":"rc","title":"Results That Would Not Return","text":["For decades, a finding published in a respected psychology journal was treated as close to settled knowledge. That confidence was badly shaken in 2015, when a large collaboration of researchers attempted to repeat one hundred studies drawn from three leading journals. Although nearly all of the original studies had reported statistically significant results, fewer than half of the repetitions produced comparable outcomes. The ensuing debate, soon labelled the 'replication crisis', has since spread to fields as distant as cancer biology and economics.","Few observers attribute the problem chiefly to fraud. Far more corrosive, they argue, were ordinary practices that once seemed harmless. A researcher who measures many outcomes, tries several statistical analyses, or stops collecting data as soon as the results look favorable can, without any intent to deceive, arrive at a pattern that is merely a product of chance. Because journals traditionally preferred striking, positive results to reports that an effect had not been found, such flukes were disproportionately likely to be published, while contradictory studies remained unseen in researchers' files.","Small samples compounded the difficulty. A study involving a few dozen participants can reliably detect only very large effects; when it nonetheless reports a significant result, the size of the effect it estimates is likely to be inflated. Larger follow-up studies then find something considerably weaker, or nothing at all. Several widely publicized claims, among them the idea that briefly adopting a confident posture alters one's hormone levels, have faded in precisely this way.","The response has been notably constructive. Many journals now invite researchers to register their hypotheses and methods in advance, making it far harder to adjust an analysis once the results are known. Some have gone further, agreeing to publish a study on the strength of its design, whatever it eventually finds. Sharing raw data, which lets others check the calculations, has also become common.","Not everyone accepts the gloomiest reading of the replication figures. Critics point out that a failed repetition may reflect differences in the population studied or in how a procedure was carried out, rather than a flaw in the original work. Even so, few would now dispute the lesson of the episode: a single study, however elegant, is a weak foundation for confident conclusions, and a field's credibility rests less on the novelty of its findings than on its willingness to test them again."],"qs":[{"q":"The passage is mainly concerned with","o":["the argument that most published psychology research is the product of deliberate fraud","a defense of well-known studies against researchers who failed to repeat them","why many psychology findings could not be reproduced and how the field has responded","the way in which the 2015 collaboration selected the studies it attempted to repeat"],"a":2,"ex":"הקטע מסביר למה ממצאים רבים לא שוחזרו (פסקאות 1-3) ומה התחום עשה בתגובה (פסקה 4). ההונאה נדחית כבר בתחילת פסקה 2, והביקורת על נתוני השחזור מופיעה רק בפסקה האחרונה ולא כהגנה על מחקרים.","w":[["reproduce","לשחזר, לחזור על"],["be concerned with","לעסוק ב..."]]},{"q":"According to the second paragraph, which of the following contributed to the problem?","o":["Journals favored positive results over reports of no effect.","Researchers often continued collecting data long after their results had become clear.","Many researchers deliberately altered their data in order to obtain significant results.","Journals refused to publish studies that measured more than one outcome."],"a":0,"ex":"בפסקה 2 כתוב שכתבי העת העדיפו תוצאות חיוביות ומרשימות על דיווחים שלא נמצא אפקט, ולכן תוצאות מקריות פורסמו יותר. האפשרות השנייה הופכת את מה שנאמר: הבעיה היא חוקר שמפסיק לאסוף נתונים מוקדם, ברגע שהתוצאות נראות טוב. הונאה מכוונת נדחית במפורש («without any intent to deceive»).","w":[["attribute to","לייחס ל..."],["fluke","מקרה, צירוף מקרים"],["disproportionately","באופן לא פרופורציונלי"]]},{"q":"In the second paragraph, the word 'corrosive' could best be replaced by","o":["widespread","damaging","deliberate","obvious"],"a":1,"ex":"«Corrosive» = משחית, מכרסם, גורם נזק הדרגתי. הכותב אומר שההרגלים הרגילים הזיקו הרבה יותר מהונאה, ולכן «damaging». «widespread» (נפוץ) מפתה כי ההרגלים היו נפוצים, אבל המילה מתארת את הנזק ולא את התפוצה.","w":[["corrosive","משחית, מכרסם"],["chiefly","בעיקר"]]},{"q":"The example of the confident posture in the third paragraph is mentioned in order to","o":["show that hormone levels are too unstable to be measured reliably","prove that body posture has a lasting effect on a person's confidence","suggest that the original researchers deliberately exaggerated their findings","illustrate how a small study's result can fade when larger studies follow"],"a":3,"ex":"הפסקה מסבירה שמחקר עם מעט משתתפים מנפח את גודל האפקט, ושמחקרים גדולים יותר מוצאים אחר כך אפקט חלש יותר או כלום. התנוחה הבטוחה היא דוגמה לטענה שנעלמה «in precisely this way». הקטע לא טוען שהחוקרים הגזימו בכוונה.","w":[["compound","להחריף, להוסיף על"],["inflate","לנפח, להגזים"],["nonetheless","בכל זאת, למרות זאת"]]},{"q":"It can be inferred from the last paragraph that the author","o":["agrees with the critics that the replication figures are of little real importance","sees the retesting of findings as more vital to a field than their novelty","believes that a failed repetition always reveals a flaw in the original study","thinks that a single, carefully designed study is enough to settle a question"],"a":1,"ex":"הכותב מציג את המבקרים, ואז אומר «Even so»: האמינות של תחום תלויה פחות בחידוש של הממצאים ויותר בנכונות לבדוק אותם שוב. האפשרות השלישית סותרת את דברי המבקרים שהכותב מביא, והרביעית סותרת את המשפט שמחקר יחיד הוא בסיס חלש.","w":[["even so","למרות זאת, ובכל זאת"],["credibility","אמינות"],["novelty","חידוש, חדשנות"]]}]},"p3rc2":{"id":"p3rc2","tier":3,"type":"rc","title":"Signs on Clay and Bone","text":["Writing is so central to modern life that it is easy to forget how recent an invention it is. Humans had been speaking for tens of thousands of years before anyone devised a way to record language; true writing appeared only about five thousand years ago. Where, how and how many times this happened are still disputed.","The oldest well-documented case comes from southern Mesopotamia, in what is now Iraq. There, according to one influential theory, writing grew out of bookkeeping. For millennia, officials had used small clay tokens of different shapes to stand for quantities of goods such as grain or sheep. Eventually, tokens were sealed inside hollow clay balls, whose surfaces were pressed with marks showing what lay within. Once it became clear that the marks alone conveyed the same information, the tokens grew redundant, and flat tablets bearing signs took their place. Only gradually were the signs adapted to represent sounds, and thus names and words, rather than merely objects and numbers.","For much of the twentieth century, many scholars assumed that this Mesopotamian invention was unique and that every other writing system descended from it, directly or through travelers who carried the idea. Egyptian hieroglyphs, which appeared at almost the same time, were often explained in this way. The assumption reflected a conviction that so complex an achievement could hardly have occurred twice.","That conviction has since weakened considerably. Early Egyptian inscriptions differ markedly from Mesopotamian ones in their signs and in how they represent language, and some appear nearly as old. More decisive are cases far removed in space and time. Chinese characters, first attested on bones used for divination around 1200 BCE, show no convincing link to any western script, while Mesoamerican writing arose among peoples entirely cut off from Asia and Africa. Most specialists therefore now accept that writing was invented independently at least three times, and perhaps four.","The debate is not merely about dates. If writing emerged on several occasions, the invention looks less like a stroke of individual genius than a predictable response to particular conditions: dense populations, centralized authority and the need to keep track of goods and obligations. Yet the parallel is not perfect. The earliest surviving Chinese texts served religious ritual rather than accounting, a reminder that similar inventions may answer quite different needs."],"qs":[{"q":"Which of the following is the best title for the passage?","o":["Clay Tokens and the Growth of Mesopotamian Trade","One Invention or Several? How Writing Began","How Writing Traveled from Mesopotamia to China","Why Ancient Writing Served Mainly Religious Purposes"],"a":1,"ex":"הקטע כולו עוסק בשאלה אם הכתב הומצא פעם אחת או כמה פעמים: ההנחה הישנה (פסקה 3), הראיות נגדה (פסקה 4) והמשמעות (פסקה 5). האסימונים הם רק פסקה אחת, והקטע אומר שהכתב הסיני לא קשור לכתב מערבי, כך שהכותרת השלישית הפוכה לטענה.","w":[["origin","מקור, מוצא"],["scholar","חוקר, מלומד"]]},{"q":"According to the second paragraph, the clay tokens were no longer needed once","o":["officials began using signs to represent the sounds of people's names and words","farmers stopped trading goods such as grain and sheep","the hollow clay balls proved too fragile to store the tokens safely","the marks on the clay balls were seen to carry the same information"],"a":3,"ex":"בפסקה 2: כשהתברר שהסימנים על כדורי החמר מוסרים את אותו מידע, האסימונים נעשו מיותרים. הסימנים שמייצגים צלילים ושמות הגיעו רק אחר כך («Only gradually»), ולכן האפשרות הראשונה מפתה אבל שגויה בסדר הזמנים.","w":[["redundant","מיותר"],["convey","להעביר, למסור"],["once","ברגע ש..., לאחר ש..."]]},{"q":"In the third paragraph, the word 'it' (in 'descended from it') refers to","o":["the Mesopotamian invention","the twentieth century","every other writing system","Egyptian hieroglyphs"],"a":0,"ex":"החוקרים הניחו שההמצאה המסופוטמית הייתה יחידה ושכל מערכת כתב אחרת התפתחה ממנה. «every other writing system» הוא מי שהתפתח, לא המקור שממנו התפתחו, ולכן הוא לא יכול להיות «it».","w":[["descend from","להתפתח מ..., לצאת מ..."],["refer to","להתייחס ל..."]]},{"q":"The main purpose of the fourth paragraph is to","o":["show that Egyptian writing is in fact older than Mesopotamian writing","explain how the idea of writing reached Mesoamerica from Asia","present evidence that writing was invented more than once","describe the methods used to date inscriptions on bone and clay"],"a":2,"ex":"הפסקה פותחת ב«That conviction has since weakened» ומביאה ראיות: הכתב המצרי שונה, הכתב הסיני לא קשור למערב, ובמסואמריקה לא היה מגע עם אסיה. המסקנה: הכתב הומצא לפחות שלוש פעמים. על מצרים נאמר רק «nearly as old», לא שהוא עתיק יותר.","w":[["markedly","באופן ניכר"],["attest","להעיד על, לתעד"],["therefore","לכן"]]},{"q":"It can be inferred from the last paragraph that the author","o":["believes that writing was most likely the work of a single gifted individual","considers the debate over the origins of writing to be mainly a question of dates","is convinced that writing always developed in order to meet economic needs","thinks that writing did not serve the same needs in every case"],"a":3,"ex":"הכותב מציע שהכתב הוא תגובה לתנאים דומים, ואז מסייג ב«Yet the parallel is not perfect»: הכתב הסיני הראשון ששרד שימש לטקסים דתיים ולא לחשבונות. כלומר הצרכים לא היו זהים בכל מקום. האפשרות השלישית סותרת את הדוגמה הסינית.","w":[["yet","ובכל זאת, אך"],["rather than","במקום, ולא"],["parallel","הקבלה, דמיון"]]}]},"p3rc3":{"id":"p3rc3","tier":3,"type":"rc","title":"Life Without Sunlight","text":["In 1977, scientists in a small submarine descended more than two kilometers to the floor of the eastern Pacific and found something no one had predicted. Around cracks where seawater heated by the rock beneath gushed back into the ocean thrived dense communities of clams, crabs and tube worms longer than a human arm. In a place that sunlight never reaches, life was not merely surviving but flourishing.","Rather than capturing the energy of sunlight, as plants and algae do, the vent communities are built on microbes that extract energy from chemicals dissolved in the hot fluid, notably hydrogen sulfide. Many of the larger animals harbor such microbes within their bodies and depend on them entirely for nourishment. Life, it turned out, could run on energy that did not come from the sun.","Some researchers soon asked whether vents might also be where life began. The idea gained momentum after the discovery in 2000 of a different kind of vent, far cooler and less acidic than the 'black smokers' found earlier. At such sites, warm alkaline fluid meets seawater inside a maze of thin mineral walls, creating differences in acidity across those walls. Since every living cell powers itself by maintaining a comparable difference across its membrane, supporters propose that this natural arrangement could have driven the first steps of metabolism before cells existed.","The hypothesis has met with serious objections. The most persistent concerns water itself. Molecules that carry genetic information, such as RNA, are long chains assembled from smaller units, and in water such chains tend to break apart more readily than they form. Critics also note that several laboratory reactions that produce life's building blocks require ultraviolet light, which never penetrates the deep sea. A rival camp therefore favors shallow pools on land, perhaps near hot springs, where repeated drying and wetting could concentrate simple molecules and help them link together, a picture recalling Darwin's passing speculation about 'some warm little pond'.","Neither side has produced decisive evidence, and perhaps none ever will, since the chemistry that preceded the first cells left no physical trace. Some researchers have accordingly suggested that the two scenarios need not be mutually exclusive, with different stages unfolding in different settings. Regardless of how the debate is resolved, the vents have already shown that life can thrive under a far wider range of conditions than biologists once imagined."],"qs":[{"q":"The passage mainly discusses","o":["what vents reveal about life, and whether life began at such sites","the methods scientists have used to explore the floor of the deep ocean since 1977","evidence that the theory of life beginning in shallow pools on land has been disproved","the ways in which microbes living near vents produce chemicals such as hydrogen sulfide"],"a":0,"ex":"הקטע מתאר מה גילו בארובות (פסקאות 1-2), ואז את הוויכוח אם החיים התחילו שם (פסקאות 3-5). הבריכות ביבשה הן חלופה שעדיין לא הוכרעה, לא תיאוריה שהופרכה, והחיידקים לא מייצרים מימן גופרתי אלא מפיקים ממנו אנרגיה.","w":[["vent","פתח פליטה, ארובה"],["reveal","לחשוף, לגלות"]]},{"q":"According to the second paragraph, many of the larger animals living near the vents","o":["capture energy directly from the chemicals in the hot fluid","depend on the small amount of sunlight that reaches the seabed","obtain their food from microbes that live inside their bodies","feed mainly on smaller creatures such as clams and crabs"],"a":2,"ex":"בפסקה 2 כתוב שבעלי חיים גדולים רבים מחזיקים חיידקים בתוך גופם ותלויים בהם לגמרי למזון. האפשרות הראשונה מפתה, אבל מי שמפיק אנרגיה מהכימיקלים הם החיידקים, לא בעלי החיים עצמם. אור שמש בכלל לא מגיע לשם.","w":[["harbor","לאכסן, להחזיק בתוכו"],["nourishment","הזנה, מזון"],["notably","במיוחד; באופן בולט"]]},{"q":"In the fourth paragraph, the word 'persistent' could best be replaced by","o":["forceful","unexpected","convincing","enduring"],"a":3,"ex":"«The most persistent» = ההתנגדות שחוזרת ונשארת הכי הרבה זמן, כלומר «enduring». «convincing» מפתה כי ההתנגדות רצינית, אבל «persistent» מתאר משך והתמדה, לא כמה היא משכנעת.","w":[["persistent","מתמשך, עיקש"],["objection","התנגדות"]]},{"q":"The main purpose of the fourth paragraph is to","o":["raise problems for the vent hypothesis and offer an alternative to it","explain how RNA was first produced by chemists in the laboratory","show that Darwin's view on the origin of life has finally been confirmed","describe how differences in acidity supply living cells with energy"],"a":0,"ex":"הפסקה מביאה שתי בעיות בהשערת הארובות (מים מפרקים שרשראות, אין אור אולטרה סגול) ואז את החלופה של בריכות ביבשה. דרווין מוזכר רק כדמיון («recalling»), ולא נאמר שההשערה שלו אושרה. ההבדלים בחומציות שייכים לפסקה 3.","w":[["hypothesis","השערה"],["therefore","לכן"],["penetrate","לחדור"]]},{"q":"It can be inferred from the last paragraph that the author believes that","o":["life certainly began in shallow pools and only later spread to the deep sea","fossils of the earliest cells will eventually settle the debate","the study of vents has been valuable even if life did not begin there","the two scenarios described in the passage cannot both be partly correct"],"a":2,"ex":"המשפט האחרון: «Regardless of how the debate is resolved», הארובות כבר הראו שהחיים יכולים לשגשג בתנאים רחבים בהרבה. כלומר המחקר שלהן חשוב בכל מקרה. הקטע אומר שהשלבים הראשונים לא השאירו עקבות, ושחוקרים מציעים ששני התרחישים יכולים להתקיים יחד.","w":[["regardless of","בלי קשר ל..., בלי להתחשב ב..."],["mutually exclusive","סותרים זה את זה, לא יכולים להתקיים יחד"],["accordingly","בהתאם לכך, לכן"]]}]},"p0sc1":{"id":"p0sc1","tier":0,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"After the long walk in the hot sun, the children were ___ and asked for something cold to drink.","o":["noisy","brave","thirsty","lazy"],"a":2,"ex":"«thirsty» = צמא. הילדים ביקשו משהו קר לשתות אחרי הליכה בשמש, ולכן הם צמאים. «lazy» (עצלן) אולי מתאים לעייפות, אבל לא מסביר למה ביקשו לשתות.","w":[["thirsty","צמא"]]},{"q":"Rina wanted to buy the blue jacket, ___ it was too expensive, so she chose a cheaper one.","o":["but","because","so","unless"],"a":0,"ex":"«but» = אבל. היא רצתה את המעיל, אבל הוא היה יקר מדי: זה ניגוד בין הרצון למה שקרה. «because» (כי) היה אומר שהיא רצתה אותו בגלל שהוא יקר, וזה לא מתאים לכך שבחרה מעיל זול יותר.","w":[["but","אבל"],["expensive","יקר"]]},{"q":"The fire spread quickly through the dry forest, and hundreds of families had to ___ their homes in the middle of the night.","o":["build","paint","clean","leave"],"a":3,"ex":"«leave» = לעזוב. בגלל השריפה המשפחות נאלצו לעזוב את הבתים באמצע הלילה. «build» (לבנות) או «clean» (לנקות) לא הגיוניים בזמן שריפה בלילה.","w":[["leave","לעזוב"],["spread","להתפשט"]]},{"q":"Please turn off your phones ___ the film, so that other people can enjoy it in silence.","o":["after","during","without","instead of"],"a":1,"ex":"«during» = במהלך. מכבים את הטלפון בזמן הסרט כדי שאחרים יוכלו ליהנות בשקט. «after» (אחרי) לא הגיוני: אחרי הסרט כבר אין צורך בשקט.","w":[["during","במהלך (+שם עצם)"],["silence","שקט"]]}]},"p0sc2":{"id":"p0sc2","tier":0,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"The small bakery on our street is always busy in the morning, because its bread is fresh and its prices are ___.","o":["strange","low","high","empty"],"a":1,"ex":"«low» = נמוך. המאפייה מלאה אנשים כי הלחם טרי והמחירים נמוכים: שתי סיבות טובות לקנות שם. «high» (גבוה) הוא ההפך, ומחירים גבוהים לא מסבירים למה תמיד יש בה קונים.","w":[["low","נמוך"],["busy","עמוס, עסוק"]]},{"q":"Lior could not ___ the name of the singer, although he knew every word of her most famous song.","o":["forget","hear","sing","remember"],"a":3,"ex":"«remember» = לזכור. הוא ידע את כל המילים של השיר, ובכל זאת לא זכר את שם הזמרת: זה הניגוד ש-«although» מבקש. «forget» (לשכוח) לא יוצר ניגוד: «לא יכול היה לשכוח את השם למרות שידע את השיר» לא הגיוני.","w":[["remember","לזכור"],["although","למרות ש... (+משפט)"]]},{"q":"The streets were still wet this morning, ___ it had rained heavily during the night.","o":["since","although","unless","so that"],"a":0,"ex":"«since» כאן = מכיוון ש. הרחובות רטובים כי ירד גשם בלילה: החלק השני הוא הסיבה. «although» (למרות ש) לא מתאים, כי אין ניגוד בין גשם לרחוב רטוב.","w":[["since","מכיוון ש..."],["heavily","בכבדות, בחוזקה"]]},{"q":"Our cat is very ___; she hides under the bed whenever a stranger comes into the house.","o":["friendly","hungry","shy","loud"],"a":2,"ex":"«shy» = ביישן. החתולה מתחבאת מתחת למיטה כשאדם זר נכנס, וזה מה שעושה חתול ביישן. «friendly» (ידידותי) הוא ההפך: חתול ידידותי היה ניגש לאורח.","w":[["shy","ביישן"],["stranger","אדם זר"]]}]},"p0sc3":{"id":"p0sc3","tier":0,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"Gal finished all his homework; ___, he cleaned his room and helped his father in the garden.","o":["however","for example","instead","in addition"],"a":3,"ex":"«in addition» = בנוסף. גל סיים שיעורי בית, וחוץ מזה גם ניקה וגם עזר: הוספה של עוד דברים. «however» (עם זאת) דורש ניגוד, ואין כאן ניגוד.","w":[["in addition","בנוסף"],["however","עם זאת, אולם"]]},{"q":"The price of tomatoes went up this month, because the cold weather ___ much of the crop in the south.","o":["protected","grew","damaged","sold"],"a":2,"ex":"«damaged» = הזיק, פגע. מזג האוויר הקר פגע בחלק גדול מהיבול, ולכן יש פחות עגבניות והמחיר עלה. «protected» (הגן) הפוך: אם היבול היה מוגן, המחיר לא היה עולה.","w":[["damage","להזיק, לפגוע"],["crop","יבול"]]},{"q":"You can stay at the party ___ ten o'clock, but after that you must come home.","o":["since","until","during","unless"],"a":1,"ex":"«until» = עד. מותר להישאר עד השעה עשר, ואחרי זה צריך לחזור. «since» (מאז) מתאר זמן שהתחיל בעבר, וזה לא מתאים למשפט על הערב הזה.","w":[["until","עד ש..."]]},{"q":"This bag is too ___ for me to carry alone; can you help me lift it?","o":["heavy","light","small","cheap"],"a":0,"ex":"«heavy» = כבד. הוא מבקש עזרה להרים את התיק, ולכן התיק כבד מדי. «light» (קל) הוא ההפך: תיק קל לא צריך עזרה.","w":[["heavy","כבד"],["lift","להרים"]]}]},"p0sc4":{"id":"p0sc4","tier":0,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"Before the exam, the teacher ___ the students to turn off their phones, because many of them had forgotten to do so the week before.","o":["reminded","allowed","forbade","invited"],"a":0,"ex":"«remind» = להזכיר. בשבוע הקודם תלמידים רבים שכחו לכבות את הטלפון, ולכן המורה הזכירה להם. «forbade» (אסרה) אומר את ההפך, ו-«allowed» (הרשתה) לא מתאים, כי מי ששכח צריך תזכורת ולא רשות.","w":[["remind","להזכיר"],["allow","להרשות"],["forbid","לאסור"]]},{"q":"The beach was closed ___ the strong winds, so we spent the afternoon at the cinema.","o":["in spite of","because of","instead of","in addition to"],"a":1,"ex":"«because of» = בגלל. החוף נסגר בגלל הרוחות החזקות, ולכן הלכו לקולנוע. «in spite of» (למרות) לא הגיוני: רוחות חזקות הן סיבה לסגור חוף, לא דבר שמנוגד לסגירה.","w":[["because of","בגלל (+שם עצם)"],["in spite of","למרות (+שם עצם)"]]},{"q":"It is ___ to swim in this river, because the water is deep and moves very fast.","o":["safe","pleasant","dangerous","useful"],"a":2,"ex":"«dangerous» = מסוכן. מים עמוקים וזרם מהיר הופכים את השחייה למסוכנת. «safe» (בטוח) הוא ההפך ממה שהסיבה במשפט מתארת.","w":[["dangerous","מסוכן"],["deep","עמוק"]]},{"q":"Yael ___ a lot of money last year by riding her bike to work instead of taking a taxi.","o":["spent","lost","borrowed","saved"],"a":3,"ex":"«save» = לחסוך. רכיבה על אופניים במקום מונית עולה פחות, ולכן היא חסכה כסף. «spent» (הוציאה) הפוך: אופניים לא גורמים להוציא הרבה כסף.","w":[["save","לחסוך; להציל"],["instead of","במקום (+שם עצם / ing)"]]}]},"p0sc5":{"id":"p0sc5","tier":0,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"___ his long day at work, Avi still went to watch his daughter's school play.","o":["Because of","Instead of","In spite of","In addition to"],"a":2,"ex":"«In spite of» = למרות. אבי היה אחרי יום עבודה ארוך, ובכל זאת הלך להצגה, והמילה «still» (ובכל זאת) מראה שיש כאן ויתור. «Because of» (בגלל) לא הגיוני: יום ארוך הוא לא סיבה ללכת להצגה.","w":[["in spite of","למרות (+שם עצם)"],["still","ובכל זאת; עדיין"]]},{"q":"The instructions in the box were so ___ that we built the new table in only twenty minutes.","o":["confusing","long","boring","clear"],"a":3,"ex":"«clear» = ברור. ההוראות היו כל כך ברורות שבנו את השולחן מהר. «confusing» (מבלבל) הפוך: הוראות מבלבלות היו גורמות לעבודה איטית.","w":[["clear","ברור"],["so... that","כל כך... ש..."]]},{"q":"Many animals sleep through most of the cold winter; bears, ___, may not eat anything for several months.","o":["for instance","however","instead","otherwise"],"a":0,"ex":"«for instance» = למשל. הדובים הם דוגמה לבעלי חיים שישנים בחורף. «however» (עם זאת) היה מציג ניגוד, אבל הדובים לא שונים משאר בעלי החיים כאן, הם דוגמה להם.","w":[["for instance","למשל"],["several","כמה, מספר"]]},{"q":"The train was ___ by an hour because of a problem on the tracks, so many passengers were late for work.","o":["repaired","delayed","filled","painted"],"a":1,"ex":"«delayed» = התעכב. בגלל בעיה במסילה הרכבת איחרה בשעה, ולכן נוסעים איחרו לעבודה. «repaired» (תוקן) לא מסביר למה הנוסעים איחרו.","w":[["delay","לעכב, עיכוב"],["passenger","נוסע"]]}]},"p0sc6":{"id":"p0sc6","tier":0,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"Shira studied hard all year, ___ she received the highest grade in her class.","o":["but","so","or","unless"],"a":1,"ex":"«so» = לכן. שירה למדה קשה, ולכן קיבלה את הציון הכי גבוה: החלק השני הוא תוצאה של הראשון. «but» (אבל) מציג ניגוד, ואין ניגוד בין למידה קשה לציון גבוה.","w":[["so","לכן, אז"],["grade","ציון"]]},{"q":"The doctor asked Ron to ___ eating sweets for a month to see whether his stomach pains would go away.","o":["stop","start","enjoy","continue"],"a":0,"ex":"«stop» = להפסיק. הרופא רוצה לבדוק אם הכאבים יעברו בלי ממתקים, ולכן ביקש להפסיק לאכול אותם. «continue» (להמשיך) לא יעזור לבדוק את זה.","w":[["stop","להפסיק"],["whether","האם; בין אם"]]},{"q":"Call me ___ you arrive at the station, and I will come to pick you up right away.","o":["until","although","unless","as soon as"],"a":3,"ex":"«as soon as» = ברגע ש. כשתגיע לתחנה תתקשר, ואני אבוא מיד. «unless» (אלא אם כן) הופך את המשמעות: «תתקשר אלא אם תגיע» לא הגיוני.","w":[["as soon as","ברגע ש..., מיד כש..."],["pick up","לאסוף"]]},{"q":"Plastic bags are a serious problem for the ___, because they can stay in the sea for hundreds of years.","o":["economy","weather","environment","traffic"],"a":2,"ex":"«environment» = הסביבה. שקיות שנשארות בים מאות שנים פוגעות בטבע ובסביבה. «economy» (כלכלה) או «weather» (מזג האוויר) לא קשורים לזיהום בים.","w":[["environment","סביבה"],["serious","רציני, חמור"]]}]},"p0rs1":{"id":"p0rs1","tier":0,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"Because the city added more buses to the morning schedule, fewer people now drive their cars to work in the center.","o":["Because fewer people drive their cars to work in the center, the city added more buses to the morning schedule.","The city put more buses on the morning schedule; as a result, fewer people drive to work downtown now.","Although the city added more buses in the morning, more people now drive their cars to work in the center.","The city added more buses to the morning schedule, but almost nobody uses them to get to work."],"a":1,"ex":"«Because» הוחלף ב-«as a result» (כתוצאה מכך), והסיבה והתוצאה נשארו באותו כיוון: יותר אוטובוסים, ולכן פחות נהגים. התשובה שמתחילה ב-«Because fewer people drive» הופכת את הסיבה והתוצאה.","w":[["as a result","כתוצאה מכך"],["because","כי, מפני ש... (+משפט)"],["schedule","לוח זמנים"]]},{"q":"Many older people find it hard to use new phones, so some shops now offer free lessons on Sunday mornings.","o":["Many older people find new phones hard to use, although all shops now offer free lessons on Sunday mornings.","Some shops offer free lessons on Sunday mornings, so many older people now find it easy to use new phones.","Many older people teach shop workers how to use new phones during free lessons on Sunday mornings.","Since a lot of older people have difficulty using new phones, several shops now give free classes on Sunday mornings."],"a":3,"ex":"«so» (לכן) הפך ל-«Since» (מכיוון ש) בתחילת המשפט, ו-«find it hard» הפך ל-«have difficulty». הקושי של המבוגרים הוא עדיין הסיבה לשיעורים. התשובה עם «all shops» משנה «some» (חלק) ל«כל», ומוסיפה ניגוד שאין במקור.","w":[["since","מכיוון ש..."],["so","לכן, אז"],["difficulty","קושי"]]},{"q":"Unlike most birds, penguins cannot fly, but they are excellent swimmers and can stay underwater for several minutes while hunting for fish.","o":["Most birds can fly, but penguins cannot; still, they swim extremely well and can spend several minutes underwater hunting fish.","Like most other birds, penguins are not able to fly, so they have to stay underwater for several minutes while hunting fish.","Penguins can fly as well as most other birds, and they can also stay underwater for several minutes while they hunt for fish.","Penguins cannot fly, and since they are poor swimmers, they rarely stay underwater for more than a few seconds when hunting fish."],"a":0,"ex":"«Unlike most birds» הפך ל-«Most birds can fly, but penguins cannot», «but» הפך ל-«still», ו-«excellent swimmers» ל-«swim extremely well». «Like most other birds» אומר שגם רוב הציפורים לא עפות, וזה הפוך מהמקור.","w":[["unlike","בניגוד ל... (+שם עצם)"],["still","ובכל זאת; עדיין"]]}]},"p0rs2":{"id":"p0rs2","tier":0,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"People who live near a park tend to walk more each day than people who live far from green areas.","o":["Living near a park makes people walk more each day, because green areas give them more energy.","People who live far from green areas tend to walk more each day than those who live near a park.","Those living close to a park usually walk more every day than those whose homes are far from green spaces.","All people who live near a park walk more each day than anyone who lives far from green areas."],"a":2,"ex":"«tend to» (נוטים) הפך ל-«usually» (בדרך כלל): זו נטייה, לא חוק. התשובה עם «makes people walk» מוסיפה שהפארק הוא הסיבה, ו-«All people» הופך נטייה לחוק שתקף לכולם.","w":[["tend to","נוטה ל..."],["usually","בדרך כלל"],["close to","קרוב ל..."]]},{"q":"If you water this plant only once a week, it will grow well even in a small apartment with little sunlight.","o":["Watering this plant once a week is enough for it to grow well, even in a small apartment that gets little sun.","This plant will grow well in a small apartment only if it gets a lot of sunlight and water every day.","This plant grows well in a small apartment, but it must be watered several times a week because there is little sunlight.","Even if you water this plant once a week, it will not grow well in a small apartment with little sunlight."],"a":0,"ex":"המקור אומר שמספיק להשקות פעם בשבוע, והצמח יגדל טוב גם עם מעט שמש. «is enough» (מספיק) מבטא את «only once a week». התשובה עם «only if it gets a lot of sunlight» סותרת את «little sunlight» שבמקור.","w":[["even","אפילו"],["only if","רק אם"],["enough","מספיק"]]},{"q":"Before the new law was passed, drivers could park on this street for free, but now they must pay for every hour.","o":["Because drivers had to pay for every hour of parking on this street, a new law now lets them park for free.","Drivers have always had to pay for every hour they park on this street, both before and after the new law.","Before the new law was passed, drivers paid for parking on this street, and now they can park for only one hour.","Drivers used to park on this street at no cost; the new law, however, now requires them to pay for each hour."],"a":3,"ex":"«used to» = נהגו בעבר, ו-«at no cost» = «for free». לפני החוק החניה הייתה חינם, ועכשיו משלמים על כל שעה. התשובה «Drivers have always had to pay» אומרת שתמיד שילמו, וזה סותר את המקור.","w":[["before","לפני"],["used to","נהג ל... (בעבר)"],["require","לדרוש, לחייב"]]}]},"p0rs3":{"id":"p0rs3","tier":0,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"Although the zoo's new elephant house opened only last week, more than ten thousand people have already come to see it.","o":["Because the zoo's new elephant house opened last week, fewer than ten thousand people have come to see it so far.","Although more than ten thousand people wanted to see the zoo's new elephant house, it has not opened yet.","The zoo's new elephant house has been open for many years, and ten thousand people visit it every week.","Over ten thousand visitors have already seen the zoo's new elephant house, even though it has been open for just one week."],"a":3,"ex":"«Although» הפך ל-«even though» וסדר החלקים התהפך, «more than» הפך ל-«over», ו-«only last week» ל-«just one week». התשובה עם «fewer than» (פחות מ) הופכת את הכמות.","w":[["although","למרות ש... (+משפט)"],["even though","אף על פי ש..."],["already","כבר"]]},{"q":"Our neighbor rarely leaves his house in the winter, but in the summer he spends almost every evening sitting in the garden.","o":["Our neighbor often leaves his house in the winter, and in the summer he also sits in the garden every evening.","In the winter our neighbor seldom goes outside, whereas during the summer he sits in the garden nearly every evening.","Our neighbor rarely sits in the garden in the summer, but in the winter he goes out almost every evening.","Our neighbor rarely leaves his house in the winter because he is ill, but in the summer he feels better."],"a":1,"ex":"«rarely» = «seldom» (לעיתים רחוקות), «almost» = «nearly» (כמעט), ו-«but» הפך ל-«whereas». «often» (לעיתים קרובות) הופך את «rarely», והתשובה עם «because he is ill» מוסיפה סיבה שאין במקור.","w":[["rarely","לעיתים רחוקות"],["seldom","לעיתים רחוקות"],["whereas","בעוד ש..., ואילו"]]},{"q":"To protect the rare birds that nest near the lake, the city has decided to close the lake path next spring.","o":["The city has decided to open a new path by the lake next spring so that visitors can see the rare birds.","Because the rare birds no longer nest near the lake, the city has decided to close the lake path next spring.","Next spring, the path by the lake will be closed by the city so that the rare birds nesting there stay safe.","Bird lovers have asked the city to close the lake path next spring, but the city has decided to keep it open."],"a":2,"ex":"המשפט הפך לסביל («will be closed by the city»), ו-«To protect» הפך ל-«so that ... stay safe» (כדי שיהיו מוגנות). המטרה נשארה: להגן על הציפורים. התשובה עם «no longer nest» אומרת שהציפורים כבר לא שם, וזה משנה את הסיבה.","w":[["so that","כדי ש... (+משפט)"],["protect","להגן"],["nest","לקנן"]]}]},"p0rs4":{"id":"p0rs4","tier":0,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"Fresh fish should be kept in the fridge and eaten within two days; otherwise, it can make people feel sick.","o":["Unless fresh fish is stored in a fridge and eaten in two days or less, it may make people ill.","Fresh fish can still make people feel sick, even if it is kept in the fridge and eaten within two days.","Fresh fish should be eaten within two days, so people who keep it in the fridge often get sick.","Fresh fish can be kept in the fridge for several weeks and still be eaten without making anyone sick."],"a":0,"ex":"«otherwise» (אחרת) הפך ל-«Unless» (אלא אם כן): אם לא שומרים במקרר ואוכלים תוך יומיים, הדג עלול להזיק. «within two days» = «in two days or less». התשובה עם «even if» אומרת שהדג מזיק גם כשעושים הכול נכון, וזה הפוך.","w":[["otherwise","אחרת"],["unless","אלא אם כן"],["within","בתוך, תוך"]]},{"q":"The new hotel by the beach brought hundreds of jobs to the town; however, it also made the beach much more crowded in summer.","o":["Because the beach was too crowded in summer, the town built a new hotel that brought hundreds of jobs.","The new hotel by the beach brought only a few jobs to the town, and the beach is now almost empty in summer.","Although the new beach hotel provided the town with hundreds of jobs, it also led to far bigger summer crowds on the beach.","The new hotel by the beach brought hundreds of jobs to the town, so local people now have more time to enjoy the beach."],"a":2,"ex":"«however» הפך ל-«Although» בתחילת המשפט, «brought jobs» ל-«provided ... with jobs», ו-«more crowded» ל-«bigger crowds». גם היתרון וגם החיסרון נשארו. התשובה עם «only a few jobs» משנה את הכמות והופכת את הצפיפות.","w":[["however","עם זאת, אולם"],["although","למרות ש... (+משפט)"],["crowded","צפוף, מלא אנשים"]]},{"q":"Children usually learn a second language more easily than adults, especially when they start before the age of ten.","o":["Adults usually learn a second language more easily than children, especially if they start before the age of ten.","Learning a second language is generally easier for children than for adults, particularly if they begin before age ten.","All children learn a second language easily, but only if they start studying it before the age of ten.","Children usually learn a second language more easily than adults, because children's teachers are especially patient with them."],"a":1,"ex":"«usually» הפך ל-«generally», «especially» ל-«particularly», והמבנה השתנה: «Learning ... is easier for children». התשובה שמתחילה ב-«Adults» הופכת מי לומד בקלות, והאחרונה מוסיפה סיבה (מורים סבלניים) שלא נאמרה.","w":[["especially","במיוחד"],["generally","בדרך כלל, באופן כללי"],["easily","בקלות"]]}]},"p0rs5":{"id":"p0rs5","tier":0,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"After the flower shop began selling online, the number of its customers doubled, so it now plans to hire more workers.","o":["The flower shop began selling online because it had hired more workers and needed twice as many customers.","The flower shop intends to employ additional staff, as it has had twice as many customers since it started selling online.","After the flower shop began selling online, it lost half of its customers, so it plans to let some workers go.","The flower shop has twice as many workers as customers since it started selling its flowers online."],"a":1,"ex":"«so» (לכן) הפך ל-«as» (מכיוון ש), «doubled» ל-«twice as many», ו-«hire more workers» ל-«employ additional staff». הסיבה (יותר לקוחות) והתוצאה (עוד עובדים) נשארו. «lost half of its customers» הופך את הנתון.","w":[["as","מכיוון ש...; כפי ש...; בזמן ש..."],["double","להכפיל"],["hire","להעסיק, לשכור"]]},{"q":"Many people believe that cats do not like water, but some kinds of cats actually enjoy swimming and playing in it.","o":["It is widely believed that cats dislike water; in fact, certain types of cats like to swim and play in it.","Many people believe that cats enjoy swimming, but in fact most kinds of cats do not like water at all.","All kinds of cats actually enjoy swimming and playing in water, even though many people do not like cats.","Since some kinds of cats enjoy swimming, many people believe that cats should play in water every day."],"a":0,"ex":"«Many people believe» הפך לסביל «It is widely believed», «actually» ל-«in fact», ו-«some kinds» ל-«certain types». התשובה עם «All kinds of cats» הופכת «some» (חלק) ל«כל», ומשנה גם את מה שאנשים לא אוהבים.","w":[["actually","בעצם, למעשה"],["in fact","למעשה, בעצם"],["dislike","לא לאהוב"]]},{"q":"The company let its workers work from home on Fridays, and since then, fewer of them have been late on other weekdays.","o":["Because the workers can stay home on Fridays, they are now never late during the rest of the week.","The company let its workers work from home on Fridays because many of them had been late during the week.","Since the company let its workers work from home on Fridays, more of them have been late on other days.","Ever since working from home on Fridays was allowed, fewer employees have come in late on the other weekdays."],"a":3,"ex":"המקור מתאר רק מה קרה מאז («since then»): פחות איחורים. «Ever since» (מאז ש) שומר על אותו קשר של זמן, בלי לטעון שזו הסיבה. התשובה עם «Because ... never late» מוסיפה סיבה ומשנה «fewer» (פחות) ל-«never» (אף פעם).","w":[["since","מאז"],["fewer","פחות (בספירה)"],["allow","להרשות, לאפשר"]]}]},"p0rs6":{"id":"p0rs6","tier":0,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"Even though the test was short, very few students finished it on time, because the questions were much harder than usual.","o":["Because the test was short, most students finished it on time, although the questions were harder than usual.","Very few students finished the test on time, since it was much longer and easier than usual tests.","The questions were far more difficult than normal, so hardly any students completed the test in time, despite its short length.","The test was short and the questions were easier than usual, so very few students needed the whole time to finish it."],"a":2,"ex":"«very few» = «hardly any» (כמעט אף אחד), «Even though» הפך ל-«despite» בסוף, ו-«because» הפך ל-«so» עם סדר הפוך. התשובה עם «most students» הופכת את הכמות, והשנייה אומרת שהמבחן ארוך, וזה סותר את המקור.","w":[["even though","אף על פי ש..."],["despite","למרות (+שם עצם)"],["hardly","כמעט לא"]]},{"q":"Instead of throwing away old clothes, many families now give them to charity or exchange them with friends and neighbors.","o":["Many families now throw away old clothes instead of giving them to charity or to friends and neighbors.","Many families now buy old clothes from charity, and they also sell them to friends and neighbors.","Few families give old clothes to charity, because their friends and neighbors usually throw them away.","Today, many families donate old clothes or swap them with friends and neighbors rather than throw them out."],"a":3,"ex":"«Instead of» הפך ל-«rather than» בסוף המשפט, «give to charity» ל-«donate», ו-«exchange» ל-«swap». התשובה הראשונה הופכת את מה שהמשפחות עושות: זורקות במקום לתרום.","w":[["instead of","במקום (+שם עצם / ing)"],["rather than","במקום, ולא"],["exchange","להחליף"]]},{"q":"The village was almost empty during the week, as most of its young people worked in the city and came home only on weekends.","o":["Most of the village's young people worked in the city and returned only for weekends, so on weekdays few people were there.","The village was almost empty on weekends, because most of its young people came home from the city only during the week.","Most of the village's young people left the city and moved back home, so the village is no longer empty during the week.","The young people of the village went to work in the city because the village was almost empty during the week."],"a":0,"ex":"«as» (מכיוון ש) הפך ל-«so» (לכן) והסדר התהפך: הצעירים עבדו בעיר, ולכן באמצע השבוע כמעט אין אנשים בכפר. התשובה הראשונה מחליפה בין סוף השבוע לימי החול, והאחרונה הופכת את הסיבה והתוצאה.","w":[["as","מכיוון ש...; כפי ש...; בזמן ש..."],["so","לכן, אז"],["empty","ריק"]]}]},"p1sc1":{"id":"p1sc1","tier":1,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"The town's water supply was found to be ___ with chemicals from a nearby factory, so residents were told to drink only bottled water.","o":["purified","enriched","contaminated","supplemented"],"a":2,"ex":"«contaminated» = מזוהם. אם התושבים התבקשו לשתות רק מים בבקבוקים, המים בעיר מסוכנים, כלומר מזוהמים בכימיקלים. «enriched» (מועשר) ו-«purified» (מטוהר) נשמעים חיוביים ולא מסבירים למה אסור לשתות.","w":[["contaminated","מזוהם"],["purify","לטהר"],["resident","תושב"]]},{"q":"Most of the company's profits come from a single product; ___, a drop in its sales could put the whole firm at risk.","o":["thus","conversely","likewise","for instance"],"a":0,"ex":"«thus» = לפיכך. החלק השני הוא מסקנה מהראשון: אם רוב הרווח בא ממוצר אחד, ירידה במכירות שלו מסכנת את כל החברה. «conversely» (מנגד) היה מציג ניגוד, ואין כאן ניגוד.","w":[["thus","לפיכך, כך"],["conversely","ובאופן הפוך, מנגד"],["likewise","כמו כן, באותו אופן"]]},{"q":"To lower the company's electricity bills, engineers are trying to ___ the amount of energy lost as heat inside the plant.","o":["exaggerate","accumulate","conceal","minimize"],"a":3,"ex":"«minimize» = לצמצם למינימום. כדי להוריד את חשבון החשמל צריך שפחות אנרגיה תלך לאיבוד. «conceal» (להסתיר) לא מוריד את החשבון, ו-«accumulate» (לצבור) היה מגדיל את הבזבוז.","w":[["minimize","לצמצם, להקטין למינימום"],["accumulate","לצבור"],["conceal","להסתיר"]]},{"q":"___ the strong opposition of local residents, the city council approved the plan to build a highway through the park.","o":["Owing to","Despite","Thanks to","In addition to"],"a":1,"ex":"«Despite» = למרות. התושבים התנגדו, ובכל זאת התוכנית אושרה, וזה ניגוד שדורש מילת ויתור. «Owing to» ו-«Thanks to» היו אומרים שההתנגדות היא הסיבה לאישור, וזה לא הגיוני.","w":[["despite","למרות (+שם עצם)"],["owing to","בשל, עקב"],["opposition","התנגדות"]]}]},"p1sc2":{"id":"p1sc2","tier":1,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"The jury's decision was ___: all twelve members agreed that the defendant was not guilty.","o":["controversial","unanimous","premature","partial"],"a":1,"ex":"«unanimous» = פה אחד. אחרי הנקודתיים מוסבר שכל שנים עשר המושבעים הסכימו. «controversial» (שנוי במחלוקת) אומר בדיוק את ההפך.","w":[["unanimous","פה אחד, בהסכמה מלאה"],["controversial","שנוי במחלוקת"],["defendant","נאשם"]]},{"q":"The area is now a dry desert, ___ the marine fossils found there show that it was once covered by a shallow sea.","o":["unless","in case","in order that","yet"],"a":3,"ex":"«yet» = ובכל זאת, אך. יש ניגוד: היום האזור הוא מדבר יבש, אבל מאובנים של בעלי חיים ימיים מראים שפעם היה שם ים. «unless» (אלא אם כן) ו-«in order that» (כדי ש) לא יוצרים משפט הגיוני.","w":[["yet","ובכל זאת, אך"],["fossil","מאובן"],["marine","ימי, של הים"]]},{"q":"Because the two studies used very different methods, any ___ between their results should be made with great care.","o":["comparison","prediction","publication","donation"],"a":0,"ex":"«comparison» = השוואה. המילה «between» (בין התוצאות) והשיטות השונות מראים שמדובר בהשוואה בין שני מחקרים. «prediction» (תחזית) לא נעשית «between» תוצאות.","w":[["comparison","השוואה"],["method","שיטה"],["prediction","תחזית"]]},{"q":"Fewer people now buy printed newspapers; ___, many publishers have moved most of their content online.","o":["on the other hand","for instance","as a result","in contrast"],"a":2,"ex":"«as a result» = כתוצאה מכך. בגלל שפחות אנשים קונים עיתון מודפס, המו\"לים עברו לאינטרנט: סיבה ותוצאה. «on the other hand» ו-«in contrast» מציגים ניגוד, ואין כאן ניגוד.","w":[["as a result","כתוצאה מכך"],["in contrast","לעומת זאת"],["publisher","מו\"ל, הוצאה לאור"]]}]},"p1sc3":{"id":"p1sc3","tier":1,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"You will not be able to vote in the election ___ you register at least thirty days before it takes place.","o":["because","unless","whereas","once"],"a":1,"ex":"«unless» = אלא אם כן. ההרשמה היא תנאי: בלי הרשמה לא מצביעים. «once» (ברגע ש) היה אומר שאחרי ההרשמה לא תוכל להצביע, וזה הפוך מההיגיון.","w":[["unless","אלא אם כן"],["once","ברגע ש..., לאחר ש..."],["register","להירשם"]]},{"q":"The museum will remain open during the renovation work, ___ some of its galleries will be closed to visitors.","o":["although","because","so","unless"],"a":0,"ex":"«although» = למרות ש. המוזיאון פתוח, אבל חלק מהאולמות סגורים: ניגוד. «because» היה אומר שהמוזיאון פתוח בגלל שאולמות סגורים, וזה לא הגיוני.","w":[["although","למרות ש... (+משפט)"],["renovation","שיפוץ"],["remain","להישאר"]]},{"q":"Later experiments ___ the original findings, showing the same effect in much larger groups of people.","o":["contradicted","delayed","confirmed","ignored"],"a":2,"ex":"«confirmed» = אישרו. הניסויים המאוחרים מצאו את אותה השפעה, כלומר הם תומכים בממצאים המקוריים. «contradicted» (סתרו) היה מתאים רק אם התוצאה הייתה שונה.","w":[["confirm","לאשר, לאמת"],["contradict","לסתור"],["findings","ממצאים"]]},{"q":"Her argument was ___: she supported every point with clear evidence and answered her critics' objections in advance.","o":["irrelevant","hesitant","biased","persuasive"],"a":3,"ex":"«persuasive» = משכנע. טיעון שכל נקודה בו נתמכת בראיות ועונה מראש על ההתנגדויות הוא טיעון משכנע. «biased» (מוטה) ו-«hesitant» (מהסס) הם תכונות שליליות שלא מתאימות לתיאור.","w":[["persuasive","משכנע"],["biased","מוטה, משוחד"],["objection","התנגדות, טענה נגדית"]]}]},"p1sc4":{"id":"p1sc4","tier":1,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"Some birds, ___ penguins and ostriches, cannot fly at all, although they still have wings.","o":["rather than","such as","unlike","except for"],"a":1,"ex":"«such as» = כגון. פינגווינים ויענים הם דוגמה לציפורים שלא עפות. «unlike» (בניגוד ל) היה אומר שהם כן עפים, וזה לא נכון.","w":[["such as","כגון, כמו"],["unlike","בניגוד ל... (+שם עצם)"],["except for","חוץ מ..."]]},{"q":"The new manager plans to ___ the department by merging small teams and removing unnecessary layers of management.","o":["abandon","imitate","celebrate","restructure"],"a":3,"ex":"«restructure» = לארגן מחדש. איחוד צוותים והסרת דרגי ניהול הם שינוי במבנה של המחלקה. «abandon» (לנטוש) לא מתאים, כי המנהל לא עוזב את המחלקה אלא משנה אותה.","w":[["restructure","לארגן מחדש"],["merge","למזג, לאחד"],["abandon","לנטוש"]]},{"q":"The instructions were so ___ that even first-time users managed to assemble the furniture in under an hour.","o":["straightforward","lengthy","complicated","outdated"],"a":0,"ex":"«straightforward» = פשוט וברור. אם גם מי שמרכיב בפעם הראשונה הצליח תוך פחות משעה, ההוראות קלות. «complicated» (מסובך) אומר את ההפך.","w":[["straightforward","פשוט, ברור"],["assemble","להרכיב"],["so... that","כל כך... ש..."]]},{"q":"Although the disease is rare, it spreads ___ once it appears in a herd, sometimes infecting every animal within a week.","o":["gradually","harmlessly","rapidly","rarely"],"a":2,"ex":"«rapidly» = במהירות. אם כל העדר נדבק תוך שבוע, המחלה מתפשטת מהר. «gradually» (בהדרגה) סותר את «within a week», ו-«harmlessly» (בלי נזק) לא מתאים למחלה שמדביקה את כולם.","w":[["rapidly","במהירות"],["gradually","בהדרגה"],["herd","עדר"]]}]},"p1sc5":{"id":"p1sc5","tier":1,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"Heavy rain caused the river to ___ its banks, flooding hundreds of homes in the valley.","o":["repair","protect","strengthen","overflow"],"a":3,"ex":"«overflow» = לעלות על גדותיו. הנהר הציף בתים, כלומר המים יצאו מהגדות. «protect» (להגן) ו-«strengthen» (לחזק) לא מסבירים את ההצפה.","w":[["overflow","לגלוש, לעלות על גדותיו"],["flood","להציף"],["bank","גדה (של נהר)"]]},{"q":"Passengers must remain seated ___ the plane has come to a complete stop.","o":["since","whereas","until","so that"],"a":2,"ex":"«until» = עד ש. הנוסעים יושבים עד לרגע שהמטוס עוצר לגמרי. «since» (מכיוון ש) היה אומר שצריך לשבת בגלל שהמטוס כבר עצר, וזה לא הגיוני.","w":[["until","עד ש..."],["since","מכיוון ש...; מאז"],["remain","להישאר"]]},{"q":"Online shopping saves customers time; ___, many people still prefer to see and touch products before buying them.","o":["on the other hand","therefore","for example","similarly"],"a":0,"ex":"«on the other hand» = מצד שני. מצד אחד קנייה ברשת חוסכת זמן, מצד שני אנשים רוצים לגעת במוצר: ניגוד. «therefore» (לכן) היה הופך את זה לתוצאה, וזה לא הגיוני.","w":[["on the other hand","מצד שני"],["therefore","לכן"],["similarly","באופן דומה"]]},{"q":"The scientist's ___ to her research was remarkable; she worked in the laboratory almost every day for thirty years.","o":["objection","dedication","threat","indifference"],"a":1,"ex":"«dedication» = מסירות. מי שעבדה במעבדה כמעט כל יום במשך שלושים שנה מסורה למחקר. «indifference» (אדישות) אומרת את ההפך.","w":[["dedication","מסירות"],["indifference","אדישות"],["remarkable","יוצא דופן, מרשים"]]}]},"p1sc6":{"id":"p1sc6","tier":1,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"The new trains are faster and quieter than the old ones; ___, their seats are wider and more comfortable.","o":["instead","otherwise","moreover","in contrast"],"a":2,"ex":"«moreover» = יתרה מזאת. החלק השני מוסיף עוד יתרון של הרכבות החדשות. «in contrast» (לעומת זאת) מתאים לניגוד, אבל כאן שני החלקים חיוביים.","w":[["moreover","יתרה מזאת"],["otherwise","אחרת"],["in contrast","לעומת זאת"]]},{"q":"Reliable data on the region's population are ___, since no official census has been carried out there for over fifty years.","o":["abundant","recent","accurate","scarce"],"a":3,"ex":"«scarce» = נדיר, מועט. אם לא נערך מפקד אוכלוסין חמישים שנה, אין כמעט נתונים אמינים. «abundant» (בשפע) ו-«recent» (עדכני) אומרים את ההפך.","w":[["scarce","נדיר, מועט"],["abundant","בשפע"],["census","מפקד אוכלוסין"]]},{"q":"The committee decided to ___ its decision until more information about the project's costs becomes available.","o":["announce","postpone","reverse","celebrate"],"a":1,"ex":"«postpone» = לדחות. «until» (עד ש) מראה שההחלטה מחכה למידע נוסף, כלומר נדחית. «announce» (להודיע) לא מתאים, כי אין עדיין החלטה להודיע עליה.","w":[["postpone","לדחות (למועד מאוחר)"],["reverse","להפוך, לבטל"],["available","זמין"]]},{"q":"Doctors advise patients to ___ from eating for at least eight hours before the operation.","o":["refrain","recover","suffer","benefit"],"a":0,"ex":"«refrain from» = להימנע מ. לפני ניתוח צריך לא לאכול שמונה שעות. «benefit from» (להפיק תועלת מ) ו-«recover from» (להחלים מ) לא מתאימים להוראה של רופא לפני ניתוח.","w":[["refrain from","להימנע מ..."],["recover","להחלים"],["advise","לייעץ, להמליץ"]]}]},"p1rs1":{"id":"p1rs1","tier":1,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"Although electric cars produce no exhaust fumes, their overall environmental benefit depends largely on how the electricity used to charge them is generated.","o":["Electric cars do not emit exhaust, but how much they actually help the environment is mostly determined by the way their charging power is produced.","Because electric cars emit no exhaust fumes, they help the environment equally regardless of the source of the electricity that charges them.","Electric cars produce some exhaust fumes, so their environmental benefit depends only slightly on how their charging electricity is produced.","How electricity is generated in a country depends largely on the number of electric cars that are being charged there, even though they produce no exhaust fumes."],"a":0,"ex":"במקור: למכוניות חשמליות אין פליטה, אבל התועלת לסביבה תלויה בעיקר באופן שבו מייצרים את החשמל. התשובה הנכונה אומרת את זה במילים אחרות («mostly determined by»). השנייה אומרת שהמקור לא משנה, השלישית משנה את המידה («only slightly») והרביעית הופכת מי תלוי במי.","w":[["although","למרות ש... (+משפט)"],["depend on","תלוי ב..."],["regardless of","בלי קשר ל..., בלי להתחשב ב..."]]},{"q":"The festival, which had attracted large crowds for decades, was cancelled this year owing to a shortage of volunteers rather than a lack of public interest.","o":["This year's festival, popular for decades, was cancelled because the public had lost interest in it, even though there were plenty of willing volunteers.","Although there were not enough volunteers this year, the festival, popular for decades, still took place because public interest remained high.","This year's festival, popular for decades, did not take place because there were not enough volunteers, not because the public had lost interest.","The festival has rarely attracted large crowds, and this year it was cancelled because both volunteers and public interest were lacking."],"a":2,"ex":"במקור: הפסטיבל בוטל בגלל מחסור במתנדבים, ולא («rather than») בגלל חוסר עניין. התשובה הנכונה שומרת על שתי הסיבות במקומן. הראשונה מחליפה ביניהן, השנייה אומרת שהפסטיבל התקיים, והרביעית אומרת שהוא כמעט לא משך קהל.","w":[["owing to","בשל, עקב"],["rather than","במקום, ולא"],["shortage","מחסור"]]},{"q":"Teenagers who sleep fewer than seven hours a night tend to get lower grades, although researchers have not shown that the lack of sleep causes this.","o":["Researchers have proven that teenagers get lower grades because they sleep fewer than seven hours a night, which harms their concentration in class.","Teenagers who get lower grades tend to sleep fewer than seven hours a night, since worrying about their schoolwork often keeps them awake until late at night.","Teenagers who sleep more than seven hours a night rarely get good grades, although researchers do not yet know exactly why this happens.","Lower grades are common among teenagers who sleep under seven hours a night, but it has not been proven that too little sleep is the reason."],"a":3,"ex":"במקור יש רק קשר («tend to»): מי שישן פחות מקבל ציונים נמוכים, אבל לא הוכח שהשינה היא הסיבה. התשובה הנכונה שומרת על זה. הראשונה טוענת שהוכחה סיבה, השנייה מוסיפה סיבה חדשה (דאגה ללימודים), והשלישית הופכת את הקשר.","w":[["tend to","נוטה ל..."],["although","למרות ש... (+משפט)"],["prove","להוכיח"]]}]},"p1rs2":{"id":"p1rs2","tier":1,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"Unlike earlier models, the new washing machine adjusts the amount of water it uses to the size of each load, thereby cutting water consumption by almost half.","o":["Like earlier models, the new washing machine uses the same amount of water for every load, although it is almost twice as efficient.","By matching its water use to how much laundry is inside, the new washing machine, in contrast to previous ones, uses nearly fifty percent less water.","The new washing machine uses almost twice as much water as earlier models because it adjusts the amount to the size of each load.","Earlier washing machines also adjusted their water use to the size of the load, but the new model has reduced consumption only slightly."],"a":1,"ex":"במקור: בניגוד לדגמים הקודמים, המכונה מתאימה את כמות המים לכביסה, ובכך («thereby») חוסכת כמעט חצי. התשובה הנכונה: «in contrast to previous ones» ו-«nearly fifty percent less». הראשונה אומרת שהמכונה כמו הקודמות, השלישית הופכת את החיסכון לבזבוז, והרביעית משנה את המידה («only slightly»).","w":[["unlike","בניגוד ל... (+שם עצם)"],["thereby","ובכך, על ידי כך"],["consumption","צריכה"]]},{"q":"Many species of frogs are disappearing at an alarming rate, and scientists believe that a fungal disease, spread partly through the international pet trade, is chiefly responsible.","o":["Scientists think a fungal infection, carried in part by the global pet trade, is the main reason that numerous frog species are rapidly vanishing.","Scientists believe that the international pet trade is the only cause of the frog disease, which has hardly affected the number of frog species.","A fungal disease is spreading quickly among pets around the world, and scientists believe that frogs sold in the pet trade are mainly to blame.","Although many frog species are disappearing, scientists doubt that a fungal disease spread through the international pet trade plays any significant role."],"a":0,"ex":"במקור: מינים רבים של צפרדעים נעלמים מהר, והמדענים חושבים שהגורם העיקרי («chiefly») הוא מחלת פטרייה שמופצת בחלקה דרך סחר בחיות מחמד. התשובה הנכונה: «the main reason». השנייה משנה את «partly» ל-«only», השלישית הופכת מי מדביק את מי, והרביעית אומרת שהמדענים מפקפקים.","w":[["chiefly","בעיקר"],["responsible","אחראי (לגורם)"],["species","מין (בטבע)"]]},{"q":"Since the bridge was closed for repairs, commuters from the northern suburbs have had to take a detour that adds roughly forty minutes to their journey.","o":["Commuters from the northern suburbs have saved about forty minutes a day since the bridge was reopened after the repairs were completed.","The bridge was closed for repairs because commuters from the northern suburbs had complained that crossing it added forty minutes to their trip.","Only a few commuters from the northern suburbs use the detour, which adds roughly four minutes to their journey since the bridge was closed.","Commuters coming from the northern suburbs now spend about forty extra minutes travelling, as they must go around while the bridge is being repaired."],"a":3,"ex":"במקור: מאז שהגשר נסגר לתיקונים, הנוסעים מהצפון עושים עיקוף שמוסיף כארבעים דקות. התשובה הנכונה: «forty extra minutes» ו-«go around». הראשונה אומרת שהגשר נפתח והם חוסכים זמן, השנייה הופכת סיבה ותוצאה, והשלישית משנה את המספרים.","w":[["since","מאז; מכיוון ש..."],["detour","עיקוף, דרך עוקפת"],["roughly","בערך"]]}]},"p1rs3":{"id":"p1rs3","tier":1,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"The manager postponed the meeting until Thursday so that the engineers would have enough time to finish testing the new software before presenting it.","o":["The engineers postponed the meeting until Thursday so that the manager would have enough time to test the new software before presenting it.","The meeting was held earlier than planned because the engineers had already finished testing the new software and wanted to present it.","To let the engineers complete their tests of the new software before showing it, the manager moved the meeting to Thursday.","Although the engineers had not finished testing the new software, the manager decided that they should present it at the meeting on Thursday."],"a":2,"ex":"במקור: המנהל דחה את הפגישה כדי («so that») שלמהנדסים יהיה זמן לסיים את הבדיקות. התשובה הנכונה מחליפה את «so that» ב-«To let». הראשונה מחליפה מי עשה מה, השנייה אומרת שהפגישה הוקדמה, והרביעית אומרת שיציגו בלי לסיים.","w":[["so that","כדי ש... (+משפט)"],["postpone","לדחות"],["in order to","כדי ל... (+פועל)"]]},{"q":"Even though the region receives very little rain, local farmers manage to grow a wide variety of crops by collecting water during the brief winter storms.","o":["Because the region receives a great deal of rain, local farmers grow many kinds of crops without needing to collect water during winter storms.","Despite the scarce rainfall in the region, the farmers there succeed in raising many kinds of crops thanks to the water they gather in short winter storms.","Local farmers grow only a few types of crops, since the little water they collect during the brief winter storms is not enough for more.","The brief winter storms in the region are so violent that local farmers can hardly collect any water, so they have stopped growing crops."],"a":1,"ex":"במקור: למרות שיורד מעט גשם, החקלאים מגדלים מגוון גידולים בזכות איסוף מים בסופות החורף. התשובה הנכונה: «Despite the scarce rainfall» ו-«thanks to». הראשונה אומרת שיש הרבה גשם, השלישית משנה את הכמות («only a few»), והרביעית אומרת שהפסיקו לגדל.","w":[["even though","אף על פי ש..."],["despite","למרות (+שם עצם)"],["thanks to","הודות ל..., בזכות"]]},{"q":"Most of the museum's funding comes from private donors, whereas the government covers only the cost of maintaining the historic building in which it is housed.","o":["The government provides most of the museum's funding, while private donors pay only for the maintenance of its historic building.","Private donors and the government share the museum's costs equally, including the cost of maintaining the historic building that houses it.","Because private donors refused to maintain the museum's historic building, the government agreed to cover most of the museum's other costs as well.","The government pays merely for the upkeep of the museum's historic building; the majority of the museum's money is provided by private donors."],"a":3,"ex":"במקור: רוב הכסף מתורמים פרטיים, והממשלה מממנת רק («only») את תחזוקת הבניין. התשובה הנכונה: «merely» במקום «only» ו-«the majority» במקום «most». הראשונה מחליפה בין התורמים לממשלה, השנייה אומרת שהם מתחלקים שווה, והשלישית ממציאה סיבה.","w":[["whereas","בעוד ש..., ואילו"],["merely","רק, לא יותר מ..."],["maintain","לתחזק"]]}]},"p1rs4":{"id":"p1rs4","tier":1,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"Few historians accepted the theory when it was first proposed, but new archaeological evidence has gradually persuaded many of them that it may be correct.","o":["Initially, only a small number of historians agreed with the theory; however, fresh archaeological findings have slowly convinced many that it could be right.","Most historians accepted the theory when it was first proposed, but new archaeological evidence has gradually persuaded them that it is wrong.","Because few historians accepted the theory at first, archaeologists searched for new evidence, which has proved beyond doubt that the theory is correct.","New archaeological evidence has persuaded a few historians to reject the theory, which most of them had found convincing when it was first proposed."],"a":0,"ex":"במקור: בהתחלה מעט («Few») היסטוריונים קיבלו את התאוריה, וראיות חדשות שכנעו רבים שאולי («may») היא נכונה. התשובה הנכונה שומרת על שני החלקים. השנייה הופכת את הכמות ואת הכיוון, השלישית מוסיפה סיבה ומשנה «may be correct» ל-«beyond doubt», והרביעית הופכת את כל הסיפור.","w":[["few","מעט (כמעט אין)"],["however","עם זאת, אולם"],["persuade","לשכנע"]]},{"q":"Children who are encouraged to explain their reasoning aloud while solving math problems tend to remember the methods better than those who work in silence.","o":["Children who work in silence while solving math problems tend to remember the methods better than children who are asked to explain their reasoning aloud.","Children remember math methods better because their teachers explain the reasoning aloud, whereas silent teachers make problems harder to solve.","Children urged to say out loud how they are thinking while doing math problems usually retain the methods better than children who work quietly.","All children who explain their reasoning aloud while solving math problems remember every method they learn, unlike those who work in silence."],"a":2,"ex":"במקור: ילדים שמסבירים בקול איך הם חושבים נוטים («tend to») לזכור טוב יותר. התשובה הנכונה: «say out loud», «usually retain». הראשונה הופכת את ההשוואה, השנייה מחליפה מי מסביר (המורים), והרביעית מגזימה («All», «every»).","w":[["tend to","נוטה ל..."],["reasoning","דרך חשיבה, נימוק"],["retain","לשמור, לזכור"]]},{"q":"The new law requires restaurants to display the calorie content of each dish on their menus, in the hope of encouraging customers to make healthier choices.","o":["The new law requires restaurants to offer healthier dishes on their menus, since customers have recently started to pay close attention to the calorie content of their food.","Restaurants must now list how many calories every dish contains on their menus, since lawmakers hope this will lead diners to choose healthier food.","Customers have asked restaurants to display the calorie content of each dish, hoping that the new law will make menus healthier.","The new law allows restaurants to display the calorie content of only some dishes, which has led customers to make healthier choices."],"a":1,"ex":"במקור: החוק מחייב («requires») להציג קלוריות של כל מנה, מתוך תקווה שהלקוחות יבחרו בריא יותר. התשובה הנכונה: «must now list». הראשונה משנה מה החוק מחייב, השלישית מחליפה מי ביקש, והרביעית משנה ל-«allows... only some» וטוענת שזה כבר קרה.","w":[["require","לחייב, לדרוש"],["in the hope of","מתוך תקווה ל..."],["content","תכולה, כמות (של חומר)"]]}]},"p1rs5":{"id":"p1rs5","tier":1,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"Although the novel received little attention when it was published, it is now regarded as a major work of its generation and is taught in many schools.","o":["Despite being mostly overlooked at first, the novel is now viewed as one of its generation's key books, and many schools include it in their teaching.","Because the novel received a great deal of attention when it was published, it is now taught in many schools as a major work of its generation.","The novel was considered a major work of its generation when it was published, but today it is rarely taught in schools and receives little attention.","Although the novel is taught in many schools, few critics regard it as an important work, since it was largely ignored when it first appeared."],"a":0,"ex":"במקור: בהתחלה כמעט לא שמו לב לרומן, והיום הוא נחשב ליצירה חשובה ונלמד בבתי ספר. התשובה הנכונה: «Despite being mostly overlooked». השנייה אומרת שקיבל הרבה תשומת לב, השלישית הופכת את הסדר בזמן, והרביעית אומרת שהמבקרים לא מעריכים אותו.","w":[["although","למרות ש... (+משפט)"],["despite","למרות (+שם עצם)"],["overlook","להתעלם, לא לשים לב"]]},{"q":"As the cost of solar panels has fallen sharply in recent years, a growing number of households have installed them on their roofs to reduce electricity bills.","o":["Although solar panels have become much cheaper lately, fewer families are putting them on their roofs, since electricity bills have also fallen.","As more households have installed solar panels on their roofs, electricity bills have risen sharply, since the panels are expensive to maintain.","The cost of solar panels has risen in recent years, so only a few households can still afford to install them on their roofs to cut their bills.","With solar panels becoming much cheaper lately, more and more families are putting them on their roofs in order to lower their electricity costs."],"a":3,"ex":"במקור: מחיר הפאנלים ירד בחדות, ובמקביל יותר ויותר משקי בית מתקינים אותם כדי לחסוך בחשמל. התשובה הנכונה אומרת את אותו דבר במילים אחרות: «With... much cheaper» ו-«in order to». הראשונה אומרת שפחות משפחות מתקינות, השנייה אומרת שהחשבונות עלו, והשלישית אומרת שהמחיר עלה.","w":[["as","מכיוון ש...; כפי ש...; בזמן ש..."],["in order to","כדי ל... (+פועל)"],["household","משק בית"]]},{"q":"Volunteers who cleaned the beach last weekend collected over two tons of plastic, much of which they believe was washed ashore by currents from distant countries.","o":["Volunteers who cleaned the beach last weekend found only a small amount of plastic, since currents from distant countries had washed most of it away.","Volunteers from distant countries collected more than two tons of plastic from the beach last weekend, most of which had been left there by local visitors.","More than two tons of plastic were gathered by last weekend's beach volunteers, who think a large part of it was brought by currents from faraway countries.","Last weekend's volunteers proved that all of the two tons of plastic they collected on the beach had come from local factories rather than from abroad."],"a":2,"ex":"במקור: המתנדבים אספו יותר משני טון פלסטיק, ולדעתם («they believe») חלק גדול הגיע עם זרמים מארצות רחוקות. התשובה הנכונה כתובה בסביל («were gathered by»). הראשונה משנה את הכמות, השנייה מחליפה מי הגיע מרחוק, והרביעית משנה «believe» ל-«proved» והופכת את המקור.","w":[["of which","ש...מהם / ממנו"],["current","זרם (בים)"],["distant","רחוק"]]}]},"p1rs6":{"id":"p1rs6","tier":1,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"Because the vaccine must be stored at extremely low temperatures, distributing it to remote villages without reliable electricity has proved far more difficult than expected.","o":["Getting the vaccine to distant villages that lack a dependable power supply has been much harder than anticipated, since it has to be kept very cold.","Although the vaccine must be kept extremely cold, distributing it to remote villages without reliable electricity has been easier than expected.","Remote villages without reliable electricity have been unable to store the vaccine at low temperatures, so health officials decided not to send it there at all.","Because distribution to remote villages proved difficult, the vaccine was changed so that it could be stored without any refrigeration."],"a":0,"ex":"במקור: החיסון צריך קירור חזק, ולכן קשה הרבה יותר מהצפוי להביא אותו לכפרים בלי חשמל אמין. התשובה הנכונה מעבירה את הסיבה לסוף עם «since». השנייה אומרת שהיה קל יותר, השלישית מוסיפה החלטה שלא נאמרה, והרביעית ממציאה שינוי בחיסון.","w":[["because","כי, מפני ש... (+משפט)"],["remote","מרוחק"],["reliable","אמין"]]},{"q":"The company's profits rose last year, not because it sold more products, but because it managed to reduce its production costs significantly.","o":["Last year the company's profits rose because it sold far more products than before, even though its production costs went up considerably.","Last year the company earned more money, owing to a considerable cut in what it spent on production rather than to any increase in sales.","Although the company reduced its production costs significantly last year, its profits fell, since it sold fewer products than in the previous year.","The company sold more products last year, and as a result it was able to reduce its production costs, which also helped its profits rise."],"a":1,"ex":"במקור: הרווחים עלו לא בגלל יותר מכירות, אלא בגלל קיצוץ בעלויות הייצור. התשובה הנכונה: «owing to a considerable cut... rather than». הראשונה הופכת את הסיבה, השלישית אומרת שהרווחים ירדו, והרביעית אומרת שהמכירות עלו וגרמו לקיצוץ.","w":[["owing to","בשל, עקב"],["rather than","במקום, ולא"],["significantly","באופן משמעותי"]]},{"q":"While some experts argue that working from home increases productivity, others claim that employees who never meet colleagues in person gradually lose their sense of belonging.","o":["Experts agree that working from home increases productivity and also helps employees who never meet their colleagues develop a sense of belonging.","Some experts argue that employees who work from home become less productive over time because they gradually lose their sense of belonging to the company.","Most experts claim that employees who meet their colleagues in person every day gradually lose both their productivity and their sense of belonging.","Some experts say remote work makes people more productive, but others maintain that staff who never see coworkers face to face slowly feel less connected."],"a":3,"ex":"כאן «While» = בעוד ש (ניגוד בין שתי דעות). במקור: יש מומחים שאומרים שעבודה מהבית מגבירה תפוקה, ואחרים טוענים שעובדים שלא פוגשים עמיתים מאבדים תחושת שייכות. השנייה מערבבת את שתי הדעות לסיבה אחת, הראשונה אומרת שכולם מסכימים, והשלישית מחליפה את מי שנפגע.","w":[["while","בעוד ש... (ניגוד)"],["productivity","תפוקה, פרודוקטיביות"],["sense of belonging","תחושת שייכות"]]}]},"p2sc1":{"id":"p2sc1","tier":2,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"The witness's account of the accident was so ___ with the footage from the security cameras that the police soon began to doubt her entire statement.","o":["compatible","inconsistent","equivalent","familiar"],"a":1,"ex":"«inconsistent with» = סותר, לא מתיישב עם. המשטרה התחילה לפקפק בעדות, ולכן העדות כנראה סתרה את הצילומים. «compatible» (תואם) היה אומר שהעדות מתאימה לראיות, ואז לא הייתה סיבה לפקפק בה.","w":[["inconsistent","לא עקבי, סותר"],["compatible","תואם, מתיישב עם"]]},{"q":"The health reform has been widely criticized as slow and costly; ___, it has achieved its main goal of shortening waiting times in public hospitals.","o":["even so","accordingly","likewise","namely"],"a":0,"ex":"«even so» = למרות זאת. קודם באה ביקורת (איטית ויקרה), ואחר כך הישג, כלומר ויתור. «accordingly» (בהתאם לכך) היה אומר שההישג נובע מהביקורת, וזה לא הגיוני.","w":[["even so","למרות זאת, ובכל זאת"],["accordingly","בהתאם לכך, לכן"]]},{"q":"Because the virus mutates so rapidly, a vaccine designed against this year's strain may be rendered ___ by next winter.","o":["contagious","indispensable","dormant","obsolete"],"a":3,"ex":"«obsolete» = מיושן, שכבר לא מועיל. הנגיף משתנה מהר, ולכן חיסון של השנה עלול להפוך ללא רלוונטי בחורף הבא. «indispensable» (הכרחי) אומר את ההפך הגמור.","w":[["obsolete","מיושן, שאבד עליו הכלח"],["indispensable","הכרחי, שאין לוותר עליו"],["mutate","לעבור מוטציה"]]},{"q":"___ the growing number of cyberattacks on hospitals, the ministry has ordered all medical centers to upgrade their computer security by the end of the year.","o":["Regardless of","In contrast to","In view of","Prior to"],"a":2,"ex":"«in view of» = לאור. ריבוי מתקפות הסייבר הוא הסיבה להוראה לשדרג את האבטחה. «regardless of» (בלי קשר ל...) היה אומר שההוראה לא קשורה למתקפות, וזה לא הגיוני.","w":[["in view of","לאור, בהתחשב ב..."],["regardless of","בלי קשר ל..., בלי להתחשב ב..."]]}]},"p2sc2":{"id":"p2sc2","tier":2,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"The restorers worked with ___ care, cleaning each square centimeter of the ancient fresco with tiny brushes over a period of four years.","o":["casual","superficial","meticulous","negligent"],"a":2,"ex":"«meticulous» = קפדני מאוד. ניקוי של כל סנטימטר במברשות זעירות במשך ארבע שנים מעיד על קפדנות. «superficial» (שטחי) ו-«negligent» (רשלני) אומרים את ההפך.","w":[["meticulous","קפדני, מדוקדק"],["superficial","שטחי"]]},{"q":"The study is especially valuable ___ it is the first to have followed the same group of patients for more than twenty years.","o":["lest","unless","even though","inasmuch as"],"a":3,"ex":"«inasmuch as» = מאחר ש... החלק השני (המחקר הראשון שעקב אחרי אותם מטופלים 20 שנה) הוא הסיבה לכך שהמחקר חשוב. «even though» (אף על פי ש) היה יוצר ניגוד, אבל להיות הראשון זה יתרון ולא חיסרון.","w":[["inasmuch as","מאחר ש..., במידה ש..."],["even though","אף על פי ש..."]]},{"q":"Despite the disappointing figures, the minister refused to ___ that the policy had failed, insisting instead that it simply needed more time.","o":["concede","conceal","forget","predict"],"a":0,"ex":"«concede» = להודות בדבר לא נעים. השר התעקש שהמדיניות רק צריכה עוד זמן, כלומר סירב להודות בכישלון. «conceal» (להסתיר) לא מתאים: «סירב להסתיר» היה אומר שהוא דיבר בגלוי על הכישלון.","w":[["concede","להודות (בדבר לא נעים), להכיר ב..."],["conceal","להסתיר"]]},{"q":"___ most of the members had already left for the holidays, the chairwoman decided to postpone the vote until January.","o":["Even if","Seeing that","As long as","Whereas"],"a":1,"ex":"«seeing that» = מאחר ש... רוב החברים כבר יצאו לחופשה, ולכן היו״ר דחתה את ההצבעה. «even if» (גם אם) ו-«as long as» (כל עוד) הן מילות תנאי, ואין כאן תנאי אלא סיבה.","w":[["seeing that","מאחר ש..., הואיל ו..."],["as long as","כל עוד, בתנאי ש..."]]}]},"p2sc3":{"id":"p2sc3","tier":2,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"Although the job offered little prestige, it proved highly ___, allowing her to pay off all of her student loans within two years.","o":["tedious","hazardous","obscure","lucrative"],"a":3,"ex":"«lucrative» = רווחי. «although» יוצר ניגוד: לעבודה לא הייתה יוקרה, אבל היא הכניסה הרבה כסף, ולכן היא סגרה את ההלוואות. «obscure» (לא מוכר) רק חוזר על חוסר היוקרה ואין בו ניגוד.","w":[["lucrative","רווחי, מכניס"],["prestige","יוקרה"],["tedious","מייגע"]]},{"q":"The newly opened archive contains dozens of letters that shed light on a ___ unknown period of the poet's life.","o":["subsequently","hitherto","simultaneously","henceforth"],"a":1,"ex":"«hitherto» = עד כה. התקופה הייתה לא ידועה עד עכשיו, והמכתבים שופכים עליה אור. «henceforth» (מעתה והלאה) לא מתאים: המכתבים דווקא חושפים את התקופה, כך שהיא לא תישאר לא ידועה.","w":[["hitherto","עד כה, עד עתה"],["henceforth","מעתה והלאה"],["shed light on","לשפוך אור על"]]},{"q":"Many voters remain ___ about the proposed merger: they welcome the promised savings but fear the loss of local jobs.","o":["indifferent","adamant","ambivalent","unanimous"],"a":2,"ex":"«ambivalent» = בעל רגשות מעורבים. אחרי הנקודתיים מוסבר שהבוחרים גם שמחים (חיסכון) וגם חוששים (אובדן משרות). «indifferent» (אדיש) לא מתאים, כי יש להם רגשות לשני הכיוונים.","w":[["ambivalent","בעל רגשות מעורבים, מתלבט"],["indifferent","אדיש"]]},{"q":"The landlord agreed to lower the rent ___ the tenants paid for the repairs to the roof themselves.","o":["on condition that","unless","in case","as though"],"a":0,"ex":"«on condition that» = בתנאי ש... בעל הבית הסכים להוריד את שכר הדירה רק אם הדיירים ישלמו בעצמם על תיקון הגג. «unless» (אלא אם כן) הופך את התנאי ויוצר משפט לא הגיוני.","w":[["on condition that","בתנאי ש..."],["unless","אלא אם כן"]]}]},"p2sc4":{"id":"p2sc4","tier":2,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"Critics warn that closing the rural clinics will only ___ the overcrowding in city hospitals, since patients from the villages will have nowhere else to go.","o":["exacerbate","alleviate","investigate","postpone"],"a":0,"ex":"«exacerbate» = להחמיר. אם המרפאות בכפרים ייסגרו, המטופלים יגיעו לבתי החולים בעיר והצפיפות תגדל. «alleviate» (להקל) אומר את ההפך.","w":[["exacerbate","להחמיר"],["alleviate","להקל, לשכך"]]},{"q":"___ the quick thinking of a passing nurse, the injured cyclist would almost certainly have died at the scene.","o":["Owing to","Apart from","But for","Along with"],"a":2,"ex":"«but for» = אלמלא. האחות הצילה את רוכב האופניים: בלעדיה הוא כנראה היה מת. «owing to» (בגלל) היה אומר שהמחשבה המהירה שלה הייתה גורמת למותו.","w":[["but for","אלמלא, לולא"],["owing to","בשל, עקב"]]},{"q":"The flood was ___: no one in the valley, not even the oldest residents, could remember the river ever rising so high.","o":["moderate","unprecedented","negligible","routine"],"a":1,"ex":"«unprecedented» = חסר תקדים. אחרי הנקודתיים מוסבר שאף אחד לא זוכר שהנהר עלה אי פעם כל כך גבוה. «routine» (שגרתי) ו-«negligible» (זניח) אומרים את ההפך.","w":[["unprecedented","חסר תקדים"],["negligible","זניח"]]},{"q":"The professor's lectures were notoriously ___, wandering from one topic to another without ever reaching a clear conclusion.","o":["concise","rigorous","focused","incoherent"],"a":3,"ex":"«incoherent» = בלי קשר הגיוני, מבולבל. ההרצאות קפצו מנושא לנושא ולא הגיעו למסקנה. «concise» (תמציתי) ו-«focused» (ממוקד) אומרים את ההפך.","w":[["incoherent","לא קוהרנטי, מבולבל"],["concise","תמציתי"],["notoriously","ידוע לשמצה"]]}]},"p2sc5":{"id":"p2sc5","tier":2,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"As young people moved to the cities in search of work, the village's population continued to ___, until only a few elderly residents remained.","o":["flourish","dwindle","fluctuate","stabilize"],"a":1,"ex":"«dwindle» = להתמעט בהדרגה. הצעירים עזבו עד שנשארו רק כמה זקנים, כלומר האוכלוסייה הלכה וקטנה. «flourish» (לשגשג) הפוך, ו-«fluctuate» (לעלות ולרדת) לא מתאים לירידה רצופה.","w":[["dwindle","להצטמצם, להתמעט"],["flourish","לשגשג"],["fluctuate","להשתנות, לעלות ולרדת"]]},{"q":"Several European countries, ___ Denmark and the Netherlands, now produce more than half of their electricity from wind.","o":["conversely","formerly","merely","notably"],"a":3,"ex":"«notably» = במיוחד, באופן בולט. דנמרק והולנד הן דוגמאות בולטות למדינות שמייצרות יותר מחצי מהחשמל מרוח. «merely» (רק) סותר את «Several», «formerly» (בעבר) לא מתאים ל-«now», ו-«conversely» (מנגד) מציג ניגוד שאין כאן.","w":[["notably","במיוחד; באופן בולט"],["merely","רק, לא יותר מ..."],["formerly","לשעבר, בעבר"]]},{"q":"The two sides have reached a ___ agreement, but it will not become final until both parliaments approve it.","o":["tentative","binding","permanent","definitive"],"a":0,"ex":"«tentative» = זמני, לא סופי. ההסכם לא יהיה סופי עד ששני הפרלמנטים יאשרו אותו. «binding» (מחייב) ו-«definitive» (סופי) סותרים את «it will not become final».","w":[["tentative","זמני, לא סופי"],["binding","מחייב"]]},{"q":"The bacteria can survive for weeks on dry surfaces; ___, hospital beds must be disinfected thoroughly between patients.","o":["conversely","otherwise","hence","nevertheless"],"a":2,"ex":"«hence» = ולכן. החיידקים שורדים שבועות על משטחים, וזו הסיבה שצריך לחטא את המיטות. «nevertheless» (למרות זאת) ו-«conversely» (מנגד) יוצרים ניגוד שלא קיים כאן.","w":[["hence","מכאן, ולכן"],["conversely","ובאופן הפוך, מנגד"]]}]},"p2sc6":{"id":"p2sc6","tier":2,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"In an unusually ___ interview, the director admitted that two of her films had been commercial failures and that she still regretted making them.","o":["evasive","guarded","candid","secretive"],"a":2,"ex":"«candid» = גלוי לב. הבמאית הודתה בכישלונות ובחרטה, וזה מראה כנות. «evasive» (מתחמק) ו-«guarded» (זהיר, מסתיר) אומרים את ההפך.","w":[["candid","גלוי לב, כן"],["evasive","מתחמק"]]},{"q":"The two companies decided to ___ their research departments, hoping that a single larger team would develop new products faster.","o":["merge","dismantle","divide","outsource"],"a":0,"ex":"«merge» = למזג, לאחד. החברות קיוו שצוות אחד גדול יעבוד מהר יותר, ולכן איחדו את מחלקות המחקר. «divide» (לחלק) ו-«dismantle» (לפרק) הפוכים לרעיון של צוות אחד גדול.","w":[["merge","למזג, להתמזג"],["dismantle","לפרק"]]},{"q":"Before the drug can be sold, every stage of the clinical trials will be ___ by an independent panel of experts to make sure that no data were hidden.","o":["fabricated","neglected","abandoned","scrutinized"],"a":3,"ex":"«scrutinize» = לבחון בקפדנות. הפאנל בודק כל שלב כדי לוודא שלא הוסתרו נתונים. «neglected» (הוזנח) סותר את המטרה, ו-«fabricated» (פוברק) לא הגיוני: מומחים בלתי תלויים לא אמורים לבדות ניסויים.","w":[["scrutinize","לבחון בקפדנות"],["fabricate","לפברק, לבדות"]]},{"q":"Residents received detailed instructions on what to do ___ an earthquake, including where to find the nearest shelter.","o":["instead of","in the event of","in spite of","in favor of"],"a":1,"ex":"«in the event of» = במקרה של. התושבים קיבלו הוראות מה לעשות אם תהיה רעידת אדמה, כולל איפה המקלט הקרוב. «in spite of» (למרות) ו-«instead of» (במקום) לא נותנים משמעות הגיונית כאן.","w":[["in the event of","במקרה של"],["in spite of","למרות (+שם עצם)"]]}]},"p2rs1":{"id":"p2rs1","tier":2,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"Although remote work has allowed many companies to cut their office expenses considerably, a number of managers report that it has made it harder to train newly hired employees.","o":["Because remote work has made it harder to train newly hired employees, many companies have been forced to spend considerably more on their offices than they did before.","Most managers report that remote work has reduced their companies' office expenses and that it has also made it easier to train employees who have just been hired.","Working from home has enabled numerous firms to reduce office costs significantly; some managers, however, say that it has complicated the training of new staff.","A number of managers report that remote work has allowed companies to cut office expenses only because they have stopped training newly hired employees altogether."],"a":2,"ex":"המקור: עבודה מרחוק חסכה לחברות הרבה בהוצאות משרד, אבל לפי חלק מהמנהלים היא הקשתה על הכשרת עובדים חדשים. התשובה הנכונה אומרת אותו דבר במילים אחרות («however» במקום «although»). אחת השגויות הופכת «harder» ל-«easier» ו-«a number of» ל-«most», ואחרות ממציאות קשר של סיבה ותוצאה שלא נאמר.","w":[["although","למרות ש... (+משפט)"],["however","עם זאת, אולם"],["considerably","במידה ניכרת"]]},{"q":"The drought, which lasted for nearly three years, did not so much destroy the region's agriculture as force farmers to switch to crops that require far less water.","o":["Rather than ruining the region's farming, the nearly three-year drought mainly pushed farmers to grow crops that need much less water.","The drought, which lasted almost three years, destroyed most of the region's agriculture, even though many farmers switched to crops that require far less water.","Farmers in the region switched to crops that need much less water several years before the drought began, and as a result their agriculture was hardly damaged.","The nearly three-year drought both destroyed the region's agriculture and forced farmers to grow crops that require much less water than they had grown before."],"a":0,"ex":"«did not so much X as Y» = לא עד כדי כך X, אלא בעיקר Y. הבצורת לא הרסה את החקלאות, אלא בעיקר אילצה את החקלאים לעבור לגידולים שצריכים פחות מים. התשובה עם «both destroyed... and forced» שגויה, כי המקור דוחה את ההרס. גם התשובה שהבצורת הרסה את רוב החקלאות סותרת את המקור.","w":[["not so much... as","לא כל כך... אלא בעיקר"],["rather than","במקום, ולא"],["nearly","כמעט"]]},{"q":"People who regularly play a musical instrument tend to score higher on memory tests in old age, though it is unclear whether music training or other lifestyle factors account for the difference.","o":["Playing a musical instrument regularly improves memory in old age, which explains why older musicians score higher on memory tests than people with other lifestyles.","Older people who score higher on memory tests tend to take up a musical instrument, although researchers are unsure which lifestyle factors encourage them to do so.","It is unclear whether people who regularly play a musical instrument score any higher on memory tests in old age than those who have never played one at all.","Why older adults who often play an instrument usually do better on memory tests is unclear: it may be the music or another part of their lifestyle."],"a":3,"ex":"המקור מתאר רק קשר (מתאם): מי שמנגן נוטה לקבל ציונים גבוהים יותר במבחני זיכרון בזקנה, ולא ידוע אם הסיבה היא הנגינה או גורמים אחרים. התשובה הנכונה מתחילה מהשאלה הפתוחה («Why... is unclear») ושומרת גם את הקשר («usually do better») וגם את הספק לגבי הסיבה. התשובה עם «improves memory» הופכת את המתאם לסיבה, וזו המלכודת. התשובה שאומרת שלא ידוע אם בכלל יש הבדל משנה את מה שלא ידוע.","w":[["tend to","נוטה ל..."],["though","אף על פי ש...; (בסוף משפט) אבל"],["account for","להסביר, להיות הסיבה ל..."]]}]},"p2rs2":{"id":"p2rs2","tier":2,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"Only after the company had received hundreds of complaints from customers did it admit that the software update was responsible for the battery problems affecting its newest phones.","o":["The company admitted that the software update was responsible for the battery problems in its newest phones before any of its customers had complained about them.","The company acknowledged that its software update had caused the battery faults in its latest phones, but not until hundreds of customers had complained.","Hundreds of customers complained that the company's software update was responsible for the battery problems, but the company has refused to admit that this is the case.","After receiving hundreds of complaints, the company admitted that its newest phones had battery problems, though it denied that the software update was in any way responsible."],"a":1,"ex":"«Only after X did Y» = רק אחרי X קרה Y. החברה הודתה שהעדכון גרם לבעיות הסוללה רק אחרי מאות תלונות, ו-«not until» בתשובה הנכונה אומר בדיוק את זה. אחת השגויות אומרת שהחברה הודתה לפני התלונות, ואחרות אומרות שהחברה סירבה להודות או הכחישה שהעדכון אשם.","w":[["only after","רק אחרי"],["not until","רק כאשר, לא לפני ש..."],["acknowledge","להודות, להכיר ב..."]]},{"q":"While the new metro line has shortened travel times for commuters from the eastern suburbs, residents of the city center complain that construction noise will continue for at least two more years.","o":["Because construction noise in the city center will continue for at least two more years, commuters from the eastern suburbs complain that the new metro line has not shortened their journeys.","Commuters from the eastern suburbs now travel faster thanks to the new metro line, whereas downtown residents object that the building noise will go on for at least another two years.","The new metro line has shortened travel times for residents of the city center, while commuters from the eastern suburbs complain about construction noise that will last at most two more years.","Although residents of the city center complain about the noise, construction of the new metro line will be finished within two years, which will shorten travel times for eastern commuters."],"a":1,"ex":"«While» כאן = בעוד ש (ניגוד): לנוסעים מהפרברים המזרחיים הנסיעה התקצרה, ואילו תושבי מרכז העיר מתלוננים שהרעש יימשך לפחות עוד שנתיים. אחת השגויות מחליפה בין שתי הקבוצות והופכת «at least» ל-«at most». אחרת מוסיפה שהבנייה תסתיים תוך שנתיים, בניגוד למקור.","w":[["while","בעוד ש... (ניגוד)"],["whereas","בעוד ש..., ואילו"],["at least","לפחות"]]},{"q":"Contrary to the widely held belief that bats are blind, most species can see quite well, and some even rely more on their eyesight than on echolocation when hunting.","o":["As is widely believed, most species of bats are blind, so they rely on echolocation rather than on their eyesight when hunting, although a few species can see quite well.","Most species of bats can see quite well; consequently, they no longer need echolocation when they hunt, contrary to what is widely believed about how they find their prey.","Some species of bats can see quite well, but most of them rely more on echolocation than on their eyesight when hunting, as is widely believed by many people today.","Although many people assume that bats cannot see, the majority of species actually have good vision, and certain species depend on sight more than on echolocation to catch prey."],"a":3,"ex":"«Contrary to» = בניגוד ל... למרות האמונה שעטלפים עיוורים, רוב המינים רואים היטב, ויש מינים שאפילו סומכים על הראייה יותר מאשר על ההד. התשובה שמחליפה בין «most» ל-«some» שגויה. התשובה עם «consequently» מוסיפה שהם כבר לא צריכים הד, וזה לא נאמר.","w":[["contrary to","בניגוד ל..."],["even","אפילו"],["rely on","לסמוך על, להסתמך על"]]}]},"p2rs3":{"id":"p2rs3","tier":2,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"The festival's organizers insist that ticket prices were raised solely to cover the rising cost of security, not to increase profits, as some critics have suggested.","o":["The festival's organizers maintain that the higher ticket prices are meant only to pay for growing security costs and not, as some critics claim, to boost profits.","Some critics have suggested that ticket prices were raised solely to cover the rising cost of security, but the festival's organizers insist that the goal was to increase profits.","The festival's organizers admit that ticket prices were raised partly to increase profits, although they insist that the rising cost of security was the main reason for the change.","Because some critics suggested that the festival was making too much profit, its organizers decided to raise ticket prices in order to cover the rising cost of security instead."],"a":0,"ex":"המארגנים טוענים שהמחירים עלו אך ורק («solely») כדי לממן את האבטחה, ולא כדי להגדיל רווחים כפי שטוענים מבקרים. אחת השגויות מחליפה מי אומר מה. אחרת הופכת «solely» ל-«partly». השלישית מוסיפה קשר של סיבה ותוצאה שלא קיים במקור.","w":[["solely","אך ורק, בלעדית"],["insist","להתעקש, לטעון בתוקף"],["suggest","לרמוז, להציע"]]},{"q":"Had the engineers not detected the crack in the dam during a routine inspection, the reservoir might have flooded several villages downstream within a matter of days.","o":["Although the engineers detected the crack in the dam during a routine inspection, the reservoir still flooded several villages downstream within a matter of days.","The engineers detected the crack in the dam only after the reservoir had flooded several villages downstream, even though they had carried out a routine inspection earlier.","But for the discovery of the crack in the dam by engineers carrying out a regular inspection, a number of villages downstream could have been flooded within days.","If the engineers detect a crack in the dam during their next routine inspection, they may decide to flood several villages downstream in order to protect the reservoir."],"a":2,"ex":"«Had the engineers not detected» = אילו המהנדסים לא היו מגלים. כלומר הם גילו את הסדק, והשיטפון לא קרה. «but for» = אלמלא, ולכן התשובה הנכונה שומרת על המשמעות. התשובה עם «although» אומרת שהשיטפון באמת קרה, וזה ההפך מהמקור.","w":[["but for","אלמלא, לולא"],["detect","לגלות, לזהות"],["routine","שגרתי"]]},{"q":"Few historians today accept the traditional account of the city's founding, which is based almost entirely on a single chronicle written more than three centuries after the events it describes.","o":["Most historians today accept the traditional account of the city's founding, even though it is based on a single chronicle written more than three centuries after the events.","Few historians today accept the traditional account of the city's founding, because the only chronicle that describes those events was lost more than three centuries ago.","Historians who accept the traditional account of the city's founding rely on several chronicles, all of which were written within a few years of the events they describe.","The conventional story of how the city was founded, which relies nearly exclusively on one chronicle composed over three hundred years later, is now rejected by most historians."],"a":3,"ex":"«Few historians accept» = מעט היסטוריונים מקבלים, כלומר רובם דוחים את הסיפור המסורתי. התשובה הנכונה אומרת שרוב ההיסטוריונים דוחים אותו, ושהוא מבוסס כמעט רק על כרוניקה אחת שנכתבה מאות שנים אחר כך. התשובה עם «Most historians today accept» הופכת את «few» ל-«most».","w":[["few","מעט (כמעט אין)"],["almost","כמעט"],["chronicle","כרוניקה, דברי הימים"]]}]},"p2rs4":{"id":"p2rs4","tier":2,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"The proposal to extend the school day was dropped not because parents opposed it, but because the ministry could not find enough qualified teachers to staff the additional hours.","o":["Parents opposed the proposal to extend the school day because they believed that the ministry would not be able to find enough qualified teachers for the additional hours.","The ministry dropped the proposal to extend the school day after parents objected to it, even though it had already found enough qualified teachers to staff the extra hours.","It was a shortage of qualified teachers for the extra hours, rather than objections from parents, that caused the plan for a longer school day to be abandoned.","Although the ministry found enough qualified teachers to staff the additional hours, the proposal to extend the school day was dropped because many parents strongly opposed it."],"a":2,"ex":"המקור: ההצעה בוטלה לא בגלל התנגדות ההורים, אלא בגלל שלא היו מספיק מורים. התשובה הנכונה משתמשת ב-«rather than» ובמבנה «It was... that» כדי להדגיש את הסיבה האמיתית. שתי שגויות הופכות את התנגדות ההורים לסיבה, וזה בדיוק מה שהמקור שולל.","w":[["rather than","במקום, ולא"],["qualified","מוסמך, בעל הכשרה"],["staff","לאייש (בכוח אדם)"]]},{"q":"Unlike most migratory birds, which travel in large flocks, young cuckoos make their first journey to Africa alone, guided only by an inherited sense of direction.","o":["Like most migratory birds, young cuckoos travel to Africa in large flocks on their first journey, guided by older birds that have already made the trip many times before.","Whereas the majority of migrating birds fly in big groups, young cuckoos fly to Africa for the first time on their own, relying solely on an instinctive sense of direction.","Young cuckoos make their first journey to Africa alone because, unlike most migratory birds, they have not inherited any sense of direction that would allow them to join a flock.","Most migratory birds travel alone and are guided only by an inherited sense of direction, whereas young cuckoos make their first journey to Africa in large flocks with other birds."],"a":1,"ex":"«Unlike» = בניגוד ל... רוב הציפורים הנודדות טסות בלהקות, אבל קוקיות צעירות טסות לבד בפעם הראשונה ומונחות רק על ידי חוש כיוון מולד. «whereas» בתשובה הנכונה שומר על הניגוד. אחת השגויות הופכת את הצדדים, ואחרת מוסיפה סיבה («because») שסותרת את המקור.","w":[["unlike","בניגוד ל... (+שם עצם)"],["whereas","בעוד ש..., ואילו"],["inherited","תורשתי, מולד"]]},{"q":"The study found that employees who were allowed to choose their own working hours took fewer sick days, although their overall productivity remained roughly the same as before.","o":["According to the study, workers permitted to set their own schedules were absent due to illness less often, but their total output stayed about the same.","The study found that employees who were allowed to choose their own working hours became much more productive, although they took roughly the same number of sick days as before.","Employees who took fewer sick days were then allowed to choose their own working hours, and as a result their overall productivity rose considerably, according to the study.","Although employees who chose their own working hours took fewer sick days, the study found that their productivity fell, since they worked fewer hours than they had before."],"a":0,"ex":"המחקר מצא שעובדים שבחרו את שעות העבודה שלהם לקחו פחות ימי מחלה, אבל התפוקה שלהם נשארה בערך אותו דבר. אחת השגויות מחליפה בין שני הממצאים. אחרת הופכת את הסדר (קודם פחות ימי מחלה ואז בחירת שעות) ומוסיפה עלייה בתפוקה. האחרונה אומרת שהתפוקה ירדה.","w":[["although","למרות ש... (+משפט)"],["productivity","תפוקה, פריון"],["roughly","בערך, בקירוב"]]}]},"p2rs5":{"id":"p2rs5","tier":2,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"So rapidly did the fire spread through the dry forest that firefighters were unable to save the old wooden cabins, despite having arrived within minutes of the first alarm.","o":["Because the firefighters arrived late, long after the first alarm, the fire was able to spread rapidly through the dry forest and destroy the old wooden cabins.","The fire spread so rapidly through the dry forest that firefighters arrived within minutes of the first alarm and still managed to save most of the old wooden cabins in the area.","Although the fire spread rapidly through the dry forest, the firefighters, who arrived within minutes of the first alarm, were able to save all of the old wooden cabins.","Even though firefighters reached the scene just minutes after the first alarm, the blaze moved through the parched forest so fast that they could not rescue the old wooden cabins."],"a":3,"ex":"«So rapidly... that» = כל כך מהר ש... האש התפשטה כל כך מהר שהכבאים לא הצליחו להציל את הבקתות, למרות שהגיעו תוך דקות. «despite having arrived» הופך בתשובה הנכונה ל-«even though... reached». אחת השגויות אומרת שהכבאים איחרו, וזה סותר את «within minutes». שתיים אחרות אומרות שהבקתות ניצלו.","w":[["so... that","כל כך... ש..."],["despite","למרות (+שם עצם)"],["even though","אף על פי ש..."]]},{"q":"Opponents of the new law claim that it will not protect consumers at all; on the contrary, it will allow large banks to charge hidden fees on ordinary savings accounts.","o":["Opponents of the new law claim that it will protect consumers by preventing large banks from charging hidden fees on ordinary savings accounts, contrary to what its supporters say.","According to its opponents, rather than safeguarding consumers, the new law will enable big banks to impose concealed charges on regular savings accounts.","Opponents of the new law admit that it will protect consumers to some extent, although they fear that large banks may still find ways to charge hidden fees on savings accounts.","Opponents of the new law claim that it will protect only the large banks, which will no longer be allowed to charge hidden fees on ordinary savings accounts."],"a":1,"ex":"המתנגדים טוענים שהחוק לא יגן על הצרכנים, ולהפך («on the contrary»): הוא יאפשר לבנקים לגבות עמלות נסתרות. «rather than safeguarding» = במקום להגן. אחת השגויות אומרת שהחוק ימנע עמלות, וזה ההפך. אחרת אומרת שהמתנגדים מודים שהחוק יגן קצת, בניגוד ל-«not... at all».","w":[["on the contrary","להפך (דוחה את מה שנאמר)"],["rather than","במקום, ולא"],["hidden","נסתר, חבוי"]]},{"q":"The stone terraces on the island's hillsides, many of which are still farmed today, were built by local villagers rather than by a central authority, as scholars once assumed.","o":["As scholars once assumed, the stone terraces on the island's hillsides were built by local villagers, although most of them are no longer farmed today because the villagers have left.","The stone terraces on the island's hillsides were built by a central authority rather than by local villagers, and scholars now believe that only a few of them are still farmed.","Scholars used to believe that a central authority had constructed the island's hillside stone terraces, a large number of which are still cultivated, but in fact local villagers built them.","Scholars once assumed that local villagers had built the stone terraces on the island's hillsides, but it has since been shown that they were planned by a central authority."],"a":2,"ex":"המקור: את הטרסות בנו תושבי הכפרים, ולא שלטון מרכזי כפי שחשבו פעם החוקרים. «as scholars once assumed» מתייחס לשלטון המרכזי. התשובה הנכונה אומרת שהחוקרים חשבו שבנה אותן שלטון מרכזי, אבל בפועל בנו אותן הכפריים. התשובה שמתחילה ב-«As scholars once assumed» מצמידה את ההנחה לחלק הלא נכון.","w":[["rather than","במקום, ולא"],["assume","להניח"],["in fact","למעשה, בעצם"]]}]},"p2rs6":{"id":"p2rs6","tier":2,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"Even when they are offered a larger reward later, young children usually choose a small reward immediately, a tendency that becomes less pronounced as they grow older.","o":["Young children generally prefer to get a small prize at once rather than wait for a bigger one, although this preference weakens with age.","As they grow older, children increasingly choose a small reward immediately, even when they are offered a larger reward if they are willing to wait for it.","Young children usually wait for a larger reward rather than choosing a small one immediately, and this tendency becomes even stronger as they grow older.","Because young children are rarely offered a larger reward later, they usually choose a small reward immediately, a habit they lose only when they are much older."],"a":0,"ex":"ילדים צעירים בדרך כלל בוחרים פרס קטן מיד, גם כשמציעים להם פרס גדול יותר אחר כך, והנטייה הזו נחלשת («becomes less pronounced») כשהם גדלים. אחת השגויות אומרת שהנטייה מתחזקת עם הגיל, ואחרת הופכת את הבחירה עצמה (הילדים מחכים). האחרונה מוסיפה סיבה שלא נאמרה.","w":[["tendency","נטייה"],["pronounced","בולט, מובהק"],["rather than","במקום, ולא"]]},{"q":"The museum will extend its opening hours on weekends only if the city agrees to cover the cost of the additional security guards that the longer schedule would require.","o":["The museum will extend its opening hours on weekends even if the city refuses to pay for the additional security guards that the longer schedule would require.","The city has agreed to cover the cost of additional security guards, so the museum will extend its opening hours on weekends as soon as the new guards are hired.","Unless the city consents to pay for the extra guards needed for a longer schedule, the museum will not stay open later on weekends.","If the museum extends its opening hours on weekends, the city will have to hire additional security guards, since the longer schedule would require more staff at night."],"a":2,"ex":"«only if» = רק אם. המוזיאון יאריך את השעות רק אם העירייה תממן את המאבטחים. «Unless... not» = אם לא... אז לא, וזו אותה משמעות. התשובה עם «even if» אומרת את ההפך: השעות יוארכו גם בלי מימון. אחרת מוסיפה שהעירייה כבר הסכימה, וזה לא נאמר.","w":[["only if","רק אם"],["unless","אלא אם כן"],["even if","גם אם, אפילו אם"]]},{"q":"The company's profits rose sharply last year, but this was largely due to the sale of one of its factories rather than to any improvement in the performance of its core business.","o":["The company's profits rose sharply last year because the performance of its core business improved so much that it was able to sell one of its factories.","Last year's steep increase in the company's earnings came mainly from selling a factory, not from better results in its main line of business.","Although the company sold one of its factories last year, its profits fell sharply, since its core business performed considerably worse than in previous years.","The company's profits rose sharply last year, partly because of the sale of a factory and partly because its core business performed much better than expected."],"a":1,"ex":"הרווחים עלו, אבל בעיקר («largely») בגלל מכירת מפעל, ולא בגלל שיפור בעסק המרכזי. התשובה עם «partly... partly» מוסיפה שיפור בעסק המרכזי, וזה בדיוק מה שהמקור שולל. אחרת אומרת שהרווחים ירדו.","w":[["due to","עקב, בגלל (+שם עצם)"],["rather than","במקום, ולא"],["core","מרכזי, עיקרי"]]}]},"p3sc1":{"id":"p3sc1","tier":3,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"The negotiator's tone was so ___ that even her opponents, who had expected a fierce confrontation, found themselves agreeing to most of her terms.","o":["belligerent","conciliatory","incoherent","pompous"],"a":1,"ex":"«Conciliatory» = מפייס, שנועד ליישב מחלוקת. היריבים ציפו לעימות ובכל זאת הסכימו לרוב התנאים, ולכן הטון היה מפייס. «belligerent» (תוקפני) הוא בדיוק מה שהם ציפו לו, והוא היה מוביל לעימות ולא להסכמה.","w":[["conciliatory","מפייס, מרצה"],["belligerent","תוקפני, לוחמני"],["confrontation","עימות"]]},{"q":"The drug proved highly effective in mice; ___, researchers caution that many compounds that cure diseases in mice turn out to be useless in people.","o":["accordingly","likewise","in other words","even so"],"a":3,"ex":"«Even so» = למרות זאת. החלק הראשון חיובי (התרופה עבדה בעכברים) והשני מסייג (החוקרים מזהירים), ולכן צריך מילת ויתור. «accordingly» (בהתאם לכך) היה הופך את האזהרה לתוצאה של ההצלחה, וזה לא הגיוני.","w":[["even so","למרות זאת, ובכל זאת"],["accordingly","בהתאם לכך, לכן"],["caution","להזהיר"]]},{"q":"Having spent most of his career at remote research stations, the geologist was notoriously ___, rarely speaking at meetings and avoiding conferences whenever he could.","o":["reticent","gregarious","meticulous","ostentatious"],"a":0,"ex":"«Reticent» = שתקן, מאופק, לא נוטה לדבר. הוא כמעט לא דיבר בישיבות ונמנע מכנסים. «gregarious» (חברותי) הוא ההפך הגמור, ו-«ostentatious» (ראוותני) לא מתאים למי שמתחמק מקהל.","w":[["reticent","שתקן, מאופק"],["gregarious","חברותי"],["notoriously","באופן ידוע (לרוב לשלילה)"]]},{"q":"Many of the families who once lived in the old city center have moved to the suburbs ___ the steep rise in rents over the past decade.","o":["regardless of","in spite of","on account of","in favor of"],"a":2,"ex":"«On account of» = בגלל. עליית שכר הדירה היא הסיבה שמשפחות עברו לפרברים. «in spite of» (למרות) היה אומר שהן עברו למרות העלייה, וזה הפוך מההיגיון.","w":[["on account of","בגלל, בשל"],["in spite of","למרות"],["regardless of","בלי קשר ל..."]]}]},"p3sc2":{"id":"p3sc2","tier":3,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"The ruling party's majority, once thought unassailable, has been steadily ___ by a series of defections, and the government now survives only with the support of two independent members.","o":["consolidated","vindicated","eroded","replenished"],"a":2,"ex":"«Erode» = לשחוק, לכרסם בהדרגה. שורת עריקות הקטינה את הרוב, ועכשיו הממשלה תלויה בשני חברים עצמאיים. «consolidate» (לבסס, לחזק) הוא ההפך: עריקות לא מחזקות רוב.","w":[["erode","לשחוק, לכרסם"],["consolidate","לבסס, לחזק"],["unassailable","בלתי ניתן לערעור"]]},{"q":"The new law requires restaurants to display the calorie content of every dish, ___ encouraging diners to make healthier choices without banning any food outright.","o":["conversely","thereby","meanwhile","nonetheless"],"a":1,"ex":"«Thereby» = ובכך, על ידי כך. הצגת הקלוריות היא האמצעי, ועידוד בחירות בריאות הוא התוצאה שלו. «conversely» (מנגד) ו-«nonetheless» (בכל זאת) מציגים ניגוד, אבל אין כאן ניגוד.","w":[["thereby","ובכך, על ידי כך"],["conversely","ובאופן הפוך, מנגד"],["outright","לגמרי, באופן מוחלט"]]},{"q":"Investors grew ___ of the start-up after it twice failed to publish its annual accounts on time, and several of them withdrew their funding.","o":["wary","enamored","oblivious","envious"],"a":0,"ex":"«Wary of» = חושד ב..., נזהר מ... החברה לא פרסמה דוחות בזמן ומשקיעים משכו את הכסף, כלומר הם נעשו חשדנים. «enamored of» (מאוהב ב...) סותר את משיכת הכסף.","w":[["wary","זהיר, חשדן"],["enamored","מאוהב, מוקסם"],["oblivious","לא מודע, לא שם לב"]]},{"q":"The open-air festival will go ahead as planned ___ the weather forecast, since all of the performances have been moved under large waterproof tents.","o":["on account of","thanks to","by virtue of","regardless of"],"a":3,"ex":"«Regardless of» = בלי קשר ל... כל ההופעות הועברו לאוהלים, ולכן התחזית לא משנה. «on account of» ו-«thanks to» היו אומרים שהתחזית היא הסיבה שהפסטיבל מתקיים, וזה לא הגיוני.","w":[["regardless of","בלי קשר ל..."],["on account of","בגלל, בשל"],["thanks to","הודות ל..., בזכות"]]}]},"p3sc3":{"id":"p3sc3","tier":3,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"What began as a ___ disagreement over the wording of a single clause eventually escalated into a dispute that delayed the signing of the treaty by two years.","o":["momentous","trifling","unanimous","lucrative"],"a":1,"ex":"«Trifling» = פעוט, חסר חשיבות. המבנה «began as... eventually escalated» מראה שהמחלוקת התחילה קטנה ורק אחר כך גדלה. «momentous» (גורלי, רב חשיבות) הורס את הניגוד בין ההתחלה הקטנה להסלמה.","w":[["trifling","פעוט, שולי"],["momentous","גורלי, רב חשיבות"],["escalate","להסלים"]]},{"q":"The tribe's oral traditions, ___ dismissed by scholars as mere legend, turned out to describe a real volcanic eruption that geologists have since dated to around 600 BCE.","o":["henceforth","thereafter","hitherto","simultaneously"],"a":2,"ex":"«Hitherto» = עד כה, עד אז. החוקרים זלזלו במסורות עד שהתברר שהן מתארות התפרצות אמיתית. «henceforth» (מעתה והלאה) מדבר על העתיד, ולא מתאים לזלזול שהיה לפני הגילוי.","w":[["hitherto","עד כה, עד עתה"],["henceforth","מעתה והלאה"],["dismiss","לבטל, לדחות כלא חשוב"]]},{"q":"The professor was known for her ___ grading: she deducted points for every misplaced comma and accepted no excuses for late submissions.","o":["lenient","cursory","sporadic","exacting"],"a":3,"ex":"«Exacting» = תובעני, קפדני מאוד. היא הורידה נקודות על כל פסיק ולא קיבלה תירוצים. «lenient» (מקל, סלחני) הוא ההפך, ו-«cursory» (שטחי, חפוז) לא מתאים לבדיקה של כל פסיק.","w":[["exacting","תובעני, קפדני"],["lenient","מקל, סלחני"],["cursory","שטחי, חפוז"]]},{"q":"The settlers could survive the winter ___ the supply ship reached them before the river froze; if it was delayed, they would have no choice but to abandon the colony.","o":["only if","even if","unless","whether"],"a":0,"ex":"«Only if» = רק אם. החלק השני אומר שאם הספינה תתעכב הם ייאלצו לעזוב, כלומר ההישרדות תלויה בהגעת הספינה. «even if» (גם אם) ו-«unless» (אלא אם כן) אומרים את ההפך.","w":[["only if","רק אם"],["even if","גם אם, אפילו אם"],["unless","אלא אם כן"]]}]},"p3sc4":{"id":"p3sc4","tier":3,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"The candidate's speeches were full of ___ promises, such as 'a brighter future for every family', that sounded inspiring but committed her to nothing in particular.","o":["binding","verifiable","candid","nebulous"],"a":3,"ex":"«Nebulous» = מעורפל, לא מוגדר. הבטחה כמו «עתיד טוב יותר» נשמעת יפה אבל לא מחייבת לשום דבר מסוים. «binding» (מחייב) ו-«verifiable» (שאפשר לבדוק) סותרים את «committed her to nothing».","w":[["nebulous","מעורפל, לא ברור"],["binding","מחייב"],["verifiable","שניתן לאמת"]]},{"q":"Birdwatching, once regarded as a pursuit so ___ that only a handful of enthusiasts took part in it, now attracts millions of participants every year.","o":["esoteric","ubiquitous","lucrative","rewarding"],"a":0,"ex":"«Esoteric» = מוכר רק לחוג מצומצם. «only a handful of enthusiasts» מתאר תחביב של מעטים, בניגוד למיליונים של היום. «ubiquitous» (נפוץ בכל מקום) הוא ההפך.","w":[["esoteric","מוכר רק למעטים, אזוטרי"],["ubiquitous","נפוץ בכל מקום"],["pursuit","עיסוק, תחביב"]]},{"q":"Although the fire gutted most of the building, the medieval manuscripts stored in the basement vault were, remarkably, left ___.","o":["charred","unscathed","illegible","dispersed"],"a":1,"ex":"«Unscathed» = לא נפגע כלל. «Although» ו-«remarkably» מראים ניגוד: הבניין נשרף, אבל כתבי היד שרדו. «charred» (חרוך) הוא מה שהיה צפוי, ואז אין שום ניגוד ושום דבר מפתיע.","w":[["unscathed","ללא פגע"],["charred","חרוך"],["gut","להחריב מבפנים (בשריפה)"]]},{"q":"The new rail line is, ___, more expensive to use than the bus; it does, however, cut the journey time between the two cities by half.","o":["consequently","likewise","admittedly","namely"],"a":2,"ex":"«Admittedly» = יש להודות ש... הכותב מודה בחיסרון (יקר יותר) ואז מציג יתרון עם «however». «consequently» (כתוצאה מכך) לא מתאים, כי אין כאן סיבה ותוצאה.","w":[["admittedly","יש להודות ש..."],["consequently","כתוצאה מכך, לפיכך"],["namely","כלומר, דהיינו"]]}]},"p3sc5":{"id":"p3sc5","tier":3,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"Both sides remained ___ throughout the talks, refusing to make even the smallest concession, and so the strike dragged on for five months.","o":["intransigent","amenable","apathetic","jubilant"],"a":0,"ex":"«Intransigent» = עקשן, שלא מוכן להתפשר. הצדדים סירבו לכל ויתור והשביתה נמשכה. «amenable» (פתוח, נכון להסכים) הוא ההפך.","w":[["intransigent","עקשן, לא מתפשר"],["amenable","נענה, פתוח לשכנוע"],["concession","ויתור"]]},{"q":"___ a last-minute donation from an anonymous benefactor, the theater would have been forced to close its doors last spring.","o":["As for","Apart from","In spite of","But for"],"a":3,"ex":"«But for» = אלמלא. בלי התרומה התיאטרון היה נסגר («would have been forced to close»), כלומר התרומה הצילה אותו. «in spite of» (למרות) לא מתאים, כי התרומה עזרה ולא הפריעה.","w":[["but for","אלמלא, לולא"],["in spite of","למרות"],["benefactor","תורם, נדבן"]]},{"q":"The company's accounts were deliberately ___, making it almost impossible for auditors to trace where the money had gone.","o":["transparent","succinct","opaque","lavish"],"a":2,"ex":"«Opaque» = אטום, לא שקוף, קשה להבנה. הדוחות נבנו בכוונה כך שאי אפשר לעקוב אחרי הכסף. «transparent» (שקוף) הוא ההפך, והוא היה מקל על המבקרים.","w":[["opaque","אטום, לא שקוף"],["transparent","שקוף"],["trace","להתחקות, לעקוב"]]},{"q":"Two years of drought have so severely ___ the region's reservoirs that several towns now receive tap water for only a few hours a day.","o":["replenished","depleted","augmented","subsidized"],"a":1,"ex":"«Deplete» = לרוקן, לדלדל. הבצורת הורידה את מאגרי המים, ולכן יש מים רק כמה שעות ביום. «replenish» (למלא מחדש) ו-«augment» (להגדיל) הם ההפך.","w":[["deplete","לרוקן, לדלדל"],["replenish","למלא מחדש"],["augment","להגדיל, להוסיף"]]}]},"p3sc6":{"id":"p3sc6","tier":3,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"The excavation team was ___ in its record-keeping: every shard, however tiny, was photographed, measured and numbered before it was lifted from the trench.","o":["haphazard","perfunctory","reluctant","painstaking"],"a":3,"ex":"«Painstaking» = קפדני, יסודי מאוד. כל רסיס, קטן ככל שיהיה, צולם, נמדד ומוספר. «haphazard» (אקראי, לא מסודר) ו-«perfunctory» (לצאת ידי חובה) הם ההפך.","w":[["painstaking","קפדני, יסודי"],["haphazard","אקראי, לא מסודר"],["perfunctory","שטחי, לצאת ידי חובה"]]},{"q":"The virus is transmitted solely through direct contact with infected blood; ___ the risk of catching it on a crowded bus is virtually nil.","o":["it follows that","even so","conversely","admittedly"],"a":0,"ex":"«It follows that» = מכאן נובע ש... אם הנגיף עובר רק במגע עם דם, המסקנה היא שהסיכון באוטובוס כמעט אפסי. «even so» (למרות זאת) היה מציג ניגוד, אבל החלק השני הוא מסקנה ישירה מהראשון.","w":[["it follows that","מכאן נובע ש..."],["solely","אך ורק, בלעדית"],["virtually","כמעט לגמרי"]]},{"q":"Rather than accept responsibility for the budget crisis, the mayor tried to ___ the blame onto her predecessor.","o":["incur","shoulder","deflect","acknowledge"],"a":2,"ex":"«Deflect» = להסיט, להפנות הלאה. במקום לקבל אחריות היא ניסתה להעביר את האשמה למי שכיהן לפניה. «shoulder» (לשאת באחריות) ו-«acknowledge» (להודות) הם בדיוק קבלת אחריות, ההפך.","w":[["deflect","להסיט, להפנות"],["shoulder","לשאת (באחריות, בנטל)"],["predecessor","קודם בתפקיד"]]},{"q":"The region is famous for its wines and cheeses, ___ the smoked sausages that tourists queue for at its weekend markets.","o":["instead of","not to mention","except for","rather than"],"a":1,"ex":"«Not to mention» = שלא לדבר על. הנקניקים שתיירים עומדים בשבילם בתור הם עוד דבר שהאזור מפורסם בו. «except for» (חוץ מ...) היה מוציא אותם מהרשימה, וזה סותר את התורים.","w":[["not to mention","שלא לדבר על"],["except for","חוץ מ..."],["rather than","במקום, ולא"]]}]},"p3rs1":{"id":"p3rs1","tier":3,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"Seldom have the findings of a single small study been cited as widely as those of the 1998 survey, whose conclusions about sleep and memory were never successfully replicated by later researchers.","o":["The 1998 survey on sleep and memory was rarely cited by other researchers, mainly because its conclusions, unlike those of most small studies, could not be reproduced later.","Few small studies have been cited as often as the 1998 survey on sleep and memory, whose conclusions were later confirmed by several larger research projects.","Few small studies have ever been quoted as frequently as the 1998 survey on sleep and memory, the results of which no later researcher managed to reproduce.","Because its conclusions about sleep and memory were never replicated, the 1998 survey has been cited more widely than any other small study published since then."],"a":2,"ex":"«Seldom have... been cited as widely as» = לעיתים רחוקות צוטטו כל כך הרבה כמו. כלומר מעט מחקרים קטנים צוטטו כמו הסקר של 1998, ואף חוקר לא הצליח לשחזר את ממצאיו. התשובה שבה הסקר «rarely cited» הופכת את המקור, וזו שבה הממצאים «confirmed» סותרת את «never replicated».","w":[["seldom","לעיתים רחוקות"],["replicate","לשחזר (ממצא, ניסוי)"],["cite","לצטט"]]},{"q":"Had the regulators heeded the warnings issued by their own inspectors two years earlier, the collapse of the dam, which flooded three villages and left thousands homeless, might well have been prevented.","o":["Thousands were left homeless and three villages flooded when the dam gave way, which might well have been avoided had the regulators acted on their inspectors' warnings two years before.","The regulators followed their inspectors' warnings two years before the dam collapsed, but this was not enough to keep it from flooding three villages and leaving thousands of people homeless.","The inspectors ignored the regulators' warnings two years earlier, and as a result the dam collapsed, flooding three villages and making thousands of people homeless.","Two years after the regulators ignored their inspectors' warnings, the dam collapsed and flooded three villages, although even full compliance with the warnings would not have saved them."],"a":0,"ex":"«Had the regulators heeded» = אילו הרגולטורים היו מקשיבים. כלומר הם לא הקשיבו, ואם היו מקשיבים ייתכן מאוד שהאסון היה נמנע. התשובה שבה הפקחים התעלמו מאזהרות הרגולטורים מחליפה מי עשה מה, וזו שבה הרגולטורים פעלו לפי האזהרות הופכת את המקור.","w":[["heed","לשים לב, לציית (לאזהרה)"],["avert","למנוע"],["might well","ייתכן מאוד ש..."]]},{"q":"Children who regularly eat dinner with their families tend to report lower levels of anxiety, although researchers stress that the habit may simply reflect other features of stable households rather than reduce anxiety itself.","o":["Eating dinner with their families regularly reduces children's anxiety, researchers say, which explains why stable households, where such meals are common, tend to raise calmer children.","Children who rarely eat dinner with their families tend to report less anxiety, though researchers think this may simply reflect other features of the stable households they come from.","Researchers stress that parents who regularly eat dinner with their children report lower anxiety, but they suspect that the habit itself does little to reduce the parents' stress.","Children who often eat with their families report less anxiety on average, but researchers note that such meals may merely signal a stable home rather than ease anxiety."],"a":3,"ex":"המקור מתאר מתאם בלבד («tend to report»), והחוקרים מדגישים שהארוחות אולי רק משקפות בית יציב ולא מורידות חרדה. התשובה הנכונה שומרת על ההסתייגות. התשובה שאומרת שהארוחות «reduce» חרדה הופכת מתאם לסיבה, בדיוק מה שהחוקרים הזהירו ממנו.","w":[["tend to","נוטה ל..."],["reflect","לשקף"],["although","למרות ש..."]]}]},"p3rs2":{"id":"p3rs2","tier":3,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"Little did the engineers who built the city's first subway in 1890 imagine that, half a century later, its tunnels would shelter thousands of residents from nightly bombing raids.","o":["The engineers who built the city's first subway in 1890 deliberately designed its tunnels so that, decades later, thousands of residents could take shelter in them from nightly bombing raids.","When they constructed the city's first subway in 1890, the engineers had no idea that fifty years on, its tunnels would protect thousands of people from bombing raids every night.","Fifty years after the city's first subway was built, engineers were surprised to discover that thousands of residents had been living permanently in its abandoned tunnels.","In 1890 few residents imagined that the city's new subway tunnels would one day protect them from bombing raids, although the engineers had planned for exactly this."],"a":1,"ex":"«Little did they imagine» = הם כלל לא דמיינו. המהנדסים לא ידעו שחמישים שנה אחר כך המנהרות ישמשו מקלט מהפצצות. התשובות שבהן המהנדסים תכננו זאת מראש הופכות את המשמעות.","w":[["little did","כלל לא (ידעו, דמיינו)"],["shelter","לתת מחסה; מחסה"],["half a century","חצי מאה"]]},{"q":"The more often a password must be changed, the weaker it tends to become, since users who must keep replacing it usually fall back on predictable patterns, such as adding a single digit.","o":["Passwords become stronger the more often they are changed, since users who must keep replacing them learn to avoid predictable patterns such as adding a single digit.","Changing a password frequently always makes it insecure, because every user who must replace it simply adds a single digit to the previous one.","Because weak passwords with predictable patterns are easy to guess, users are now required to change them frequently, usually by adding a single digit.","Passwords that have to be replaced frequently are generally weaker, because people obliged to change them repeatedly tend to make predictable alterations, like adding one more digit."],"a":3,"ex":"«The more... the weaker» = ככל שמחליפים סיסמה יותר, כך היא נוטה להיות חלשה יותר, כי אנשים נאחזים בדפוסים צפויים. התשובה שאומרת שהסיסמה נעשית חזקה יותר הופכת את הקשר, וזו עם «always» ו-«every user» מחמירה כמות שלא נאמרה במקור.","w":[["the more... the","ככל ש... כך..."],["fall back on","להיאחז ב..., לחזור ל... (כברירת מחדל)"],["predictable","צפוי"]]},{"q":"Whatever the merits of the new curriculum, introducing it midway through the school year, without any training for teachers, was bound to cause confusion in classrooms across the country.","o":["Regardless of how good the new curriculum may be, launching it in the middle of the school year without first training teachers was certain to create confusion in classrooms nationwide.","Because the new curriculum had so many merits, teachers across the country adapted to it easily, even though it was introduced in the middle of the school year without training.","The new curriculum caused confusion in classrooms across the country mainly because it was poorly designed, not because it was introduced in the middle of the school year.","Introducing the new curriculum in the middle of the school year would have caused confusion in classrooms had teachers not received thorough training in it beforehand."],"a":0,"ex":"«Whatever the merits» = יהיו היתרונות אשר יהיו, כלומר בלי קשר לטיב התוכנית. הבלבול נבע מההכנסה באמצע השנה ובלי הכשרה. התשובה שמאשימה את תכנון התוכנית סותרת את המקור, וזו שאומרת שהמורים קיבלו הכשרה הופכת אותו.","w":[["regardless of","בלי קשר ל..."],["merit","יתרון, ערך"],["bound to","ודאי ש..., נועד ל..."]]}]},"p3rs3":{"id":"p3rs3","tier":3,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"Should the central bank raise interest rates again this year, economists warn, small businesses already burdened with debt from the pandemic may find it impossible to keep up with their loan repayments.","o":["Economists warn that the central bank will raise interest rates again this year because small businesses, burdened by pandemic debts, have stopped repaying their loans.","Economists believe that even if the central bank raises interest rates again this year, small businesses will manage to repay the loans they took out during the pandemic.","According to economists, if the central bank increases interest rates again this year, small firms still weighed down by pandemic-era debt might be unable to go on repaying their loans.","Economists warn that unless the central bank raises interest rates again this year, small businesses still in debt from the pandemic may be unable to keep up with their repayments."],"a":2,"ex":"«Should the bank raise» = אם הבנק יעלה. זה תנאי ולא קביעה. התשובה עם «unless» הופכת את התנאי, וזו עם «even if... will manage» אומרת את ההפך מהאזהרה.","w":[["should","(בפתיחת משפט) אם, במקרה ש..."],["burdened","עמוס, מוכבד"],["keep up with","לעמוד בקצב של"]]},{"q":"Not only did the new irrigation system cut the farm's water consumption by nearly half, but it also raised crop yields, a result that surprised even the engineers who had designed it.","o":["The new irrigation system raised the farm's crop yields just as its engineers had predicted, although it also nearly doubled the amount of water that the farm consumed.","The farm's new irrigation system reduced its water use by almost fifty percent and, to the astonishment of even its own designers, increased the size of its harvests as well.","The engineers who designed the new irrigation system were surprised that it reduced the farm's water use by only a small amount and did nothing to improve its crop yields.","Because the new irrigation system halved the farm's water consumption, its crop yields fell slightly, which surprised even the engineers who had designed it."],"a":1,"ex":"«Not only... but also» = לא רק... אלא גם: המערכת גם חסכה כמחצית מהמים וגם העלתה את היבול, וזה הפתיע אפילו את המתכננים. התשובה שבה היבול ירד הופכת את התוצאה, וזו שבה צריכת המים כמעט הוכפלה סותרת את המקור.","w":[["not only... but also","לא רק... אלא גם"],["yield","יבול, תפוקה"],["consumption","צריכה"]]},{"q":"Insofar as the museum depends on ticket sales for most of its income, any prolonged closure, however necessary for renovations, poses a serious threat to its survival.","o":["Since most of the museum's revenue comes from ticket sales, closing it for a long time endangers its very existence, even if the closure is essential for renovation.","Since the museum earns very little of its income from ticket sales, it can easily afford to close for long renovations without putting its survival at any serious risk.","The museum's survival is threatened mainly by the cost of its renovations, which are necessary even though they will reduce its income from ticket sales.","Any long closure for renovations would threaten the museum's survival, so its managers have decided to postpone the work until ticket sales improve."],"a":0,"ex":"«Insofar as» = מאחר ש..., במידה ש... המוזיאון תלוי בכרטיסים, ולכן כל סגירה ארוכה, הכרחית ככל שתהיה, מסכנת אותו. התשובה שאומרת שהמוזיאון מרוויח מעט מכרטיסים הופכת את הנחת היסוד, וזו שמספרת על דחיית השיפוץ מוסיפה החלטה שלא נאמרה.","w":[["insofar as","במידה ש..., מאחר ש..."],["prolonged","ממושך"],["however necessary","הכרחי ככל שיהיה"]]}]},"p3rs4":{"id":"p3rs4","tier":3,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"Rarely, if ever, do migrating cranes alter their route from one year to the next, which is why the sudden appearance of thousands of them over the desert last autumn baffled ornithologists.","o":["Migrating cranes often change their route from one year to the next, so ornithologists were not surprised when thousands of them suddenly appeared over the desert last autumn.","Ornithologists were puzzled last autumn when thousands of migrating cranes failed to appear over the desert, a route they had followed every year for as long as anyone could remember.","Because thousands of cranes flew over the desert last autumn, ornithologists now believe that the birds will permanently alter their migration route in the coming years.","Since migrating cranes almost never change the path they follow from year to year, bird experts were puzzled when thousands of them unexpectedly turned up above the desert last fall."],"a":3,"ex":"«Rarely, if ever» = לעיתים רחוקות, אם בכלל, כלומר כמעט אף פעם. מכיוון שהעגורים כמעט לא משנים מסלול, הופעתם הפתאומית מעל המדבר בלבלה את החוקרים. התשובה עם «often change» הופכת את התדירות, וזו שבה העגורים לא הופיעו הופכת את האירוע.","w":[["rarely","לעיתים רחוקות"],["if ever","אם בכלל"],["baffle","לבלבל, להביך"]]},{"q":"For all its popularity among divers, the island's coral reef has attracted surprisingly little scientific study, so that even the rate at which it is deteriorating remains largely a matter of guesswork.","o":["Because it is so popular among divers, the island's coral reef has been studied extensively, and scientists now know precisely how fast it is deteriorating.","The island's coral reef is deteriorating so quickly that divers have lost interest in it, although scientists have studied the process in great detail.","Although divers flock to the island's coral reef, scientists have examined it so rarely that nobody can really say how quickly it is declining.","Scientists have paid little attention to the island's coral reef because crowds of divers make research there impossible, so its rate of decline is still unknown."],"a":2,"ex":"«For all its popularity» = למרות הפופולריות שלו. השונית פופולרית אצל צוללנים, ובכל זאת כמעט לא נחקרה, ולכן לא יודעים כמה מהר היא מתדרדרת. התשובה עם «Because it is so popular» הופכת את «for all» מוויתור לסיבה, וזו שמאשימה את הצוללנים מוסיפה סיבה שלא נאמרה.","w":[["for all","למרות, על אף"],["deteriorate","להידרדר, להתדרדר"],["guesswork","ניחוש"]]},{"q":"Whereas earlier historians portrayed the queen as a mere figurehead manipulated by her advisers, recent studies of her private letters suggest that she personally shaped many of the kingdom's key policies.","o":["Recent studies of the queen's private letters confirm the view of earlier historians that she was a mere figurehead whose policies were shaped by her advisers.","Older historians saw the queen as a powerless puppet of her advisers, but recent research into her correspondence suggests that she herself set much of the kingdom's major policy.","Earlier historians believed that the queen personally shaped the kingdom's key policies, but her private letters show that her advisers actually manipulated her into making most of her decisions.","Recent studies of her advisers' private letters suggest that the queen, whom earlier historians had ignored, was manipulated into shaping many of the kingdom's key policies."],"a":1,"ex":"«Whereas» = ואילו, בעוד ש... בעבר ראו במלכה בובה בידי יועציה, ואילו מחקרים חדשים מראים שהיא עצמה עיצבה מדיניות. התשובה עם «confirm» הופכת את המקור, וזו שבה ההיסטוריונים הישנים חשבו שהיא שלטה הופכת את הכיוון.","w":[["whereas","בעוד ש..., ואילו"],["figurehead","דמות סמלית בלי סמכות"],["manipulate","לתמרן, להפעיל"]]}]},"p3rs5":{"id":"p3rs5","tier":3,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"Only by drastically reducing its reliance on imported grain, analysts argue, can the country hope to shield its population from the sharp swings in food prices that have repeatedly triggered unrest.","o":["According to analysts, the country's only hope of protecting its people from the steep food price fluctuations that keep sparking unrest is to cut its dependence on foreign grain sharply.","Analysts argue that by importing more grain, the country can protect its population from the sharp swings in food prices that have repeatedly caused unrest.","According to analysts, cutting grain imports drastically is one of several ways the country could protect its people from food price swings, which have occasionally led to unrest.","Analysts argue that the repeated unrest in the country has caused sharp swings in food prices, which can be stopped only if the country drastically reduces the amount of grain it imports."],"a":0,"ex":"«Only by... can» = רק על ידי... אפשר. לפי המנתחים, צמצום התלות ביבוא תבואה הוא הדרך היחידה להגן מפני תנודות מחירים. התשובה עם «one of several ways» משנה «רק» ל«אחת מכמה», וזו שבה המהומות גרמו לתנודות הופכת סיבה ותוצאה.","w":[["only by","רק באמצעות"],["reliance","תלות, הסתמכות"],["shield","להגן, לסוכך"]]},{"q":"So persuasive was the defense lawyer's closing argument that several jurors who had initially been convinced of the defendant's guilt changed their minds, and the trial ended in acquittal.","o":["Although the defense lawyer's closing argument was highly persuasive, several jurors remained convinced of the defendant's guilt, and so the trial ended without any verdict.","Several jurors changed their minds about the defendant's innocence after the prosecutor's persuasive closing argument, and as a result the defendant was convicted.","The defendant was acquitted because all of the jurors, who had believed from the very start that he was innocent, found the defense lawyer's closing argument persuasive.","The defense lawyer's final speech convinced several jurors who had at first thought the defendant guilty to reconsider, and so the defendant was found not guilty."],"a":3,"ex":"«So persuasive was... that» = כל כך משכנע היה... ש... הנאום של הסנגור שכנע כמה מושבעים לשנות את דעתם, והנאשם זוכה. התשובה שבה התובע שכנע והנאשם הורשע מחליפה מי עשה מה, וזו עם «all of the jurors» משנה את הכמות ואת מה שהם חשבו בהתחלה.","w":[["so... that","כל כך... ש..."],["acquittal","זיכוי"],["initially","בתחילה"]]},{"q":"While the new drug relieves symptoms in roughly two-thirds of patients, it does nothing to slow the underlying progression of the disease, a limitation that its manufacturer's advertising rarely mentions.","o":["The new drug slows the progression of the disease in about two-thirds of patients, but its manufacturer's advertising rarely mentions that it does little to relieve their symptoms.","The new drug relieves symptoms in only a third of patients and does not slow the disease at all, a limitation that its manufacturer's advertising repeatedly emphasizes.","The new drug eases symptoms in about two out of three patients but does not slow the disease's course, a shortcoming the company's advertisements seldom point out.","Because it relieves symptoms in two-thirds of patients, the new drug also slows the progression of the disease, as its manufacturer's advertising frequently points out."],"a":2,"ex":"«While» כאן = בעוד ש... (ניגוד): התרופה מקלה על התסמינים אצל כשני שלישים, אבל לא מאטה את המחלה, והפרסומות כמעט לא מזכירות זאת. התשובה עם «repeatedly emphasizes» הופכת את «rarely», וזו שבה התרופה מאטה את המחלה מוסיפה קשר סיבתי שלא קיים.","w":[["while","בעוד ש... (ניגוד)"],["progression","התקדמות (של מחלה)"],["seldom","לעיתים רחוקות"]]}]},"p3rs6":{"id":"p3rs6","tier":3,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"Under no circumstances may researchers publish a patient's name, even with the patient's consent, unless an independent ethics board has first reviewed the case and approved the disclosure in writing.","o":["Researchers may publish patients' names whenever the patients themselves agree to it, provided that an independent ethics board is later informed of the whole case in writing.","Researchers may reveal a patient's name only after an independent ethics board has examined the case and given written approval; the patient's own consent is not enough.","An independent ethics board may never approve the publication of patients' names, even when researchers have obtained the patients' written consent beforehand.","Once a patient has given written consent, researchers must ask an independent ethics board whether the patient's name may be withheld from their publication."],"a":1,"ex":"«Under no circumstances... unless» = בשום מקרה לא... אלא אם כן. אסור לפרסם שם, גם בהסכמת המטופל, בלי אישור מוקדם בכתב של ועדת אתיקה. התשובה שמסתפקת בהסכמת המטופל ובדיווח לוועדה אחר כך הופכת את הכלל, וזו שבה הוועדה לעולם לא מאשרת סותרת את «unless».","w":[["under no circumstances","בשום מקרה לא"],["unless","אלא אם כן"],["disclosure","חשיפה, גילוי"]]},{"q":"Despite having been banned in most European countries for over two decades, the pesticide is still detectable in the region's groundwater, an indication of how slowly some chemicals break down in soil.","o":["Though most European countries outlawed the pesticide over twenty years ago, traces of it remain in the region's groundwater, showing how long certain chemicals take to decompose in soil.","Because the pesticide breaks down slowly in soil, most European countries banned it over two decades ago, and it has since disappeared from the region's groundwater.","The pesticide was banned in only a few European countries two decades ago, which explains why it can still be detected in the region's groundwater today.","Although the pesticide has been banned in most European countries for over twenty years, farmers in the region are still secretly using it, and it continues to contaminate the local groundwater."],"a":0,"ex":"«Despite having been banned» = למרות שנאסר. החומר נאסר לפני יותר מעשרים שנה ועדיין נמצא במי התהום, וזה מראה כמה לאט חומרים מסוימים מתפרקים. התשובה שאומרת שחקלאים עדיין משתמשים בו מוסיפה טענה שלא נאמרה, וזו עם «only a few countries» משנה את הכמות.","w":[["despite","למרות (+שם עצם)"],["detectable","ניתן לגילוי"],["break down","להתפרק"]]},{"q":"No matter how carefully a translation is prepared, some of the original text's humor is bound to be lost, since jokes often depend on sounds and double meanings peculiar to a single language.","o":["A carefully prepared translation can preserve all of the original text's humor, as long as the translator understands the sounds and double meanings on which its jokes depend.","Jokes are often lost only in careless translations, because such translators ignore the sounds and double meanings of the original, which careful translators usually manage to reproduce.","Since most jokes depend on sounds and double meanings that many languages share, a careful translation usually loses only a very small part of the original humor.","Even the most painstaking translation will inevitably fail to preserve part of the original's humor, because jokes frequently rely on sounds and double meanings that exist in only one language."],"a":3,"ex":"«No matter how carefully» = לא משנה כמה בקפידה. גם התרגום הזהיר ביותר יאבד חלק מההומור, כי בדיחות נשענות על צלילים ומשמעויות כפולות של שפה אחת. התשובה שאומרת שאפשר לשמר את כל ההומור הופכת את המקור, וזו שאומרת שהמשמעויות משותפות לשפות רבות הופכת את הסיבה.","w":[["no matter how","לא משנה כמה"],["bound to","ודאי ש..., נועד ל..."],["peculiar to","ייחודי ל..."]]}]},"s1c0":{"id":"s1c0","tier":0,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"Many students drink coffee in the evening ___ they have to study late for their exams.","o":["unless","because","although","whereas"],"a":1,"ex":"«because» = כי, מפני ש. החלק השני (צריך ללמוד עד מאוחר) הוא הסיבה לחלק הראשון (שותים קפה בערב). «although» היה יוצר ניגוד, אבל אין כאן שום ניגוד.","w":[["because","כי, מפני ש..."],["although","למרות ש..."]]},{"q":"Doctors say that regular exercise can ___ your sleep, so people who walk every day often rest better at night.","o":["improve","avoid","delay","waste"],"a":0,"ex":"«improve» = לשפר. סוף המשפט אומר שמי שהולך כל יום ישן טוב יותר, ולכן הפעילות משפרת את השינה. «delay» (לדחות) או «waste» (לבזבז) היו אומרים שהשינה נפגעת.","w":[["improve","לשפר"],["regular","קבוע, סדיר"]]},{"q":"___ the museum is free on Sundays, very few people visit it during the winter.","o":["Since","Unless","As soon as","Although"],"a":3,"ex":"«Although» = למרות ש. היינו מצפים שכניסה חינם תביא הרבה מבקרים, אבל מגיעים מעט: זה ניגוד, ולכן צריך מילת ויתור. «Since» (מכיוון ש) היה אומר שהכניסה החינמית היא הסיבה לכך שמעטים מגיעים, וזה לא הגיוני.","w":[["although","למרות ש..."],["since","מכיוון ש..."]]},{"q":"The number of small shops in the town center has ___ sharply in recent years, as more people now buy everything online.","o":["appeared","repaired","declined","celebrated"],"a":2,"ex":"«decline» = לרדת, לפחות. אנשים קונים באינטרנט, ולכן מספר החנויות ירד. «sharply» (בחדות) מתאר שינוי בכמות, וזה מתאים רק ל-«declined».","w":[["decline","לרדת, לפחות"],["sharply","בחדות"]]}]},"s1c1":{"id":"s1c1","tier":0,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"To save money, Dana decided to cook dinner at home ___ eating at an expensive restaurant every night.","o":["because of","in addition to","instead of","as a result of"],"a":2,"ex":"«instead of» = במקום. כדי לחסוך, דנה מבשלת בבית במקום לאכול במסעדה יקרה. «in addition to» (בנוסף ל) היה אומר שהיא גם אוכלת במסעדה כל ערב, וזה לא חוסך כסף.","w":[["instead of","במקום (+שם עצם / ing)"],["in addition to","בנוסף ל... (+שם עצם)"]]},{"q":"Because infections spread easily, most hospitals ___ visitors to wash their hands; anyone who refuses is not allowed to enter.","o":["forbid","require","pay","encourage"],"a":1,"ex":"«require» = לדרוש, לחייב. מי שמסרב לא נכנס, כלומר זו חובה ולא המלצה. «encourage» (לעודד) מפתה, אבל עידוד לא בא עם עונש למי שמסרב.","w":[["require","לדרוש, לחייב"],["refuse","לסרב"]]},{"q":"You will not be able to join the trip ___ you return the signed form by Friday.","o":["unless","because","so that","although"],"a":0,"ex":"«unless» = אלא אם כן. לא תוכל להצטרף לטיול אלא אם תחזיר את הטופס: זה תנאי. «because» היה אומר שהחזרת הטופס היא הסיבה שלא תצטרף, וזה הפוך מההיגיון.","w":[["unless","אלא אם כן"],["so that","כדי ש... (+משפט)"]]},{"q":"Archaeologists found ___ coins in the desert that were used by traders more than two thousand years ago.","o":["modern","plastic","electronic","ancient"],"a":3,"ex":"«ancient» = עתיק. מטבעות שהשתמשו בהם לפני יותר מאלפיים שנה הם עתיקים. «modern» (מודרני) הוא בדיוק ההפך.","w":[["ancient","עתיק"],["trader","סוחר"]]}]},"s1c2":{"id":"s1c2","tier":0,"type":"rc","title":"Travelers in the Dark","text":["Every spring and autumn, billions of birds travel thousands of kilometers between their summer and winter homes. What surprises many people is that a large number of these birds, including most small songbirds, make their journeys at night. While we sleep, the sky above us may be full of tiny travelers that we never see.","Scientists believe there are several reasons for this behavior. First, the air at night is usually cooler and calmer than during the day. Flying is hard work, and small birds can easily lose too much water if they fly under a hot sun. Cool night air helps them avoid this danger. In addition, the dark sky protects them from hawks and other hunters, which mostly look for food in daylight.","Night travel also allows birds to use their time well. During the day, they can rest and eat in fields and forests, so they replace the energy they used the night before. Without these daily stops, few birds would have enough strength to complete such a long trip.","But how do birds find their way in the dark? Research shows that they use several tools at once. Some young birds learn the pattern of the stars, especially the stars around the North Star, which hardly moves during the night. Birds can also sense the earth's magnetic field, which works for them like a natural compass. Unfortunately, bright city lights can confuse them, and many birds crash into tall buildings. For this reason, some cities now ask building owners to turn off unnecessary lights during migration season."],"qs":[{"q":"The passage mainly discusses","o":["the dangers that hawks present to small songbirds","why many birds migrate at night and how they find their way","how cities have reduced the number of birds in the sky","the differences between the summer and winter homes of birds"],"a":1,"ex":"הקטע כולו עוסק בשתי שאלות: למה ציפורים נודדות בלילה (פסקאות 2-3) ואיך הן מוצאות את הדרך בחושך (פסקה 4). הנצים מוזכרים רק במשפט אחד, ולכן זו לא התשובה הכללית.","w":[["migrate","לנדוד"],["mainly","בעיקר"]]},{"q":"According to the second paragraph, one advantage of flying at night is that","o":["birds can find more food in the dark","the stars are easier to see in autumn","hawks are more active after sunset","birds lose less water in the cool air"],"a":3,"ex":"בפסקה 2 כתוב שבשמש חמה ציפורים קטנות מאבדות יותר מדי מים, ושאוויר הלילה הקריר עוזר להן להימנע מזה. לגבי הנצים כתוב ההפך: הם צדים בעיקר ביום.","w":[["advantage","יתרון"],["avoid","להימנע מ..."]]},{"q":"In the third paragraph, the word 'they' in 'so they replace the energy' refers to","o":["the birds","the fields and forests","the days","the hunters"],"a":0,"ex":"מי שנח ואוכל ביום וכך ממלא את האנרגיה שבזבז בלילה הן הציפורים. שדות ויערות הם רק המקום שבו הן נחות.","w":[["replace","להחליף, למלא מחדש"],["energy","אנרגיה, כוח"]]},{"q":"The main purpose of the last sentence of the passage is to","o":["explain why birds prefer to fly near big cities","show that the North Star is difficult to see from cities","describe one step that is taken to protect migrating birds","prove that birds cannot use the earth's magnetic field"],"a":2,"ex":"המשפט האחרון מתחיל ב-«For this reason» (מסיבה זו): בגלל שהאורות מבלבלים את הציפורים, ערים מבקשות לכבות אורות מיותרים. זה צעד שנועד להגן עליהן. הקטע לא אומר שציפורים מעדיפות ערים.","w":[["for this reason","מסיבה זו"],["unnecessary","מיותר"]]},{"q":"It can be inferred from paragraph 3 that if birds could not stop during the day,","o":["they would fly faster at night","most of them would not finish their journey","they would learn the pattern of the stars more quickly","hunters would stop looking for them"],"a":1,"ex":"בפסקה 3 כתוב שבלי העצירות היומיות מעט ציפורים (few birds) היו מצליחות להשלים את המסע. כלומר רובן לא היו מסיימות אותו. אין בקטע שום דבר על טיסה מהירה יותר.","w":[["infer","להסיק"],["few","מעט (כמעט אין)"]]}]},"s1c3":{"id":"s1c3","tier":0,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"Although the new bridge cost much more than planned, most residents believe it was worth the money because it cut their travel time in half.","o":["Because the new bridge cost much more than planned, most residents believe it was not worth the money, even though it cut their travel time.","Most residents believe the new bridge was worth the money, since it cost less than planned and cut their travel time in half.","The new bridge was far more expensive than expected; nevertheless, most residents think it was a good investment, since it halved their travel time.","Only a few residents think the new bridge was a good investment, even though it cost more than planned and cut their travel time in half."],"a":2,"ex":"«Although» הוחלף ב-«nevertheless» (למרות זאת), ו-«cut in half» הוחלף ב-«halved». המשמעות זהה: הגשר יקר, ובכל זאת רוב התושבים חושבים שהוא שווה. בתשובה האחרונה «Only a few» (רק מעטים) הופך את «most» (רוב).","w":[["nevertheless","למרות זאת, אף על פי כן"],["worth","שווה"],["resident","תושב"]]},{"q":"Unless farmers receive more rain this winter, they will have to plant fewer crops next year, which may raise food prices.","o":["If it does not rain more this winter, farmers will have to grow fewer crops next year, and food may get more expensive.","Even if much more rain falls this winter, farmers will still plant fewer crops next year, so food prices will certainly go down.","Farmers will plant more crops next year only if food prices rise sharply during this winter, regardless of the rain.","Because farmers received a lot of rain this winter, they will plant fewer crops next year, and food prices may fall as a result."],"a":0,"ex":"«Unless» = אלא אם כן, ובמילים אחרות «If ... not». התשובה הנכונה שומרת את התנאי (בלי גשם), את התוצאה (פחות גידולים) ואת האפשרות שהמחירים יעלו. «Even if» (גם אם) מבטל את התנאי, ושם המחירים גם יורדים.","w":[["unless","אלא אם כן"],["even if","גם אם, אפילו אם"],["crop","יבול, גידול חקלאי"]]},{"q":"Children who read for pleasure every day tend to develop a richer vocabulary than children who read only for school assignments.","o":["Children who read only for their school assignments usually know more words than children who read for fun every day.","Reading every day for pleasure makes it harder for children to finish their school assignments.","All children develop the same vocabulary, whether they read for fun or only for school.","Children who read daily for enjoyment usually know more words than those who read just for school tasks."],"a":3,"ex":"«for pleasure» = «for enjoyment», ו-«tend to develop a richer vocabulary» = בדרך כלל יודעים יותר מילים. התשובה הראשונה הופכת את ההשוואה, כאילו מי שקורא רק לבית הספר יודע יותר מילים.","w":[["tend to","נוטה ל..."],["vocabulary","אוצר מילים"],["assignment","מטלה"]]}]},"s1c4":{"id":"s1c4","tier":0,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"Many people avoid going to the dentist because they are afraid of pain, even though modern treatments are usually quick and almost painless.","o":["Modern dental treatments are often slow and painful, which is why many people refuse to visit the dentist at all.","Fear of pain keeps many people away from the dentist, although today's treatments are usually fast and nearly painless.","Many people visit the dentist often and without fear, because modern treatments are quick and almost painless.","Few people are afraid of the dentist today, since modern treatments have become quick and almost painless for most patients."],"a":1,"ex":"«even though» הוחלף ב-«although» (שתיהן: למרות ש), ו-«avoid going» הוחלף ב-«keeps away». הפחד מרחיק אנשים למרות שהטיפולים כמעט לא כואבים. בתשובה הראשונה הטיפולים כואבים, וזה ההפך מהמקור.","w":[["even though","אף על פי ש..."],["although","למרות ש..."],["avoid","להימנע מ..."]]},{"q":"The company decided to improve its training program after a survey showed that new workers did not understand many of their basic tasks.","o":["A survey found that new workers understood their basic tasks well, so the company kept its training program as it was.","The company improved its training program, and as a result, new workers began to complete a survey about their tasks.","New workers asked the company to cancel its training program because they already understood their basic tasks.","When a survey revealed that new employees were confused about many basic duties, the company chose to make its training better."],"a":3,"ex":"קודם הסקר הראה שהעובדים לא מבינים, ורק אחר כך החברה החליטה לשפר את ההדרכה. «improve» = «make better», ו-«did not understand» = «were confused». בתשובה השנייה הסדר הפוך: הסקר מופיע כתוצאה של השיפור.","w":[["improve","לשפר"],["after","אחרי"],["survey","סקר"]]},{"q":"Ancient sailors could cross wide seas without modern tools, since they learned to read the positions of the sun and the stars.","o":["Because they knew how to navigate by the sun and stars, sailors long ago could cross large seas without modern equipment.","Sailors long ago could not cross wide seas, because without modern tools they had no reliable way to find their direction.","Ancient sailors used modern tools to study the positions of the sun and the stars before they crossed wide seas.","Although ancient sailors studied the sun and the stars carefully, this knowledge rarely helped them when they tried to cross wide seas."],"a":0,"ex":"«since» כאן = מכיוון ש, ובתשובה הנכונה הוא הוחלף ב-«Because». «Ancient» = «long ago», ו-«tools» = «equipment». התשובה האחרונה הופכת את הסיבה לניגוד ואומרת שהידע כמעט לא עזר.","w":[["since","מכיוון ש..."],["ancient","עתיק, מימי קדם"],["rarely","לעיתים רחוקות"]]}]},"s1c5":{"id":"s1c5","tier":0,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"The road to the village was blocked by snow; ___, the doctor had to reach the patient by helicopter.","o":["however","for example","therefore","in contrast"],"a":2,"ex":"«therefore» = לכן. הכביש חסום, ולכן הרופא הגיע במסוק: זו תוצאה. «however» (עם זאת) היה יוצר ניגוד, אבל אין כאן ניגוד.","w":[["therefore","לכן"],["however","עם זאת, אולם"],["block","לחסום"]]},{"q":"Many drivers leave home before 7 a.m. in order to ___ the heavy traffic that fills the roads later in the morning.","o":["avoid","enjoy","create","measure"],"a":0,"ex":"«avoid» = להימנע מ. נהגים יוצאים מוקדם כדי לא להיתקע בפקקים. «create» (ליצור) או «enjoy» (ליהנות) לא מתאימים, כי אף אחד לא יוצא מוקדם כדי ליצור פקקים או ליהנות מהם.","w":[["avoid","להימנע מ..."],["in order to","כדי ל... (+פועל)"]]},{"q":"The new medicine must be tested on thousands of patients before doctors can ___ that it is safe.","o":["forget","hide","doubt","confirm"],"a":3,"ex":"«confirm» = לאשר, לוודא. בודקים את התרופה על אלפי חולים כדי לדעת בוודאות שהיא בטוחה. «doubt» (לפקפק) הוא ההפך: לא עושים ניסויים ארוכים כדי להתחיל לפקפק.","w":[["confirm","לאשר, לוודא"],["doubt","לפקפק"]]},{"q":"The old bus was so ___ that it broke down almost every week, and passengers often arrived late.","o":["popular","unreliable","expensive","comfortable"],"a":1,"ex":"«unreliable» = לא אמין. אוטובוס שמתקלקל כל שבוע ומאחר הוא לא אמין. «so ... that» (כל כך... ש) מחייב שהתכונה תסביר את התקלות, ו-«popular» או «comfortable» לא מסבירים אותן.","w":[["unreliable","לא אמין"],["so... that","כל כך... ש..."],["break down","להתקלקל"]]}]},"s10c0":{"id":"s10c0","tier":2,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"The committee's report was deliberately ___, offering broad recommendations while avoiding any specific commitment that might later prove embarrassing.","o":["meticulous","candid","vague","lavish"],"a":2,"ex":"«vague» = מעורפל, לא ברור. הדוח נמנע בכוונה מהתחייבות ספציפית ונתן רק המלצות כלליות, כלומר הוא מעורפל. «meticulous» (קפדני, מדוקדק) ו-«candid» (גלוי, כן) הם בדיוק ההפך מדוח שמתחמק מפרטים.","w":[["vague","מעורפל, לא ברור"],["deliberately","בכוונה"],["commitment","התחייבות"]]},{"q":"The theory was widely ridiculed when it was first proposed; ___, within two decades it had become the accepted explanation among geologists.","o":["consequently","nonetheless","likewise","namely"],"a":1,"ex":"«nonetheless» = למרות זאת. בהתחלה לעגו לתיאוריה, ובכל זאת היא התקבלה: יש כאן ניגוד. «consequently» (כתוצאה מכך) לא מתאים, כי הלעג לא גרם לתיאוריה להתקבל.","w":[["nonetheless","בכל זאת, למרות זאת"],["ridicule","ללעוג ל..."]]},{"q":"Years of drought had so ___ the soil that even after heavy rains, the farmers' crops failed to recover.","o":["depleted","enriched","replenished","insulated"],"a":0,"ex":"«deplete» = לרוקן, לדלדל. הבצורת דלדלה את האדמה, ולכן היבולים לא התאוששו גם אחרי גשם. «enriched» ו-«replenished» (העשיר, מילא מחדש) הם ההפך, ואז היבול היה אמור להצליח.","w":[["deplete","לדלדל, לרוקן"],["replenish","למלא מחדש"]]},{"q":"___ the museum receives additional funding, several of its galleries will have to close by the end of the year.","o":["Provided that","Since","Whereas","Unless"],"a":3,"ex":"«Unless» = אלא אם כן. האולמות ייסגרו, אלא אם כן המוזיאון יקבל עוד כסף. «Provided that» (בתנאי ש...) היה אומר שהכסף הנוסף הוא מה שיגרום לסגירה, וזה לא הגיוני.","w":[["unless","אלא אם כן"],["provided that","בתנאי ש..."]]}]},"s10c1":{"id":"s10c1","tier":2,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"The senator's remarks were widely condemned as ___, since they appeared to encourage hostility toward an entire community.","o":["conciliatory","tedious","inconspicuous","inflammatory"],"a":3,"ex":"«inflammatory» = מסית, מלבה יצרים. דברים שמעודדים עוינות כלפי קהילה שלמה הם מסיתים. «conciliatory» (מפייס) הוא ההפך, ו-«tedious» (משעמם) לא קשור לעידוד עוינות.","w":[["inflammatory","מסית, מלבה יצרים"],["conciliatory","מפייס"],["hostility","עוינות"]]},{"q":"The novel received little attention from critics when it first appeared, ___ it went on to sell millions of copies and was translated into forty languages.","o":["so","for","yet","as"],"a":2,"ex":"«yet» = ובכל זאת, אך. המבקרים כמעט התעלמו מהספר, ובכל זאת הוא נמכר במיליונים: ניגוד. «so» (לכן) היה אומר שההתעלמות גרמה להצלחה, וזה לא הגיוני.","w":[["yet","ובכל זאת, אך"]]},{"q":"Although the two scientists worked independently on different continents, they arrived at remarkably ___ conclusions about the origin of the disease.","o":["divergent","analogous","obscure","tentative"],"a":1,"ex":"«analogous» = דומה, מקביל. המילה «Although» מראה שמשהו מפתיע: למרות שעבדו בנפרד, הם הגיעו למסקנות דומות. «divergent» (שונות זו מזו) לא היה מפתיע בכלל, ולכן לא מתאים ל-«Although».","w":[["analogous","דומה, מקביל"],["divergent","שונה, מתפצל"],["although","למרות ש..."]]},{"q":"The city has introduced strict water quotas ___ its reservoirs run dry before the rainy season arrives.","o":["lest","once","so that","whereas"],"a":0,"ex":"«lest» = כדי שלא, פן. העירייה הגבילה את המים כדי שהמאגרים לא יתרוקנו. «so that» (כדי ש...) היה אומר שהמטרה היא לרוקן את המאגרים, וזה הפוך מההיגיון.","w":[["lest","פן, כדי שלא"],["quota","מכסה"],["reservoir","מאגר מים"]]}]},"s10c2":{"id":"s10c2","tier":2,"type":"rc","title":"After the Bleaching: Why Some Reefs Return and Others Do Not","text":["Coral reefs owe their existence to a partnership. Inside the tissues of each coral live microscopic algae that, through photosynthesis, supply the coral with most of the energy it needs. This arrangement, however, is remarkably sensitive to heat. When the water stays only one or two degrees above its usual summer maximum for several weeks, the corals expel their algae and, stripped of their color, turn white. A bleached coral is not yet dead. If temperatures drop quickly, the algae can return within weeks; if the heat persists, the coral gradually starves, and its skeleton is soon covered by seaweed.","When large numbers of corals die, a reef's recovery depends largely on new arrivals. Surviving colonies release larvae, which drift with the currents until they settle on a hard surface. Reefs that are well connected to healthy reefs upstream therefore tend to recover faster than isolated ones. Yet larvae are demanding: they attach readily to clean, bare rock but struggle where seaweed has taken over. This is why plant-eating fish, which graze the seaweed down, play a surprisingly important role: reefs where catching them is restricted often recover faster.","Even under favorable conditions, recovery is slow and uneven. Fast-growing branching corals may restore much of a reef's cover within a decade, whereas massive, dome-shaped species, some of which are several centuries old, may need far longer to replace themselves. A return of coral cover can therefore be deceptive. A reef may appear healthy while its composition has shifted toward a few fast-growing species, and these happen to be among the most vulnerable to heat.","The greatest threat, scientists argue, is no longer the severity of individual bleaching events but their frequency. Until recently, severe episodes were separated by decades, which gave reefs time to rebuild. As the oceans warm, that interval has shrunk in some regions to only a few years. Local measures, such as protecting grazing fish and reducing pollution, can speed recovery, but they cannot on their own make up for gaps that are simply too short. Some researchers are now trying to breed corals that tolerate higher temperatures; others warn that such efforts can, at best, buy reefs time."],"qs":[{"q":"Which of the following is the best title for the passage?","o":["Why Corals Turn White in Warm Water","What Determines Whether Reefs Recover from Bleaching","How Overfishing Has Destroyed the World's Reefs","Heat-Tolerant Corals: A Solution Within Reach"],"a":1,"ex":"הקטע עוסק כולו בשאלה מה קובע אם שונית מתאוששת אחרי הלבנה: זרמים, דגים, קצב גדילה ותדירות האירועים. «Why Corals Turn White» מתאים רק לפסקה הראשונה, ולכן הוא צר מדי.","w":[["recover","להתאושש"],["bleaching","הלבנה (של אלמוגים)"]]},{"q":"According to the second paragraph, plant-eating fish help reefs recover because they","o":["carry coral larvae on their bodies from healthy reefs to damaged ones","feed on the algae that bleached corals expel","protect young corals from fish that eat them","keep the rock clear enough for larvae to attach to it"],"a":3,"ex":"בפסקה 2 כתוב שהלרוות נאחזות בסלע נקי וחשוף ומתקשות במקום שהאצות השתלטו עליו, והדגים אוכלים את האצות. כלומר הם שומרים על הסלע נקי. את הלרוות מביאים הזרמים, לא הדגים.","w":[["graze","ללחך, לאכול צמחייה"],["larvae","זחלים, לרוות"],["attach","להיצמד"]]},{"q":"In the third paragraph, the word 'deceptive' could best be replaced by","o":["misleading","encouraging","temporary","accurate"],"a":0,"ex":"«deceptive» = מטעה. המשפט שאחריו מסביר: השונית נראית בריאה, אבל בפועל היא השתנתה. «encouraging» (מעודד) מפתה, כי כיסוי אלמוגים שחוזר נראה חיובי, אבל הפסקה מדגישה שהמראה מטעה.","w":[["deceptive","מטעה"],["composition","הרכב"]]},{"q":"The third paragraph mainly serves to","o":["explain why branching corals withstand heat better than massive ones","show that all coral species need about a decade to recover fully from a bleaching event","warn that a reef that looks recovered may have changed in important ways","describe how scientists determine the age of massive corals"],"a":2,"ex":"עיקר הפסקה: שונית שנראית מבריאה יכולה להיות מורכבת ממינים אחרים, רגישים יותר לחום. התשובה הראשונה הפוכה: לפי הקטע, האלמוגים המהירים דווקא מהפגיעים ביותר לחום.","w":[["uneven","לא אחיד"],["vulnerable","פגיע"]]},{"q":"It can be inferred from the last paragraph that local measures such as protecting grazing fish","o":["have become unnecessary now that heat-tolerant corals can be bred","are the main reason that bleaching events now occur more often","work only in regions where bleaching occurs every few years","can help reefs recover but are not enough if bleaching becomes too frequent"],"a":3,"ex":"כתוב שהצעדים המקומיים מאיצים התאוששות, אבל לא יכולים לבדם לפצות על מרווחים קצרים מדי. כלומר הם עוזרים אבל לא מספיקים. אין בקטע שום טענה שהגידול של אלמוגים עמידים כבר מצליח או שהוא מייתר אותם.","w":[["make up for","לפצות על"],["frequency","תדירות"],["at best","במקרה הטוב"]]}]},"s10c3":{"id":"s10c3","tier":2,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"Cities with more public parks tend to report lower rates of depression among their residents, although researchers have not established whether the parks themselves are responsible for this difference.","o":["Researchers have shown that public parks lower rates of depression, which explains why residents of cities with more parks report being less depressed than others.","Residents of cities with fewer public parks tend to report lower rates of depression, a pattern that researchers have so far been unable to fully explain.","Depression is generally less common in cities that have more public parks, but it remains unclear whether the parks actually cause residents to be less depressed.","Although cities with more public parks have lower rates of depression, researchers are convinced that the parks have nothing to do with their residents' mental health."],"a":2,"ex":"במשפט המקורי יש קשר (יותר פארקים, פחות דיכאון) אבל לא הוכח שהפארקים הם הסיבה. התשובה הנכונה שומרת על זה: «it remains unclear whether the parks actually cause». התשובה הראשונה מציגה את הקשר כהוכחה של סיבה ותוצאה, וזה לא נאמר.","w":[["although","למרות ש..."],["establish","לקבוע, להוכיח"],["be responsible for","להיות הגורם ל..."]]},{"q":"Only a handful of the ancient city's original buildings survived the earthquake intact, yet archaeologists were able to reconstruct much of its layout from the foundations that remained beneath the rubble.","o":["Although very few of the ancient city's original buildings came through the earthquake undamaged, archaeologists managed to recreate a large part of its plan using the foundations left under the ruins.","Most of the ancient city's original buildings survived the earthquake undamaged, so archaeologists could easily reconstruct its layout without having to dig through the rubble to reach the foundations.","Because only a few of the ancient city's buildings survived the earthquake, archaeologists could reconstruct barely any of its layout, even though the foundations beneath the rubble remained.","Archaeologists reconstructed the entire layout of the ancient city from its foundations, and as a result, a handful of its original buildings were restored to the condition they had been in before the earthquake."],"a":0,"ex":"«Only a handful» = רק מעט מאוד, ו-«much of its layout» = חלק גדול מהתוכנית. התשובה הנכונה שומרת על שתי הכמויות. «Most» הופך את «מעט» ל«רוב», ו-«barely any» הופך את «הרבה» ל«כמעט כלום».","w":[["a handful","קומץ, מעט מאוד"],["intact","שלם, ללא פגע"],["yet","ובכל זאת, אך"]]},{"q":"The new vaccine proved highly effective among adults under sixty, but the trial included too few elderly participants to determine whether it offers the same protection to older people.","o":["The trial showed that the new vaccine is highly effective among adults under sixty but offers considerably less protection to older people, who took part in smaller numbers.","The new vaccine proved highly effective among people of all ages, although the trial included fewer elderly participants than the researchers had originally planned to recruit.","Because too many elderly people took part in the trial, researchers were unable to determine how effective the new vaccine is among adults who are younger than sixty.","Although the new vaccine worked very well for adults younger than sixty, too few older participants took part in the trial to show whether it protects them equally well."],"a":3,"ex":"המקור אומר שלגבי המבוגרים פשוט אין מספיק מידע. התשובה הראשונה טוענת שהחיסון מגן עליהם פחות, וזו טענה שלא נאמרה. התשובה השנייה מרחיבה את ההצלחה ל«all ages», וזו טעות בהיקף.","w":[["participant","משתתף"],["determine","לקבוע"],["elderly","קשישים"]]}]},"s10c4":{"id":"s10c4","tier":2,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"Owing to a sharp rise in the cost of imported grain, many small bakeries have been forced to raise their prices, while several others have closed altogether.","o":["Many small bakeries have raised their prices or closed altogether, and as a result, the cost of imported grain has risen sharply over the past several months.","Since imported grain has become much more expensive, a large number of small bakeries have had to charge more, and some have even shut down completely.","In spite of a sharp rise in the cost of imported grain, most small bakeries have managed to keep their prices low, and only a few have closed down.","A sharp rise in the cost of imported grain has forced all small bakeries to raise their prices, and many of them are now considering closing altogether."],"a":1,"ex":"«Owing to» = בשל, עקב: התייקרות הדגן היא הסיבה, והעלאת המחירים והסגירה הן התוצאה. בתשובה הראשונה הסיבה והתוצאה התהפכו. בתשובה האחרונה «many» הפך ל«all», והמאפיות שנסגרו הפכו למאפיות ש«שוקלות» להיסגר.","w":[["owing to","בשל, עקב"],["as a result","כתוצאה מכך"],["in spite of","למרות"]]},{"q":"Far from discouraging further research, the failure of the first experiment led the team to question an assumption that had previously been accepted by almost everyone in the field.","o":["Rather than putting the team off further research, the unsuccessful first experiment caused the researchers to doubt an assumption that nearly all experts in the field had formerly taken for granted.","The failure of the first experiment discouraged the team from carrying out further research, since it showed that an assumption accepted by almost everyone in the field was in fact correct.","Although the first experiment failed, the team continued its research, largely because almost everyone in the field had warned them not to question an assumption that was widely accepted.","The team questioned an assumption accepted by only a few researchers in the field, and this eventually caused the first experiment to fail and all further research to come to a stop."],"a":0,"ex":"«Far from discouraging» = לא רק שלא ריפה את ידיהם, אלא להפך. הכישלון גרם לצוות לפקפק בהנחה מקובלת. «Rather than» שומר על המשמעות הזו. התשובה השנייה הופכת את ההיגיון (הכישלון כן עצר את המחקר), והאחרונה הופכת את «almost everyone» ל«only a few».","w":[["rather than","במקום, ולא"],["far from","רחוק מ..., להפך מ..."],["take for granted","לקבל כמובן מאליו"]]},{"q":"The committee's findings, while by no means conclusive, lend considerable support to the view that the bridge collapsed because of design flaws rather than poor maintenance.","o":["The committee's findings prove beyond any doubt that the bridge collapsed because of design flaws, although poor maintenance may also have played some part in its collapse.","Although the committee's findings are not conclusive, they strongly suggest that the bridge collapsed mainly because it was poorly maintained over time rather than because it was badly designed.","Although they do not settle the matter, the committee's findings strongly back the claim that defects in the bridge's design, and not inadequate upkeep, caused it to collapse.","The committee's findings offer little support to the view that design flaws caused the bridge to collapse, since they are by no means conclusive about its maintenance."],"a":2,"ex":"«by no means conclusive» = בשום אופן לא חד משמעיים, ובכל זאת הממצאים תומכים מאוד בכך שהסיבה היא תכנון לקוי ולא תחזוקה. התשובה הראשונה טוענת «prove beyond any doubt», וזה סותר את «not conclusive». התשובה השנייה הופכת את הסיבה.","w":[["by no means","בשום אופן לא"],["conclusive","חד משמעי, מכריע"],["rather than","במקום, ולא"]]}]},"s10c5":{"id":"s10c5","tier":2,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"Critics argued that the new regulations were merely ___, designed to reassure the public rather than to bring about any real change.","o":["radical","cosmetic","rigorous","retroactive"],"a":1,"ex":"«cosmetic» = שטחי, למראית עין. תקנות שנועדו רק להרגיע את הציבור ולא לשנות באמת הן קוסמטיות. «radical» (קיצוני, יסודי) ו-«rigorous» (קפדני) הם ההפך משינוי שאינו אמיתי.","w":[["cosmetic","שטחי, למראית עין"],["merely","רק, לא יותר מ..."],["reassure","להרגיע"]]},{"q":"The region's economy relies ___ on tourism, so the sudden drop in foreign visitors has had devastating consequences.","o":["seldom","barely","solely","hardly"],"a":2,"ex":"«solely» = אך ורק. אם הכלכלה נשענת רק על תיירות, ירידה בתיירים הרסנית, ולכן «so» הגיוני. «barely» ו-«hardly» (כמעט לא) היו אומרים שהתיירות כמעט לא חשובה, ואז הירידה לא הייתה הרסנית.","w":[["solely","אך ורק, בלעדית"],["barely","בקושי, כמעט לא"],["devastating","הרסני"]]},{"q":"The negotiations reached a ___ when neither side was willing to make any further concessions.","o":["consensus","milestone","prerequisite","deadlock"],"a":3,"ex":"«deadlock» = מבוי סתום. כששני הצדדים מסרבים לוותר, המשא ומתן נתקע. «consensus» (הסכמה כללית) הוא ההפך: כשאף צד לא מוותר, אין הסכמה.","w":[["deadlock","מבוי סתום, קיפאון"],["concession","ויתור"],["consensus","הסכמה רחבה"]]},{"q":"___, the new method is more expensive than the traditional one, but the savings it produces over time more than justify the initial cost.","o":["Admittedly","Consequently","Likewise","Conversely"],"a":0,"ex":"«Admittedly» = יש להודות ש... מודים בחיסרון (השיטה יקרה יותר), ואז ה-«but» מציג את היתרון שגובר עליו. «Consequently» (כתוצאה מכך) לא מתאים, כי אין כאן תוצאה של משהו שנאמר קודם.","w":[["admittedly","יש להודות ש..."],["justify","להצדיק"]]}]},"s11c0":{"id":"s11c0","tier":3,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"Critics dismissed the chief executive's apology as ___, noting that it came only after the scandal had begun to hurt the company's sales.","o":["candid","disingenuous","spontaneous","magnanimous"],"a":1,"ex":"«disingenuous» = לא כן, מעמיד פנים. המבקרים טוענים שההתנצלות הגיעה רק כשהמכירות נפגעו, כלומר היא לא אמיתית. «candid» (גלוי לב) ו-«spontaneous» (ספונטני) הם ההפך ממה שהמשפט רומז.","w":[["disingenuous","לא כן, צבוע"],["dismiss","לבטל, לפטור כלא חשוב"],["candid","גלוי לב"]]},{"q":"The museum will lend the painting to the exhibition ___ it is insured for its full value and kept at a constant temperature throughout the tour.","o":["even though","whereas","on condition that","in case"],"a":2,"ex":"«on condition that» = בתנאי ש. הביטוח והטמפרטורה הם התנאים שבלעדיהם המוזיאון לא ישאיל את הציור. «in case» (למקרה ש) נותן אמצעי זהירות ולא תנאי, ו-«even though» יוצר ויתור שאין לו היגיון כאן.","w":[["on condition that","בתנאי ש..."],["in case","למקרה ש..."]]},{"q":"The once-thriving fishing village has become ___, its harbor silted up and most of its houses standing empty for much of the year.","o":["bustling","affluent","pristine","desolate"],"a":3,"ex":"«desolate» = שומם, עזוב. נמל סתום ובתים ריקים מתארים מקום נטוש. «bustling» (הומה) ו-«affluent» (אמיד) מתאימים לכפר המשגשג של פעם, לא למצבו היום.","w":[["desolate","שומם, נטוש"],["thriving","משגשג"],["bustling","הומה, שוקק"]]},{"q":"The new policy did little to reduce traffic in the city center; ___, by making parking cheaper on the outskirts, it seems to have encouraged even more people to drive.","o":["on the contrary","likewise","accordingly","for instance"],"a":0,"ex":"«on the contrary» = להפך. החלק השני אומר שהמדיניות לא רק שלא הפחיתה תנועה אלא אף הגבירה אותה, וזה ההפך מהמטרה. «accordingly» (לכן) לא מתאים, כי אי ההצלחה להפחית תנועה איננה סיבה לכך שיותר אנשים נוסעים.","w":[["on the contrary","להפך"],["accordingly","בהתאם לכך, לכן"],["outskirts","פאתי העיר"]]}]},"s11c1":{"id":"s11c1","tier":3,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"The professor's argument was so ___ that even students with no background in philosophy could follow each step without difficulty.","o":["convoluted","esoteric","lucid","spurious"],"a":2,"ex":"«lucid» = בהיר, צלול. אם גם מי שלא למד פילוסופיה הבין כל שלב, הטיעון היה ברור. «convoluted» (מסובך) ו-«esoteric» (מובן רק למעטים) הם ההפך.","w":[["lucid","בהיר, צלול"],["convoluted","מסובך, מפותל"],["esoteric","מובן רק ליודעי ח״ן"]]},{"q":"The reform did raise literacy rates in rural areas, ___ far more slowly and at a far higher cost than its architects had promised.","o":["let alone","thereby","not to mention","albeit"],"a":3,"ex":"«albeit» = אם כי. הרפורמה הצליחה, אבל עם הסתייגות: לאט ויקר יותר מהמתוכנן. «not to mention» מוסיף עוד דבר באותו כיוון ולא מסייג, ו-«let alone» בא רק אחרי משפט שלילי.","w":[["albeit","אם כי"],["not to mention","שלא לדבר על"],["let alone","ובטח שלא, קל וחומר"]]},{"q":"Rather than resolving the dispute, the court's ambiguous ruling only served to ___ it, as both sides claimed that the decision supported their position.","o":["alleviate","exacerbate","settle","preclude"],"a":1,"ex":"«exacerbate» = להחמיר. «Rather than resolving» אומר שהפסיקה לא פתרה את הסכסוך אלא עשתה משהו הפוך, ושני הצדדים טוענים לניצחון. «alleviate» (להקל) ו-«settle» (ליישב) הם בדיוק מה שלא קרה.","w":[["exacerbate","להחמיר"],["alleviate","להקל"],["rather than","במקום, ולא"]]},{"q":"___ its modest budget, the documentary attracted a larger audience than any of the big-studio productions released that year.","o":["Notwithstanding","By virtue of","In view of","Owing to"],"a":0,"ex":"«notwithstanding» = על אף, למרות. תקציב צנוע הוא סיבה לצפות להצלחה קטנה, ובכל זאת הסרט הצליח יותר מהפקות גדולות. שלוש האפשרויות האחרות נותנות סיבה, כאילו התקציב הקטן גרם להצלחה.","w":[["notwithstanding","על אף, למרות"],["by virtue of","מתוקף, בזכות"],["owing to","בשל, עקב"]]}]},"s11c2":{"id":"s11c2","tier":3,"type":"rc","title":"When a Language Falls Silent","text":["Of the roughly 7,000 languages spoken in the world today, linguists estimate that close to half may fall out of use by the end of this century. Popular accounts tend to picture such a loss as sudden, as though a language vanished at the moment its last speaker died. In reality, that death is usually only the final step in a process that began generations earlier.","The process typically starts when a community comes under pressure, whether economic, political or social, to adopt a more dominant language. Parents who see that the dominant language opens the way to schooling and employment may stop speaking their ancestral tongue to their children, often out of a sincere wish to spare them disadvantage. Once a single generation grows up without it, the language is in serious danger: it may still be heard among the elderly, but it is no longer being passed on. Linguists call such a language 'moribund' long before its final speaker is gone.","Revival movements have tried to reverse this decline, with uneven results. The case most often cited as a success is Hebrew, which, although it had been preserved for centuries in prayer and scholarship, had not been anyone's everyday language. Within a few decades it acquired millions of native speakers. Yet Hebrew's case is in many respects exceptional: its revivers could draw on an extensive written tradition, and they were building a new society in which a shared language met an urgent practical need.","Most communities attempting revival enjoy neither advantage. Programs in which young children are taught entirely in the threatened language, known as 'language nests', have produced a new generation of speakers among the Maori of New Zealand and in Hawaii. Even there, however, many graduates use the language mainly at school and turn to English at home and with friends. Teaching a language, it seems, is considerably easier than restoring the conditions under which people choose to speak it.","For languages whose last speakers have already died, the goals are necessarily more modest. Recordings, dictionaries and grammars compiled by linguists cannot by themselves bring a language back to life, but they can preserve enough of it for later generations to reclaim, should they so wish. Some scholars argue that this, rather than the number of fluent speakers, is the more realistic measure of success."],"qs":[{"q":"The passage mainly discusses","o":["why Hebrew is a model that every endangered language can follow","how languages decline and how far efforts to revive them have succeeded","the reasons parents prefer to raise their children in a dominant language","the methods linguists use to record languages that have no living speakers"],"a":1,"ex":"הקטע מתאר איך שפה נעלמת (פסקאות 1-2) ומה הצליחו ולא הצליחו מאמצי ההחייאה (פסקאות 3-5). ההורים, העברית והתיעוד הם רק חלקים מהתמונה, והקטע אף אומר שהעברית היא מקרה חריג ולא מודל.","w":[["revive","להחיות"],["decline","דעיכה; לדעוך"],["endangered","בסכנת הכחדה"]]},{"q":"According to the second paragraph, linguists describe a language as 'moribund' when","o":["its last speaker has died","it is used only in prayer and scholarship","children no longer learn it, although some people still speak it","its community is under economic pressure to adopt another language"],"a":2,"ex":"בפסקה 2: כשדור שלם גדל בלי השפה, היא עדיין נשמעת אצל הזקנים אבל כבר לא עוברת הלאה, ואז קוראים לה «moribund», עוד הרבה לפני שהדובר האחרון מת. לכן התשובה הראשונה שגויה, והלחץ הכלכלי הוא רק תחילת התהליך.","w":[["moribund","גוסס, על סף מוות"],["pass on","להעביר הלאה"],["ancestral","של האבות, מסורתי"]]},{"q":"In the third paragraph, the word 'exceptional' could best be replaced by","o":["atypical","outstanding","admirable","unexplained"],"a":0,"ex":"בפסקה 3 «exceptional» = חריג, יוצא דופן במובן של לא מייצג. המשפט מסביר שלעברית היו יתרונות שאין לשפות אחרות. «outstanding» (מצוין) מפתה, אבל הכותב לא משבח כאן את העברית אלא אומר שהמקרה שלה לא טיפוסי.","w":[["exceptional","חריג; יוצא מן הכלל"],["atypical","לא טיפוסי"],["in many respects","במובנים רבים"]]},{"q":"The main purpose of the fourth paragraph is to","o":["argue that language nests are more effective than the methods that were used to revive Hebrew","explain why Maori and Hawaiian are no longer considered endangered","suggest that children should not be taught entirely in a threatened language","show that even relatively successful programs have not fully restored everyday use of a language"],"a":3,"ex":"פסקה 4 מביאה את «language nests» כהצלחה יחסית, ואז אומרת «Even there, however»: הבוגרים מדברים בשפה בעיקר בבית הספר. המטרה היא להראות את הגבול של ההצלחה. הפסקה לא משווה לעברית ולא טוענת שהשפות כבר לא בסכנה.","w":[["threatened","מאוים"],["restore","להשיב, לשקם"],["considerably","במידה ניכרת"]]},{"q":"It can be inferred from the last paragraph that some scholars believe that","o":["recordings and dictionaries are enough to bring a language back to life","documenting a language is pointless once its last speakers have died","an effort may count as successful even if it produces few fluent speakers","the number of fluent speakers is the only true measure of a revival's success"],"a":2,"ex":"המשפט האחרון: יש חוקרים שחושבים ששימור השפה לדורות הבאים, «rather than the number of fluent speakers», הוא מדד ההצלחה הריאלי. כלומר אפשר להצליח גם בלי הרבה דוברים. התשובה הראשונה סותרת את «cannot by themselves bring a language back to life».","w":[["reclaim","לדרוש בחזרה, להשיב לעצמו"],["compile","לחבר, לאסוף לכדי"],["measure","מדד; למדוד"]]}]},"s11c3":{"id":"s11c3","tier":3,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"Only after the old bridge had partially collapsed did the city council agree to fund the repairs that engineers had been urging for more than a decade.","o":["The city council agreed to pay for the repairs that engineers had long demanded, so the old bridge, which had been at risk for years, never collapsed.","Although engineers had pressed for repairs for over ten years, the council did not approve the money for them until part of the old bridge had actually collapsed.","Engineers began urging the city council to fund repairs only after part of the old bridge had collapsed, and the council approved the money ten years later.","For more than a decade, the council paid for repairs to the old bridge, but engineers warned that the work could not prevent it from partly collapsing."],"a":1,"ex":"«Only after... did» = רק אחרי ש... המועצה הסכימה לממן את התיקון רק אחרי שהגשר קרס חלקית, למרות שהמהנדסים דרשו זאת יותר מעשור. בתשובה השלישית המהנדסים התחילו לדרוש רק אחרי הקריסה, וזה הפוך מהמקור.","w":[["only after","רק לאחר ש..."],["urge","לדחוק, להפציר"],["although","למרות ש..."]]},{"q":"But for the timely intervention of a handful of volunteers, the archive of rare manuscripts, which the flood had left soaked and scattered across the library floor, would almost certainly have been lost.","o":["The flood scattered the rare manuscripts across the library floor, and although a few volunteers intervened in time, the archive was almost entirely lost.","A few volunteers had moved the rare manuscripts before the flood arrived, so the archive was neither soaked nor scattered across the library floor.","Because a handful of volunteers reacted too slowly, the flood soaked the archive of rare manuscripts and scattered it across the library floor.","The rare manuscripts, soaked and scattered by the flood, would probably have been destroyed had a few volunteers not stepped in just in time."],"a":3,"ex":"«but for» = אלמלא. אלמלא המתנדבים, הארכיון היה אובד, כלומר בזכותם הוא ניצל. התשובה הנכונה משתמשת ב-«had... not» באותה משמעות. בתשובה הראשונה הארכיון אבד, ובשנייה כתבי היד בכלל לא נרטבו, בניגוד למקור.","w":[["but for","אלמלא, לולא"],["timely","בזמן, בעיתוי הנכון"],["intervention","התערבות"]]},{"q":"Far from slowing the rumor's spread, the company's repeated denials appear to have lent it credibility, since many readers assumed that no one would deny a story so vigorously unless it were true.","o":["The company's repeated denials seem to have made the rumor more believable, because many readers took such strong denials as a sign that the story was true.","The company's repeated denials slowed the spread of the rumor, since many readers assumed that a company would not deny a story so firmly unless it were false.","Many readers already believed the rumor before the company denied it, so its repeated denials had no effect at all on how widely the story spread.","Although the company's repeated denials made the rumor seem more credible to some, few readers believed that a story denied so strongly could actually be true."],"a":0,"ex":"«Far from slowing» = רחוק מלהאט, כלומר ההכחשות לא האטו את השמועה אלא חיזקו אותה, כי קוראים הניחו שלא מכחישים כך סיפור אלא אם הוא נכון. התשובה השנייה הופכת את התוצאה, והרביעית אומרת שמעטים האמינו, בסתירה למקור.","w":[["far from","רחוק מ..., ממש לא"],["credibility","אמינות"],["unless","אלא אם כן"]]}]},"s11c4":{"id":"s11c4","tier":3,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"While few economists now dispute that the tariff contributed to the recession, there remains considerable disagreement over whether it was the decisive cause or merely one factor among many.","o":["Most economists now agree that the tariff was the main cause of the recession, though a few still argue that it was only one of several contributing factors.","Few economists now believe that the tariff played any part in the recession, although they still disagree about which of the other factors was the decisive one.","Most economists now accept that the tariff played some part in the recession, but they still differ on whether it was the main cause or one of several.","Economists still disagree about whether the tariff played any part at all in the recession, but most of them accept that it was not the decisive cause."],"a":2,"ex":"«few dispute that» = מעטים חולקים על כך, כלומר רובם מסכימים שהמכס תרם למיתון. המחלוקת היא רק האם הוא היה הסיבה המכרעת. בתשובה הראשונה רובם כבר מסכימים שהוא הסיבה העיקרית, וזו בדיוק הנקודה שעדיין שנויה במחלוקת.","w":[["while","בעוד ש... (ניגוד)"],["dispute","לחלוק על, לערער"],["merely","רק, לא יותר מ..."]]},{"q":"Unless the coral reefs are given at least a decade free from rising water temperatures, scientists warn, even the most ambitious replanting programs will be unable to restore them to their former diversity.","o":["Scientists warn that ambitious replanting programs will restore the coral reefs to their former diversity within a decade, even if water temperatures continue to rise.","According to scientists, replanting programs, however ambitious, can bring back the reefs' former diversity only if water temperatures stop rising for at least ten years.","Scientists warn that rising water temperatures have already damaged the coral reefs so badly that no replanting program could ever restore their former diversity.","According to scientists, the reefs will regain their former diversity after ten years of stable water temperatures, provided that no replanting program interferes with them."],"a":1,"ex":"«unless» = אלא אם כן. בלי עשור של טמפרטורות יציבות, שום תוכנית לא תצליח; התשובה הנכונה אומרת זאת עם «only if» (רק אם). בתשובה השלישית אין בכלל סיכוי, אבל המקור משאיר תנאי שבו ההצלחה אפשרית.","w":[["unless","אלא אם כן"],["only if","רק אם"],["diversity","מגוון"]]},{"q":"The new screening test is no more accurate than the one it replaced; its advantage lies rather in the fact that a nurse can perform it in minutes, without a specialist laboratory.","o":["The new screening test is more accurate than the old one and, unlike it, can be carried out in a few minutes by a nurse rather than in a specialist laboratory.","Although the new screening test is quicker than the old one, it is also less accurate, since it is performed by a nurse rather than in a specialist laboratory.","The new screening test is no more accurate than the old one and, like it, still requires a specialist laboratory, although a nurse can now perform part of it.","What makes the new screening test better than the old one is not greater accuracy but the fact that a nurse can do it quickly, without a specialist laboratory."],"a":3,"ex":"«no more accurate than» = לא מדויק יותר (מדויק באותה מידה). היתרון היחיד: אחות מבצעת אותה בדקות בלי מעבדה. בתשובה הראשונה הבדיקה מדויקת יותר, ובשנייה פחות מדויקת, ושתיהן משנות את נקודת הדיוק.","w":[["no more... than","לא יותר... מ..."],["rather than","במקום, ולא"],["instead of","במקום (+שם עצם / ing)"]]}]},"s11c5":{"id":"s11c5","tier":3,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"Wary of appearing to take sides, the mediator remained scrupulously ___ throughout the negotiations, refusing even to comment on either party's proposals.","o":["impartial","partisan","vehement","gullible"],"a":0,"ex":"«impartial» = לא משוחד, ניטרלי. המתווך נזהר מלהיראות כמי שבוחר צד, ולכן לא הגיב על אף הצעה. «partisan» (מצדד בצד אחד) הוא בדיוק ההפך.","w":[["impartial","ניטרלי, לא משוחד"],["wary","זהיר, חושש"],["partisan","מפלגתי, מצדד"]]},{"q":"Few of the trainees could solve even the basic problems in the manual, ___ the advanced ones that the examiners had added at the end.","o":["apart from","such as","let alone","instead of"],"a":2,"ex":"«let alone» = ובטח שלא. אם מעטים פתרו אפילו את הבעיות הבסיסיות, ודאי שלא פתרו את המתקדמות. «apart from» (חוץ מ) היה אומר שהמתקדמות דווקא נפתרו, וזה לא הגיוני.","w":[["let alone","ובטח שלא, קל וחומר"],["apart from","חוץ מ...; מלבד"],["few","מעט (כמעט אין)"]]},{"q":"The ambassador's ___ remarks, made off the record at a private dinner, caused a diplomatic incident that took both governments months to repair.","o":["prudent","indiscreet","tactful","guarded"],"a":1,"ex":"«indiscreet» = לא זהיר, חסר טקט בדיבור. דברים שגרמו לתקרית דיפלומטית ארוכה לא היו זהירים. «prudent», «tactful» ו-«guarded» כולן אומרות זהירות, ההפך מהתוצאה.","w":[["indiscreet","לא זהיר בדיבור, פטפטן"],["prudent","נבון, זהיר"],["tactful","בעל טקט"]]},{"q":"The study was small and lasted only six weeks; its results, ___, are consistent with those of several much larger and longer trials.","o":["all the same","consequently","that is","similarly"],"a":0,"ex":"«all the same» = בכל זאת. המחקר קטן וקצר (חולשה), ובכל זאת התוצאות שלו תואמות מחקרים גדולים. «consequently» (כתוצאה מכך) לא מתאים, כי היותו קטן איננה הסיבה להתאמה.","w":[["all the same","בכל זאת"],["consequently","כתוצאה מכך, לפיכך"],["consistent with","תואם, עולה בקנה אחד עם"]]}]},"s12c0":{"id":"s12c0","tier":3,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"The new regulations were so ___ that judges in different courts reached opposite conclusions about what they actually required.","o":["ambiguous","stringent","explicit","redundant"],"a":0,"ex":"«Ambiguous» = דו-משמעי, לא ברור. שופטים הגיעו למסקנות הפוכות לגבי מה התקנות דורשות, כלומר אפשר לפרש אותן ביותר מדרך אחת. «explicit» (מפורש) אומרת בדיוק את ההפך, ו-«stringent» (מחמיר) לא מסבירה למה הפרשנויות שונות.","w":[["ambiguous","דו-משמעי, עמום"],["explicit","מפורש"],["stringent","מחמיר, נוקשה"]]},{"q":"The museum agreed to lend the painting to the exhibition ___ it would be kept behind glass at a constant temperature.","o":["even though","on condition that","whereas","lest"],"a":1,"ex":"«On condition that» = בתנאי ש.... המוזיאון הסכים להשאיל את הציור, ובתנאי שישמרו עליו מאחורי זכוכית. «lest» (כדי שלא) היה אומר שהמוזיאון רצה למנוע את השמירה מאחורי זכוכית, וזה לא הגיוני.","w":[["on condition that","בתנאי ש..."],["lest","פן, שמא, כדי שלא"]]},{"q":"Critics dismissed the minister's apology as ___, pointing out that he had repeated the very same remarks in a radio interview the following day.","o":["heartfelt","candid","disingenuous","belated"],"a":2,"ex":"«Disingenuous» = לא כן, מתחסד. השר חזר על אותם דברים כבר למחרת, ולכן המבקרים טענו שההתנצלות לא הייתה אמיתית. «heartfelt» (מכל הלב) אומרת ההפך, ו-«belated» (מאוחר מדי) עוסקת בתזמון, והמשפט לא מדבר על איחור.","w":[["disingenuous","לא כן, צבוע"],["dismiss","לבטל, לפטור כלא חשוב"],["belated","מאוחר, שבא באיחור"]]},{"q":"The reforms did produce a rise in literacy, ___ a far more modest one than their architects had promised.","o":["hence","namely","likewise","albeit"],"a":3,"ex":"«Albeit» = אם כי. הרפורמות אכן העלו את האוריינות, אבל העלייה הייתה קטנה בהרבה ממה שהובטח: זו הסתייגות. «namely» (כלומר) מפרטת ולא מסתייגת, ו-«hence» (לכן) יוצרת קשר של תוצאה שאין כאן.","w":[["albeit","אם כי"],["namely","כלומר, דהיינו"],["modest","צנוע, מתון"]]}]},"s12c1":{"id":"s12c1","tier":3,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"Years without rain had left the land so ___ that even the hardiest crops failed to take root.","o":["fertile","lush","arid","saturated"],"a":2,"ex":"«Arid» = צחיח, יבש מאוד. שנים בלי גשם השאירו את האדמה יבשה, ולכן אפילו הגידולים העמידים לא נקלטו. «fertile» (פורה) ו-«lush» (שופע צמחייה) אומרות ההפך, ו-«saturated» (רווי במים) לא מתאימה לשנים בלי גשם.","w":[["arid","צחיח, יבש"],["fertile","פורה"],["saturated","רווי"]]},{"q":"___ the board's repeated assurances, many employees remained convinced that further layoffs were imminent.","o":["Owing to","In view of","By virtue of","Notwithstanding"],"a":3,"ex":"«Notwithstanding» = על אף, למרות. ההנהלה הרגיעה שוב ושוב, ובכל זאת העובדים היו משוכנעים שיהיו פיטורים. שלוש האפשרויות האחרות מציינות סיבה (בגלל, לאור), וההבטחות לא יכולות להיות הסיבה לחשש מפיטורים.","w":[["notwithstanding","על אף, למרות"],["owing to","בשל, עקב"],["imminent","קרוב, עומד לקרות"]]},{"q":"The professor's lectures were notoriously ___: a single point could take her forty minutes to make, with countless digressions along the way.","o":["verbose","concise","succinct","coherent"],"a":0,"ex":"«Verbose» = מילולי מדי, ארכני. נקודה אחת לקחה ארבעים דקות עם אינספור סטיות מהנושא. «concise» ו-«succinct» פירושן תמציתי, בדיוק ההפך, ו-«coherent» (קוהרנטי, מסודר) לא מתיישבת עם הסטיות הרבות.","w":[["verbose","ארכני, מכביר מילים"],["succinct","תמציתי"],["digression","סטייה מהנושא"]]},{"q":"Few historians accept the chronicle's account of the battle, ___ its author was born nearly a century after the events he describes.","o":["whereas","seeing that","so that","unless"],"a":1,"ex":"«Seeing that» = מאחר ש..., הואיל ו.... המחבר נולד מאה שנה אחרי הקרב, וזו הסיבה שהיסטוריונים לא סומכים על התיאור. «whereas» מציינת ניגוד, ואין ניגוד בין שני החלקים.","w":[["seeing that","מאחר ש..., הואיל ו..."],["whereas","בעוד ש..., ואילו"],["account","תיאור, דיווח"]]}]},"s12c2":{"id":"s12c2","tier":3,"type":"rc","title":"The Trouble with Sugar Pills","text":["When a patient feels better after swallowing a pill that contains nothing but sugar, the improvement is real in the sense that matters most: the pain has eased or the nausea has passed. This phenomenon, known as the placebo effect, has been documented for over a century, yet it remains one of the most puzzling features of modern medicine. For those who design clinical trials, it is also one of the most troublesome.","The effect appears to arise largely from expectation. A patient who believes that a treatment will work tends to notice signs of improvement and to describe symptoms as less severe. Brain-imaging studies suggest, however, that more than mere reporting is involved: in some patients, an inert pill triggers the release of the body's own pain-relieving chemicals. The details matter, too. Two pills often outperform one, injections tend to outperform pills, and a dummy capsule presented as expensive may relieve more pain than an identical one described as cheap.","It is precisely this power that complicates the testing of new drugs. To show that a medicine works, researchers cannot simply compare patients who take it with patients who receive nothing, since the first group would improve partly because they expect to. Instead, trials give one group the real drug and another an identical-looking placebo, and neither the patients nor their doctors are told who is receiving which. Only if the drug clearly outperforms the dummy can it be considered effective.","Yet even this careful design has weaknesses. Many genuine drugs cause noticeable side effects, which allow participants to guess that they belong to the treatment group; their heightened expectations may then inflate the apparent benefit of the drug. Moreover, placebo responses in certain fields, most notably pain and depression, have grown stronger over recent decades. As a result, several promising compounds have failed not because they were useless but because the placebo did almost as well.","Some researchers argue that the placebo effect should be viewed less as an obstacle than as a resource. If expectation alone can ease suffering, doctors might learn to harness it deliberately, for instance by describing treatments in ways that build confidence. Such proposals, however, raise ethical questions of their own, since deceiving patients, even with good intentions, could undermine the trust on which medicine depends."],"qs":[{"q":"The passage is mainly concerned with","o":["the history of the placebo effect from the time it was first documented over a century ago","how the placebo effect works and why it makes the testing of new drugs difficult","the ethical problems raised by giving patients pills that contain only sugar","why drugs for pain and depression have become less effective than they once were"],"a":1,"ex":"הקטע מסביר מה גורם לאפקט הפלצבו (פסקה 2) ולמה הוא מסבך ניסויים קליניים (פסקאות 3-4). השאלות האתיות מופיעות רק בפסקה האחרונה, ולגבי כאב ודיכאון הקטע אומר שהפלצבו התחזק, לא שהתרופות נחלשו.","w":[["be concerned with","לעסוק ב..."],["clinical trial","ניסוי קליני"]]},{"q":"According to the second paragraph, which of the following is true?","o":["A placebo helps only those patients who have been told in advance that the pill is inert.","Brain-imaging studies show that the effect exists only in what patients report.","A single pill usually relieves more pain than two pills do.","The form and the presented price of a dummy treatment can affect how well it works."],"a":3,"ex":"בפסקה 2 כתוב ששתי גלולות עובדות טוב יותר מאחת, זריקה טוב יותר מגלולה, וגלולה «יקרה» מקלה יותר מגלולה זהה «זולה». התשובה על סריקות המוח הופכת את מה שנאמר: הן מראות שמדובר ביותר מדיווח בלבד.","w":[["inert","לא פעיל, חסר השפעה"],["outperform","להצליח יותר מ..."]]},{"q":"In the third paragraph, the word 'they' (in 'because they expect to') refers to","o":["patients who take the new medicine","patients who receive nothing","researchers","the doctors who treat these patients"],"a":0,"ex":"«The first group would improve partly because they expect to»: הקבוצה הראשונה היא המטופלים שלוקחים את התרופה, והם משתפרים בין היתר כי הם מצפים להשתפר. «patients who receive nothing» מפתה, אבל זו הקבוצה השנייה, שאין לה ציפייה כזו.","w":[["refer to","להתייחס ל..."],["since","מכיוון ש..."]]},{"q":"The main purpose of the fourth paragraph is to","o":["argue that placebo-controlled trials should be abandoned","describe the methods that researchers use to prevent participants from guessing which group they are in","explain why even a carefully designed trial may fail to reveal a drug's true value","show that drugs with side effects are generally more effective than other drugs"],"a":2,"ex":"הפסקה פותחת ב«Yet even this careful design has weaknesses» ומסבירה שתופעות לוואי והתחזקות הפלצבו גורמות לתרופות טובות להיכשל. היא לא מציעה לוותר על הניסויים, ולא מתארת איך מונעים מהמשתתפים לנחש, אלא להפך.","w":[["yet","ובכל זאת, אך"],["as a result","כתוצאה מכך"],["inflate","לנפח, להגזים"]]},{"q":"According to the last paragraph, proposals to make deliberate use of the placebo effect are problematic because","o":["the placebo effect is too weak to relieve real suffering","most doctors lack the training to describe treatments clearly","they would make it impossible to conduct clinical trials","they may involve misleading patients, which could damage trust in medicine"],"a":3,"ex":"בפסקה האחרונה כתוב שהצעות כאלה מעלות שאלות אתיות, כי הטעיה של מטופלים, גם בכוונה טובה, עלולה לפגוע באמון שהרפואה נשענת עליו. האפשרות הראשונה סותרת את הקטע, שאומר שציפייה לבדה יכולה להקל על סבל.","w":[["harness","לרתום, לנצל"],["deceive","להונות, להטעות"],["undermine","לערער, לחתור תחת"]]}]},"s12c3":{"id":"s12c3","tier":3,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"Were it not for the generous grants it received from private foundations during its first decade, the orchestra would almost certainly have been forced to disband long before it gained international recognition.","o":["Although private foundations supported the orchestra generously throughout its first ten years, it was still forced to disband long before it could gain international recognition.","The orchestra gained international recognition during its first ten years, and this success persuaded private foundations to give it the generous grants it needed to survive.","The orchestra probably managed to survive long enough to gain international recognition only because private foundations supported it generously throughout its first ten years.","The orchestra probably managed to survive long enough to gain international recognition even though private foundations refused to support it during its first ten years."],"a":2,"ex":"«Were it not for» = אלמלא. בלי המענקים התזמורת הייתה כמעט בוודאות מתפרקת, כלומר היא שרדה בזכותם. בתשובה הראשונה התזמורת התפרקה בכל זאת, ובשנייה סיבה ותוצאה מתהפכות (ההכרה הביאה את המענקים).","w":[["but for","אלמלא, לולא"],["were it not for","אלמלא"],["disband","להתפרק, להתפזר"]]},{"q":"No sooner had the archaeologists begun excavating the site than heavy rains flooded the trenches, delaying the project by several months and destroying a number of fragile artifacts that had not yet been recorded.","o":["Almost immediately after the archaeologists started digging at the site, heavy rains flooded the trenches, setting the project back by months and ruining several delicate finds that were still undocumented.","The archaeologists started digging at the site immediately after heavy rains had flooded the area, which set the project back by months and ruined several delicate finds that were still undocumented.","Almost immediately after the archaeologists started digging at the site, heavy rains flooded the trenches and set the project back by months, although every delicate find there had already been documented.","The archaeologists' careless digging at the site, rather than the heavy rains that followed it, set the project back by months and ruined several delicate finds that were still undocumented."],"a":0,"ex":"«No sooner... than» = רק... וכבר, מיד אחרי ש.... החפירה התחילה, ומיד אחריה הגשמים הציפו, עיכבו והרסו ממצאים שלא תועדו. בתשובה השנייה סדר האירועים הפוך (הגשם קודם), בשלישית כל הממצאים כבר תועדו, וברביעית הנזק נגרם מהחפירה ולא מהגשם.","w":[["no sooner... than","רק... וכבר, מיד אחרי ש..."],["as soon as","ברגע ש..., מיד כש..."],["excavate","לחפור (חפירה ארכיאולוגית)"]]},{"q":"Much as the committee admired the originality of the proposal, it could not recommend funding a project whose costs had been so poorly estimated and whose benefits remained largely speculative.","o":["Because the committee was greatly impressed by how original the proposal was, it recommended funding the project, even though its costs were badly estimated and its benefits mostly uncertain.","Although the committee was greatly impressed by how original the proposal was, it refused to recommend funding the project, since its costs, though carefully estimated, were too high for its benefits.","Although the committee had serious doubts about how original the proposal was, it refused to recommend funding the project mainly because its costs were badly estimated and its benefits mostly uncertain.","Although the committee was greatly impressed by how original the proposal was, it refused to recommend funding the project, since its costs were badly estimated and its benefits mostly uncertain."],"a":3,"ex":"«Much as» = עד כמה ש..., למרות ש.... הוועדה העריכה מאוד את המקוריות, ובכל זאת לא המליצה, כי העלויות הוערכו גרוע והתועלת ספקולטיבית. בראשונה הוועדה המליצה, בשנייה העלויות הוערכו בקפידה, ובשלישית הוועדה פקפקה במקוריות.","w":[["although","למרות ש..."],["much as","עד כמה ש..., למרות ש..."],["speculative","ספקולטיבי, השערתי"]]}]},"s12c4":{"id":"s12c4","tier":3,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"It was not until the late nineteenth century, when improved microscopes revealed that many diseases were caused by microorganisms, that surgeons began routinely washing their hands and sterilizing their instruments before operating.","o":["Surgeons had been routinely washing their hands and sterilizing their instruments long before better microscopes showed, in the late nineteenth century, that microorganisms were responsible for many diseases.","Surgeons started to wash their hands and sterilize their instruments as a matter of routine only after better microscopes showed, in the late nineteenth century, that microorganisms caused many diseases.","In the late nineteenth century, surgeons who routinely washed their hands and sterilized their instruments helped to improve microscopes, which then showed that microorganisms caused many diseases.","Surgeons started to wash their hands and sterilize their instruments as a matter of routine only after better microscopes showed, in the late nineteenth century, that microorganisms caused all diseases."],"a":1,"ex":"«It was not until X that Y» = רק ב-X התחיל Y. המנתחים התחילו לשטוף ידיים ולעקר רק אחרי שהמיקרוסקופים הראו שמיקרואורגניזמים גורמים למחלות רבות. הראשונה הופכת את הזמן (הרבה לפני), השלישית הופכת סיבה ותוצאה, והרביעית משנה «many» ל-«all».","w":[["until","עד ש..."],["after","אחרי"],["routinely","באופן קבוע, כשגרה"]]},{"q":"Such was the shortage of paper in the besieged city that its only remaining newspaper managed to keep appearing solely by printing each edition on the back of old wallpaper.","o":["Paper had become so scarce in the besieged city that the one newspaper still in operation stopped appearing altogether, even though old wallpaper could have been used instead.","Although paper was plentiful in the besieged city, the one newspaper still in operation chose to print each edition on the reverse side of old wallpaper in order to save money.","Paper had become so scarce in the besieged city that the one newspaper still in operation could go on being published only because it used the reverse side of old wallpaper.","Paper had become so scarce in the besieged city that several newspapers could go on being published only because they used the reverse side of old wallpaper."],"a":2,"ex":"«Such was X that» = כזה היה X ש..., כלומר המחסור היה כל כך גדול ש.... העיתון היחיד שנשאר המשיך לצאת רק בזכות הדפסה על גב טפטים ישנים. בראשונה העיתון הפסיק לצאת, בשנייה לא היה מחסור בנייר, וברביעית מדובר בכמה עיתונים ולא בעיתון אחד.","w":[["such... that","כזה... ש..."],["so... that","כל כך... ש..."],["solely","אך ורק, בלעדית"]]},{"q":"Contrary to what its critics had predicted, the ban on single-use plastic bags did not drive shoppers away from local supermarkets; if anything, sales rose slightly in the months after it took effect.","o":["Critics had expected the ban on single-use plastic bags to drive shoppers away from local supermarkets, but in fact sales went up a little in the months following its introduction.","As its critics had predicted, the ban on single-use plastic bags drove shoppers away from local supermarkets, and sales fell a little in the months following its introduction.","Critics had expected the ban on single-use plastic bags to drive shoppers away from local supermarkets, and although they were wrong, sales did not change at all after its introduction.","Critics had expected the ban on single-use plastic bags to increase sales at local supermarkets, but in fact shoppers stayed away from them in the months following its introduction."],"a":0,"ex":"«Contrary to» = בניגוד ל.... המבקרים חזו שהקונים יברחו, אבל זה לא קרה, ואם כבר, המכירות עלו מעט. «if anything» = אם כבר, דווקא. השנייה מאשרת את התחזית, השלישית אומרת שהמכירות לא השתנו בכלל, והרביעית מחליפה בין התחזית לתוצאה.","w":[["in fact","למעשה, בעצם"],["contrary to","בניגוד ל..."],["if anything","אם כבר, דווקא"]]}]},"s12c5":{"id":"s12c5","tier":3,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"The witness's account was ___ by security footage that showed her leaving the building at exactly the time she had stated.","o":["contradicted","fabricated","undermined","corroborated"],"a":3,"ex":"«Corroborate» = לאשש, לחזק בראיה. המצלמה הראתה אותה יוצאת בדיוק בשעה שאמרה, ולכן הסרטון חיזק את העדות. «contradicted» ו-«undermined» (סתר, ערער) אומרות ההפך.","w":[["corroborate","לאשש, לחזק"],["undermine","לערער"],["fabricate","לבדות, לזייף"]]},{"q":"The two parties could not even agree on a date for their next meeting, ___ on the substance of the proposed reforms.","o":["as well as","rather than","let alone","apart from"],"a":2,"ex":"«Let alone» = ובטח שלא, קל וחומר. אם הצדדים לא הצליחו להסכים אפילו על תאריך, בטח שלא יסכימו על תוכן הרפורמות. «as well as» (וגם) לא מתאימה למבנה השלילי של «could not even».","w":[["let alone","ובטח שלא, קל וחומר"],["substance","מהות, תוכן"]]},{"q":"Rather than resolving the dispute, the court's ruling only served to ___ it, prompting both sides to file new lawsuits within days.","o":["settle","exacerbate","defuse","mitigate"],"a":1,"ex":"«Exacerbate» = להחריף, להחמיר. במקום לפתור את הסכסוך, פסק הדין גרם לתביעות חדשות, כלומר החריף אותו. «settle», «defuse» ו-«mitigate» פירושן ליישב, לנטרל ולהקל, כולן ההפך.","w":[["exacerbate","להחריף, להחמיר"],["mitigate","להקל, למתן"],["defuse","לנטרל, להרגיע"]]},{"q":"Doctors are urged to prescribe antibiotics sparingly; ___, bacteria will continue to develop resistance to them at an alarming rate.","o":["otherwise","accordingly","similarly","in particular"],"a":0,"ex":"«Otherwise» = אחרת. אם הרופאים לא ירשמו אנטיביוטיקה בחסכנות, החיידקים ימשיכו לפתח עמידות. «accordingly» (בהתאם לכך) היה אומר שהעמידות נובעת מהרישום החסכוני, וזה הפוך מההיגיון.","w":[["otherwise","אחרת"],["accordingly","בהתאם לכך, לכן"],["sparingly","בחסכנות, במשורה"]]}]},"s2c0":{"id":"s2c0","tier":0,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"Many students are ___ to ask questions in class because they are afraid of looking foolish.","o":["reluctant","eager","proud","certain"],"a":0,"ex":"«Reluctant» = לא ששׂ, מהסס. הסיבה (הם מפחדים להיראות טיפשים) מסבירה למה הם לא רוצים לשאול. «Eager» (להוט) הוא ההפך ולא מתאים לפחד.","w":[["reluctant","מסרב, לא ששׂ"],["eager","להוט"],["because","כי, מפני ש..."]]},{"q":"Tom prefers quiet mornings, ___ his sister enjoys loud music as soon as she wakes up.","o":["so that","whereas","as a result","because"],"a":1,"ex":"«Whereas» = ואילו. משווים בין שני אנשים שונים: טום אוהב שקט, ואילו אחותו אוהבת מוזיקה רועשת. «Because» היה אומר שהמוזיקה שלה היא הסיבה שהוא אוהב שקט, וזה לא מה שהמשפט אומר.","w":[["whereas","בעוד ש..., ואילו"],["as soon as","ברגע ש..., מיד כש..."]]},{"q":"The number of people who smoke has ___ steadily over the last twenty years, thanks to strong public health campaigns.","o":["increased","doubled","declined","appeared"],"a":2,"ex":"«Declined» = ירד. קמפיינים לבריאות הציבור אמורים להוריד את מספר המעשנים, ו«thanks to» (בזכות) מראה שזו תוצאה טובה. «Increased» ו«doubled» (עלה, הכפיל את עצמו) הם תוצאה רעה, ולא מתאימים ל«בזכות».","w":[["decline","לרדת, לפחות"],["thanks to","הודות ל..., בזכות"],["steadily","בהתמדה, בהדרגה"]]},{"q":"You should save your work every few minutes; ___, you may lose everything if the computer crashes.","o":["moreover","similarly","for instance","otherwise"],"a":3,"ex":"«Otherwise» = אחרת. אם לא תשמור, תאבד הכול. החלק השני מתאר מה יקרה אם לא נעשה את מה שבחלק הראשון. «Moreover» (יתרה מזאת) רק מוסיף מידע ולא מתאים לאזהרה.","w":[["otherwise","אחרת"],["moreover","יתרה מזאת"]]}]},"s2c1":{"id":"s2c1","tier":0,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"The museum staff check the temperature in each room every day to ___ that the old paintings are not damaged.","o":["doubt","ensure","forget","deny"],"a":1,"ex":"«Ensure» = לוודא, להבטיח. הצוות בודק את הטמפרטורה כדי לוודא שהציורים לא ייפגעו. «Doubt» (לפקפק) ו«deny» (להכחיש) לא מסבירים למה בודקים כל יום.","w":[["ensure","לוודא, להבטיח"],["damage","לגרום נזק"]]},{"q":"___ the long delay at the airport, the passengers remained calm and polite.","o":["Despite","Because of","Instead of","In addition to"],"a":0,"ex":"«Despite» = למרות. עיכוב ארוך בדרך כלל מעצבן, ובכל זאת הנוסעים נשארו רגועים: זה ניגוד. «Because of» היה אומר שהעיכוב גרם להם להיות רגועים, וזה לא הגיוני.","w":[["despite","למרות (+שם עצם)"],["because of","בגלל (+שם עצם)"],["remain","להישאר"]]},{"q":"Snow is ___ in this part of the country; most people who live here have seen it only once or twice in their lives.","o":["common","heavy","welcome","rare"],"a":3,"ex":"«Rare» = נדיר. אם רוב התושבים ראו שלג רק פעם או פעמיים, השלג נדיר שם. «Common» (נפוץ) ו«heavy» (כבד) סותרים את החלק השני של המשפט.","w":[["rare","נדיר"],["common","נפוץ"]]},{"q":"You may borrow my car this weekend, ___ you return it with a full tank of gas.","o":["even though","whereas","provided that","so that"],"a":2,"ex":"«Provided that» = בתנאי ש. מותר לקחת את הרכב בתנאי שתחזיר אותו עם מיכל מלא. «Even though» (אף על פי ש) מראה ניגוד, ואין כאן ניגוד אלא תנאי.","w":[["provided that","בתנאי ש..."],["even though","אף על פי ש..."]]}]},"s2c2":{"id":"s2c2","tier":0,"type":"rc","title":"From Private Shelves to Public Spaces","text":["For most of history, books were rare and expensive. Before the invention of the printing press, each copy had to be written by hand, a process that could take months. As a result, collections of books belonged mainly to kings, religious institutions and wealthy families. Ordinary people were seldom allowed to enter these collections, and many of them could not read in any case.","This situation began to change in the nineteenth century. As cities grew and more children attended school, reformers argued that knowledge should not be limited to the rich. They believed that a free library would help workers improve themselves and become better citizens. In the middle of the century, Britain passed a law that allowed towns to use public money to open libraries, and the United States soon followed. Some officials were reluctant to spend tax money on books, but the idea gradually spread.","For about a hundred years, the main role of the public library was simple: to lend books and to provide a quiet place to read. In the late twentieth century, however, this role was challenged. Television, and later the internet, gave people new ways to find information and entertainment. Many experts predicted that the number of visitors would decline and that libraries would eventually disappear.","That prediction has not come true. Instead, libraries have changed their role. Today, many of them offer free internet access, classes in computer skills and help for people who are looking for work. In addition, they serve as meeting places for local groups and as safe spaces for children after school. Whereas the early library was mainly a storehouse of books, the modern library is closer to a community center. Its goal, however, remains the same: to ensure that everyone, whatever their income, has access to knowledge."],"qs":[{"q":"The passage mainly discusses","o":["why the printing press made books cheaper","why the internet will soon replace public libraries","how public libraries began and how their role has changed over time","the differences between libraries in Britain and the United States"],"a":2,"ex":"הקטע עובר מההיסטוריה (ספרים נדירים, ספריות ציבוריות במאה ה-19) אל השינוי בתפקיד הספרייה היום. האפשרות על האינטרנט סותרת את הפסקה האחרונה, שאומרת שהתחזית לא התגשמה.","w":[["role","תפקיד"],["mainly","בעיקר"]]},{"q":"According to the first paragraph, collections of books belonged mainly to the rich because","o":["books were copied slowly by hand and were therefore expensive","the law did not allow ordinary people to buy books","religious institutions refused to share their books","most ordinary people preferred to listen to stories"],"a":0,"ex":"בפסקה 1: כל עותק נכתב ביד ולקח חודשים, ולכן «As a result» הספרים היו של מלכים ועשירים. אין בפסקה שום חוק שאסר לקנות ספרים.","w":[["as a result","כתוצאה מכך"],["wealthy","עשיר"],["seldom","לעיתים רחוקות"]]},{"q":"In the second paragraph, the word 'They' (in 'They believed that...') refers to","o":["cities","children","workers","reformers"],"a":3,"ex":"המשפט הקודם אומר ש«reformers» (אנשי רפורמה) טענו שידע לא צריך להיות רק לעשירים, והם אלה ש«האמינו» שספרייה חינמית תעזור לפועלים. «Workers» מופיעים באותו משפט, אבל הם מי שעוזרים לו, לא מי שמאמין.","w":[["reformer","מתקן חברתי, איש רפורמה"],["argue","לטעון"]]},{"q":"According to the third paragraph, many experts expected that","o":["television would make people read more books","libraries would lose visitors and finally close","libraries would start to lend computers","the number of public libraries would grow quickly"],"a":1,"ex":"בפסקה 3 כתוב שהמומחים חזו שמספר המבקרים «would decline» (ירד) ושהספריות «would eventually disappear» (ייעלמו בסוף). «Grow quickly» הוא ההפך.","w":[["predict","לחזות"],["eventually","בסופו של דבר"],["decline","לרדת, לפחות"]]},{"q":"The main purpose of the last paragraph is to","o":["explain why the experts' prediction about the number of visitors was correct","describe how libraries have adapted to people's new needs","argue that libraries should stop lending books","compare libraries in poor and rich neighborhoods"],"a":1,"ex":"הפסקה האחרונה מתארת מה הספריות מציעות היום (אינטרנט, קורסים, מקום מפגש) כלומר איך הן השתנו. היא פותחת במילים «That prediction has not come true», ולכן היא לא מסבירה שהתחזית הייתה נכונה.","w":[["instead","במקום זאת"],["in addition","בנוסף"],["whereas","בעוד ש..., ואילו"]]}]},"s2c3":{"id":"s2c3","tier":0,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"Although the new highway shortened the trip to the city, many local residents were unhappy with it because it brought noise and pollution to their neighborhood.","o":["Because the new highway made the trip to the city shorter, local residents were pleased with it in spite of the noise and pollution it brought.","Many local residents opposed the new highway because it made the trip to the city longer and their area noisier.","The new highway made the trip to the city shorter; nevertheless, many people living nearby disliked it, since it caused noise and pollution in their area.","The noise and pollution in the neighborhood were caused mainly by local residents who used the new highway every day to travel to the city."],"a":2,"ex":"במקור: הכביש קיצר את הדרך, ובכל זאת התושבים לא מרוצים בגלל רעש וזיהום. «nevertheless» שומר על אותו ניגוד כמו «Although». התשובה הראשונה הופכת את המשמעות (התושבים מרוצים), והשנייה אומרת שהדרך התארכה.","w":[["although","למרות ש... (+משפט)"],["nevertheless","למרות זאת, אף על פי כן"],["resident","תושב"]]},{"q":"Scientists rarely agree on the exact causes of climate change in a particular region, since local weather is influenced by many factors at the same time.","o":["Because many factors affect local weather simultaneously, scientists seldom reach agreement about what exactly causes climate change in a specific region.","Scientists usually agree on the exact causes of climate change in a region, even though local weather is affected by many factors.","Since scientists rarely agree with each other, local weather in a particular region is influenced by many different factors.","Scientists rarely study local weather, because climate change in a particular region has only one main cause."],"a":0,"ex":"«rarely» = «seldom» (לעיתים רחוקות), ו«since» = «because» (מכיוון ש). התשובה השנייה משנה את «rarely» ל«usually», והשלישית הופכת סיבה ותוצאה: כאילו חוסר ההסכמה גורם למזג האוויר.","w":[["rarely","לעיתים רחוקות"],["seldom","לעיתים רחוקות"],["simultaneously","בו זמנית"]]},{"q":"Unless the city council finds additional funding by the end of the year, the plan to build a new public swimming pool will be canceled.","o":["The city council will find additional funding by the end of the year, so the new public swimming pool will be built.","Even if the city council finds more money by the end of the year, the plan for the new swimming pool will be canceled.","The plan to build a new swimming pool was canceled because the city council spent its money before the end of the year.","The plan for a new public swimming pool will be canceled if the city council does not find more money before the year ends."],"a":3,"ex":"«Unless» = אלא אם כן, כלומר «if ... not». התוכנית תבוטל אם לא יימצא כסף. «Even if» (גם אם) אומר שהיא תבוטל בכל מקרה, וזו משמעות אחרת. התשובה הראשונה טוענת בוודאות שהכסף יימצא, וזה לא כתוב במקור.","w":[["unless","אלא אם כן"],["even if","גם אם, אפילו אם"],["funding","מימון"]]}]},"s2c4":{"id":"s2c4","tier":0,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"Unlike earlier studies, the new research found that children who read for pleasure every day also tend to perform better in mathematics.","o":["Like earlier studies, the new research found that children who are good at mathematics usually enjoy reading every day.","Unlike earlier studies, the new research found that children who read every day for pleasure tend to do worse in mathematics.","Earlier studies found that daily reading improves mathematics, but the new research found no connection between the two.","The new research, unlike previous studies, showed that children who read for enjoyment every day generally do better in math as well."],"a":3,"ex":"«Unlike» = בניגוד ל. רק המחקר החדש מצא שילדים שקוראים להנאה כל יום מצליחים יותר במתמטיקה. התשובה השנייה משנה «better» ל«worse», והשלישית מחליפה בין המחקר החדש למחקרים הקודמים.","w":[["unlike","בניגוד ל... (+שם עצם)"],["tend to","נוטה ל..."],["perform","לבצע, להצליח (במשימה)"]]},{"q":"Demand for the company's products grew rapidly in the north; as a result, the company decided to open a second factory in that region.","o":["The company decided to open another factory in the north because demand for its products in that area had increased quickly.","Because the company opened a second factory in the north, demand for its products in that region grew rapidly.","Although demand for its products grew in the north, the company decided not to open a second factory there.","The company closed its factory in the north and opened a second one elsewhere, since demand in the north was falling."],"a":0,"ex":"במקור: הביקוש עלה (סיבה), ולכן נפתח מפעל שני (תוצאה). «because» בתשובה הנכונה שומר על אותו סדר הגיוני. התשובה השנייה הופכת סיבה ותוצאה: כאילו המפעל גרם לביקוש.","w":[["as a result","כתוצאה מכך"],["demand","ביקוש"],["rapidly","במהירות"]]},{"q":"Despite being one of the oldest buildings in town, the library is visited by hundreds of young people every week, many of whom come to study for exams.","o":["Because the library is one of the oldest buildings in town, very few young people visit it, except those who come to study for exams.","Hundreds of young people visit the library every week in order to see one of the oldest and most famous buildings in town.","Although the library is among the oldest buildings in town, hundreds of young people go there each week, many of them to study for exams.","The library, which was built only a few years ago, is visited every week by hundreds of young people, many of whom come to study for exams."],"a":2,"ex":"«Despite» = «Although» (למרות). הבניין ישן, ובכל זאת מאות צעירים מגיעים, ורבים מהם לומדים למבחנים. התשובה הראשונה אומרת שמעט מבקרים, והרביעית אומרת שהבניין חדש.","w":[["despite","למרות (+שם עצם)"],["although","למרות ש... (+משפט)"],["in order to","כדי ל... (+פועל)"]]}]},"s2c5":{"id":"s2c5","tier":0,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"Driving while very tired can have serious ___, such as accidents that hurt both the driver and other people on the road.","o":["benefits","consequences","habits","reasons"],"a":1,"ex":"«Consequences» = השלכות, תוצאות. תאונות הן תוצאה של נהיגה בעייפות. «Benefits» (יתרונות) הוא ההפך, ו«reasons» (סיבות) לא מתאים כי התאונה באה אחרי הנהיגה ולא לפניה.","w":[["consequence","תוצאה, השלכה"],["such as","כגון, כמו"],["benefit","יתרון, תועלת"]]},{"q":"The old bridge was in such poor ___ that the city closed it to traffic until the repairs were finished.","o":["condition","position","attention","opinion"],"a":0,"ex":"«Condition» = מצב. הגשר היה במצב כל כך גרוע שסגרו אותו עד סוף התיקונים. «Position» (מיקום) לא מסביר למה צריך תיקונים.","w":[["condition","מצב"],["so... that","כל כך... ש..."],["until","עד ש..."]]},{"q":"Because the road was icy, the driver tried to ___ sudden stops, which could cause the car to slide.","o":["practice","enjoy","require","avoid"],"a":3,"ex":"«Avoid» = להימנע מ. עצירות פתאומיות על כביש קפוא מסוכנות, ולכן הנהג ניסה להימנע מהן. «Practice» (להתאמן) או «enjoy» (ליהנות) לא הגיוניים כשמדובר בסכנה.","w":[["avoid","להימנע מ..."],["because","כי, מפני ש... (+משפט)"]]},{"q":"The team trained hard for months; ___, they won the national championship for the first time.","o":["nevertheless","for instance","as a result","in contrast"],"a":2,"ex":"«As a result» = כתוצאה מכך. האימונים הקשים (סיבה) הובילו לזכייה (תוצאה). «Nevertheless» (למרות זאת) מתאים רק כשיש ניגוד, ואין ניגוד בין אימון קשה לניצחון.","w":[["as a result","כתוצאה מכך"],["nevertheless","למרות זאת, אף על פי כן"]]}]},"s3c0":{"id":"s3c0","tier":1,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"Scientists warn that, unless action is taken soon, the loss of several coral reefs will become ___.","o":["reversible","voluntary","inevitable","temporary"],"a":2,"ex":"«inevitable» = בלתי נמנע. המדענים מזהירים שאם לא יפעלו מהר, האובדן של השוניות כמעט בטוח יקרה. «reversible» (הפיך) הפוך מהכוונה של האזהרה.","w":[["inevitable","בלתי נמנע"],["unless","אלא אם כן"]]},{"q":"The museum's new exhibition received poor reviews from critics; ___, it attracted a record number of visitors.","o":["nevertheless","consequently","similarly","for instance"],"a":0,"ex":"«nevertheless» = למרות זאת. הביקורות היו רעות, ובכל זאת הגיע מספר שיא של מבקרים: יש כאן ניגוד. «consequently» (כתוצאה מכך) לא מתאים, כי ביקורות רעות לא גורמות לשיא מבקרים.","w":[["nevertheless","למרות זאת, אף על פי כן"],["record","שיא"]]},{"q":"Rising rents have forced many young families to leave the city center, a trend that threatens to ___ the area's sense of community.","o":["strengthen","celebrate","imitate","undermine"],"a":3,"ex":"«undermine» = לערער, להחליש. עזיבת המשפחות הצעירות פוגעת בתחושת הקהילה, ולכן המגמה «מאיימת לערער» אותה. «strengthen» (לחזק) הפוך: מגמה מאיימת לא מחזקת.","w":[["undermine","לערער, להחליש"],["threaten","לאיים"]]},{"q":"Few of the volunteers could afford a car, ___ a house of their own.","o":["rather than","let alone","in order to","as well as"],"a":1,"ex":"«let alone» = ובטח שלא, קל וחומר. רובם לא יכלו להרשות לעצמם אפילו מכונית, ובטח שלא בית, שהוא יקר הרבה יותר. «as well as» (וגם) לא מוסיף את הרעיון של «ובטח שלא», שהוא כל הטעם של המשפט.","w":[["let alone","ובטח שלא, קל וחומר"],["afford","להרשות לעצמו (כלכלית)"]]}]},"s3c1":{"id":"s3c1","tier":1,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"The professor's theory was once rejected by most of her colleagues, but today it enjoys ___ support across the field.","o":["reluctant","widespread","scarce","hidden"],"a":1,"ex":"«widespread» = נפוץ, רחב. פעם רוב העמיתים דחו את התיאוריה, «but» היום היא נהנית מתמיכה רחבה: זה הניגוד ש-«but» דורש. «scarce» (מועט) לא יוצר ניגוד לעבר.","w":[["widespread","נפוץ, רחב היקף"],["reject","לדחות"]]},{"q":"The northern region receives heavy rainfall throughout the year, ___ the south remains dry for most months.","o":["so that","because","unless","whereas"],"a":3,"ex":"«whereas» = ואילו, בעוד ש. משווים בין הצפון הגשום לדרום היבש, כלומר ניגוד בין שני צדדים. «because» היה אומר שהגשם בצפון גורם ליובש בדרום, וזה לא הגיוני.","w":[["whereas","בעוד ש..., ואילו"],["throughout","לאורך, במשך כל"]]},{"q":"Children who grow up speaking two languages often ___ a third one more easily than those who speak only one.","o":["acquire","abandon","ignore","conceal"],"a":0,"ex":"«acquire» = לרכוש (ידע, שפה). ילדים דו-לשוניים לומדים שפה שלישית בקלות רבה יותר. «abandon» (לנטוש) לא מתאים ל-«more easily» ולהקשר של יתרון.","w":[["acquire","לרכוש"],["abandon","לנטוש, לזנוח"]]},{"q":"The bridge had not been inspected for over a decade; ___, nobody was surprised when engineers declared it unsafe.","o":["in contrast","even so","consequently","otherwise"],"a":2,"ex":"«consequently» = כתוצאה מכך. הגשר לא נבדק יותר מעשר שנים, ולכן אף אחד לא הופתע שהוכרז מסוכן: סיבה ותוצאה. «even so» (למרות זאת) היה רומז שהיה צפוי שיופתעו, וזה הפוך.","w":[["consequently","כתוצאה מכך, לפיכך"],["inspect","לבדוק, לפקח"]]}]},"s3c2":{"id":"s3c2","tier":1,"type":"rc","title":"The Story That Changes Each Time","text":["Most people assume that a memory works like a recording: once an event is stored, it can be played back whenever it is needed. Psychologists who study memory, however, have found that this common belief is largely mistaken. Rather than retrieving a fixed copy, the brain rebuilds an experience each time we recall it, using fragments of the original event together with our current knowledge, feelings and expectations. As a result, a story that we have told many times may differ substantially from what actually happened.","One explanation for this effect is a process known as reconsolidation. When a memory is brought to mind, it becomes unstable for a short period before it is stored again. During this window, new information can be added and old details can be lost. If, for example, a listener reacts with surprise to a particular part of a story, the speaker may emphasize that part the next time and gradually drop details that seemed less interesting. Each retelling, in other words, becomes the new \"original.\"","Experiments support this idea. In one type of study, volunteers watch a short film and are later asked to describe it to different listeners. Those who describe it to a listener who is believed to dislike the main character tend to present that character more negatively. Weeks later, even when asked to recall the film itself rather than their own description, they still remember the character in the less favorable way. Their memory has apparently been shaped by the version they chose to tell.","These findings have important consequences. In courts, witnesses who have repeated their account many times may feel highly confident even though their memories have shifted. Nevertheless, researchers stress that the flexibility of memory is not simply a flaw. A system that constantly updates itself allows people to connect past experiences to new situations and to learn from them. The price of this flexibility is that our most cherished stories are, to some degree, always being rewritten."],"qs":[{"q":"Which of the following is the best title for the passage?","o":["Why Children Forget Their Early Years","How Retelling a Story Reshapes Our Memories","The Role of Witnesses in Modern Courts","A Simple Method for Improving Memory"],"a":1,"ex":"הקטע כולו עוסק בכך שכל פעם שמספרים סיפור, הזיכרון נבנה מחדש ומשתנה. עדים בבית משפט מוזכרים רק בפסקה האחרונה כדוגמה, ולכן זו לא כותרת לכל הקטע.","w":[["retell","לספר מחדש"],["reshape","לעצב מחדש"]]},{"q":"According to the second paragraph, while a memory is being recalled, it","o":["is permanently erased from the brain","becomes more accurate than before","is passed on unchanged to the listener","can be altered before it is stored again"],"a":3,"ex":"בפסקה 2 כתוב שכשנזכרים, הזיכרון «becomes unstable» לזמן קצר לפני שהוא נשמר שוב, ובחלון הזה אפשר להוסיף פרטים ולאבד אחרים. אין שם טענה שהוא נמחק לגמרי או נעשה מדויק יותר.","w":[["unstable","לא יציב"],["alter","לשנות"]]},{"q":"In paragraph 3, the word \"Their\" (in \"Their memory has apparently been shaped\") refers to","o":["the listeners","the main characters","the volunteers","the films"],"a":2,"ex":"המשפט מתאר את המתנדבים שתיארו את הסרט, ושאחרי שבועות זכרו את הדמות באופן שלילי יותר. «Their memory» = הזיכרון של המתנדבים. המאזינים לא זוכרים את הסרט, כי הם לא ראו אותו.","w":[["volunteer","מתנדב"],["apparently","ככל הנראה"]]},{"q":"What does the experiment described in paragraph 3 suggest?","o":["The way people describe an event can later change how they remember it.","People remember films more accurately than real-life events.","Listeners usually adopt the speaker's opinion of a character after hearing the story.","Volunteers deliberately lied about the film in order to please their listeners."],"a":0,"ex":"המתנדבים שתיארו את הדמות באופן שלילי זכרו אותה כך גם שבועות אחר כך, «even when asked to recall the film itself». כלומר הגרסה שסיפרו שינתה את הזיכרון. לא נאמר שהם שיקרו בכוונה.","w":[["favorable","חיובי, אוהד"],["deliberately","בכוונה"]]},{"q":"The main purpose of the last paragraph is to","o":["describe a new experiment carried out on witnesses who had repeated their stories","prove that human memory should never be trusted","point out both a practical risk and an advantage of memory's flexibility","argue that courts should stop relying on witnesses"],"a":2,"ex":"הפסקה האחרונה מציגה סיכון (עדים בטוחים בעצמם למרות שהזיכרון שלהם השתנה), ואז «Nevertheless» מביאה יתרון: גמישות שמאפשרת ללמוד. «should never be trusted» קיצוני מדי, כי נאמר במפורש שזה «not simply a flaw».","w":[["nevertheless","למרות זאת, אף על פי כן"],["flaw","פגם"]]}]},"s3c3":{"id":"s3c3","tier":1,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"Although the new medication reduced symptoms in most patients, doctors remain cautious because its long-term effects have not yet been studied in sufficient depth.","o":["Because the new medication reduced symptoms in most patients, doctors are confident that its long-term effects will also prove to be safe for them.","The new medication helped only a few patients, so doctors will remain cautious until its long-term effects are studied in depth.","Doctors have stopped prescribing the new medication to most patients, since recent studies have shown that its long-term effects are harmful.","Doctors are still careful about the new medication, even though it helped most patients, since its long-term effects have not been studied enough."],"a":3,"ex":"במקור: התרופה עזרה לרוב החולים, אבל הרופאים זהירים כי ההשפעות ארוכות הטווח לא נחקרו מספיק. התשובה הנכונה מחליפה «Although» ב-«even though» ומשנה את סדר החלקים. «only a few patients» משנה את הכמות (במקור «most»).","w":[["cautious","זהיר"],["even though","אף על פי ש..."],["sufficient","מספיק"]]},{"q":"The ancient city was eventually abandoned, not because of a sudden invasion, as was once widely believed, but as a result of a slow decline in its water supply.","o":["Contrary to a once common view, a gradual shortage of water, rather than an unexpected attack, finally led people to leave the ancient city.","As was once widely believed, the ancient city was abandoned after a sudden invasion by its enemies, which also damaged its water supply.","Many people once believed that the ancient city had a serious water problem, but it was actually destroyed by invaders who attacked it suddenly.","Although its water supply was declining slowly, the ancient city was never abandoned by its people, who found new sources of water nearby."],"a":0,"ex":"במקור: העיר ננטשה לא בגלל פלישה, כפי שחשבו פעם, אלא בגלל ירידה איטית באספקת המים. התשובה הנכונה אומרת את זה עם «rather than» ועם «Contrary to a once common view». האפשרויות על הפולשים הופכות את הסיבה.","w":[["abandon","לנטוש"],["as a result of","כתוצאה מ..."],["rather than","במקום, ולא"]]},{"q":"Few employees took advantage of the flexible working hours, since most of them feared that their managers would regard it as a lack of commitment.","o":["Many employees used the flexible working hours, although they feared that their managers would view it as a lack of commitment.","Worried that their managers might see it as low commitment, only a small number of employees used the flexible working hours.","Most managers feared that employees who used the flexible hours would show a lack of commitment, so they cancelled the option.","Because their managers already considered them uncommitted to the company, only a few employees were ever offered the chance to work flexible hours."],"a":1,"ex":"«Few» = מעט מאוד עובדים השתמשו בשעות הגמישות, כי פחדו שהמנהלים יראו בזה חוסר מחויבות. התשובה הנכונה מעבירה את הסיבה לתחילת המשפט ואומרת «only a small number». «Many employees» הופך את הכמות.","w":[["few","מעט (כמעט אין)"],["take advantage of","לנצל, להשתמש ב..."],["commitment","מחויבות"]]}]},"s3c4":{"id":"s3c4","tier":1,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"Even though online courses are cheaper and more convenient, many students still prefer traditional classes, in which they can interact directly with teachers and classmates.","o":["Because online courses are cheaper and more convenient, most students have stopped attending traditional classes and now study only from home.","Many students now prefer online courses to traditional classes, since online courses allow them to interact more directly with teachers and classmates.","Many students still choose traditional classes, which allow face-to-face contact with teachers and classmates, despite the lower cost and greater convenience of online courses.","Traditional classes are actually cheaper and more convenient than online courses, so many students still prefer them in order to meet their teachers."],"a":2,"ex":"במקור: למרות שקורסים מקוונים זולים ונוחים יותר, הרבה סטודנטים עדיין מעדיפים כיתות רגילות, שבהן יש קשר ישיר עם המרצים. התשובה הנכונה מחליפה «Even though» ב-«despite» ומעבירה אותו לסוף. האפשרות הראשונה הופכת את הוויתור לסיבה.","w":[["even though","אף על פי ש..."],["despite","למרות (+שם עצם)"],["still","ובכל זאת; עדיין"]]},{"q":"The government introduced a tax on sugary drinks so as to reduce their consumption, and within two years, sales of such drinks had fallen considerably.","o":["The government decided to introduce a tax on sugary drinks because their sales had already fallen considerably over the previous two years.","In order to cut consumption of sugary drinks, a tax was placed on them by the government; within two years, sales had dropped sharply.","Although the government taxed sugary drinks in order to reduce their consumption, sales of these drinks hardly changed at all within the next two years.","Drink companies themselves raised the price of sugary drinks so as to reduce their consumption, and within two years sales had fallen considerably."],"a":1,"ex":"במקור: הממשלה הטילה מס על משקאות ממותקים כדי להפחית את הצריכה, ותוך שנתיים המכירות ירדו מאוד. התשובה הנכונה עוברת לסביל («a tax was placed on them by the government») ו-«so as to» הופך ל-«In order to». באפשרות הראשונה הירידה במכירות היא הסיבה למס, וזה הפוך.","w":[["so as to","כדי ל..."],["in order to","כדי ל... (+פועל)"],["considerably","במידה ניכרת"]]},{"q":"Whereas earlier researchers relied mainly on questionnaires, today's scientists can observe brain activity directly, which allows them to test theories that were once impossible to examine.","o":["Both earlier and modern researchers have relied mainly on questionnaires rather than on brain activity, which is why some important theories still cannot be tested today.","Today's scientists still rely mainly on questionnaires, just as earlier researchers did, since observing brain activity directly has turned out to be impossible.","Earlier researchers were able to observe brain activity directly, whereas today's scientists prefer to use questionnaires in order to test theories that were once impossible to examine.","Unlike past researchers, who depended mostly on questionnaires, modern scientists can watch the brain at work, which lets them test theories that could not be tested before."],"a":3,"ex":"במקור: חוקרים בעבר הסתמכו בעיקר על שאלונים, ואילו היום אפשר לצפות במוח ישירות ולבדוק תיאוריות שלא היה אפשר לבדוק קודם. התשובה הנכונה מחליפה «Whereas» ב-«Unlike». האפשרות השלישית מחליפה בין העבר להווה.","w":[["whereas","בעוד ש..., ואילו"],["unlike","בניגוד ל... (+שם עצם)"],["rely","להסתמך"]]}]},"s3c5":{"id":"s3c5","tier":1,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"The two reports differ ___ in their conclusions: one predicts steady growth, while the other predicts a deep recession.","o":["substantially","slightly","barely","equally"],"a":0,"ex":"«substantially» = באופן משמעותי. דוח אחד צופה צמיחה והשני מיתון עמוק, כלומר הבדל גדול. «slightly» (מעט) ו-«barely» (בקושי) סותרים את ההבדל החד שמתואר אחרי הנקודתיים.","w":[["substantially","באופן משמעותי, ניכר"],["recession","מיתון"]]},{"q":"The athlete continued to train every morning ___ she had been told by her doctor to rest.","o":["so that","as long as","even though","in case"],"a":2,"ex":"«even though» = אף על פי ש. הרופא אמר לה לנוח, ובכל זאת היא המשיכה להתאמן: ויתור. «as long as» (כל עוד) היה הופך את הוראת הרופא לתנאי לאימון, וזה לא הגיוני.","w":[["even though","אף על פי ש..."],["as long as","כל עוד, בתנאי ש..."]]},{"q":"Since the original documents were destroyed in a fire, historians are forced to ___ later copies whose accuracy cannot be fully confirmed.","o":["do without","dispose of","apply for","rely on"],"a":3,"ex":"«rely on» = להסתמך על. המסמכים המקוריים נשרפו, ולכן ההיסטוריונים נאלצים להסתמך על העותקים המאוחרים. «do without» (להסתדר בלי) הפוך: אין להם ברירה אלא להשתמש בעותקים.","w":[["rely on","להסתמך על"],["accuracy","דיוק"]]},{"q":"Many students record their lectures ___ review the material later at their own pace.","o":["let alone","so as to","rather than","so as not to"],"a":1,"ex":"«so as to» = כדי ל. מקליטים את ההרצאה כדי לחזור על החומר אחר כך: מטרה. «so as not to» אומר «כדי לא לחזור על החומר», וזה הפוך מהסיבה שמקליטים. «rather than» (במקום) ו-«let alone» (ועל אחת כמה וכמה לא) לא מתאימים למשמעות.","w":[["so as to","כדי ל..."],["at one's own pace","בקצב של עצמו"]]}]},"s4c0":{"id":"s4c0","tier":2,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"Because fresh water had become ___ in the region after three dry winters, farmers were forced to ration it among their crops.","o":["abundant","transparent","scarce","fragile"],"a":2,"ex":"«scarce» = נדיר, מועט. אחרי שלושה חורפים יבשים יש מעט מים, ולכן החקלאים נאלצו לחלק אותם במנות. «abundant» (בשפע) הוא ההפך: אם היו מים בשפע לא היה צורך לקצוב אותם.","w":[["scarce","נדיר, מועט"],["ration","לחלק במנות קצובות"],["abundant","שופע, בשפע"]]},{"q":"___ the strong objections of local residents, the city council voted to build the new highway along the river.","o":["Notwithstanding","Owing to","In view of","By virtue of"],"a":0,"ex":"«notwithstanding» = על אף, למרות. התושבים התנגדו, ובכל זאת המועצה הצביעה בעד הכביש: זה ניגוד, ולכן צריך מילת ויתור. «owing to» ו-«in view of» נותנים סיבה, וזה לא הגיוני שההתנגדות היא הסיבה לבנות.","w":[["notwithstanding","על אף, למרות"],["owing to","בשל, עקב"],["objection","התנגדות"]]},{"q":"Without regular maintenance, the old wooden bridge continued to ___ until engineers finally declared it unsafe for traffic.","o":["flourish","accelerate","comply","deteriorate"],"a":3,"ex":"«deteriorate» = להידרדר, להתבלות. גשר בלי תחזוקה הולך ומתקלקל עד שהוא לא בטוח. «flourish» (לשגשג) הוא ההפך הגמור.","w":[["deteriorate","להידרדר, להתבלות"],["maintenance","תחזוקה"],["flourish","לשגשג, לפרוח"]]},{"q":"The new drug lowered blood pressure in most of the patients who took it, ___ reducing their risk of suffering a heart attack.","o":["despite","thereby","instead of","unlike"],"a":1,"ex":"«thereby» = ובכך, על ידי כך. הורדת לחץ הדם היא הדרך שבה ירד הסיכון להתקף לב, כלומר זו תוצאה. «despite» (למרות) יוצר ניגוד שאין כאן, ו-«instead of» אומר שהסיכון לא ירד.","w":[["thereby","ובכך, על ידי כך"],["instead of","במקום"]]}]},"s4c1":{"id":"s4c1","tier":2,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"The lawyer's argument was so ___ that even the judge, who had seemed doubtful at first, was eventually persuaded.","o":["tedious","compelling","ambiguous","reluctant"],"a":1,"ex":"«compelling» = משכנע, חזק. הטיעון שכנע אפילו שופט שהיה בספק. «ambiguous» (דו-משמעי) הוא תכונה שמחלישה טיעון, לא כזו שמשכנעת.","w":[["compelling","משכנע, חזק"],["persuade","לשכנע"],["ambiguous","דו-משמעי"]]},{"q":"The museum agreed to lend the famous painting to the exhibition, ___ only for a limited period of three weeks.","o":["hence","whereby","lest","albeit"],"a":3,"ex":"«albeit» = אם כי. המוזיאון הסכים להשאיל, אבל עם הגבלה (רק לשלושה שבועות): זה ויתור חלקי. «hence» (ולכן) היה הופך את ההגבלה לתוצאה של ההסכמה, וזה לא הגיוני.","w":[["albeit","אם כי"],["hence","מכאן, ולכן"]]},{"q":"Planting trees along the river banks can ___ the damage caused by floods, although it cannot prevent flooding altogether.","o":["mitigate","intensify","precede","conceal"],"a":0,"ex":"«mitigate» = למתן, להקל. העצים מקטינים את הנזק, אבל (although) לא מונעים את השיטפון לגמרי. «intensify» (להגביר) הוא ההפך, ואז החלק השני עם «although» לא מתחבר.","w":[["mitigate","למתן, להקל"],["intensify","להגביר, להחריף"],["altogether","לגמרי"]]},{"q":"Unlike the old system, ___ every student was given exactly the same exam, the new program allows teachers to adapt tests to individual needs.","o":["whereas","thereby","whereby","hence"],"a":2,"ex":"«whereby» = שבאמצעותו, שלפיו. הוא מתאר את השיטה הישנה: שיטה שלפיה כל תלמיד קיבל אותו מבחן. «whereas» (בעוד ש) מוסיף ניגוד שני, אבל הניגוד כבר נאמר במילה «Unlike».","w":[["whereby","שבאמצעותו, שלפיו"],["whereas","בעוד ש..., ואילו"],["adapt","להתאים"]]}]},"s4c2":{"id":"s4c2","tier":2,"type":"rc","title":"Counting the Invisible: Microplastics in the Deep Sea","text":["For decades, public concern about plastic in the ocean focused on what could be seen: bottles floating on the surface and bags washed up on beaches. In recent years, however, researchers have turned their attention to the deep sea. Microplastics, fragments smaller than five millimeters, have been found in sediments thousands of meters below the surface, and even at the bottom of the deepest trenches. Many scientists now suspect that the ocean floor holds far more plastic than the surface does, although no one can yet say how much.","One reason for this uncertainty is that the deep sea is vast and expensive to reach. Collecting a single core of sediment may require a research ship, a trained crew and specialized equipment for several weeks. Hence, samples are scarce, and most come from a handful of locations that may not represent the ocean floor as a whole. Moreover, the particles themselves are tiny. The smallest cannot be seen even under an ordinary microscope, and all of them must first be separated from sand, shells and organic matter. This is a slow process whereby a sample is treated with chemicals, some of which can damage certain types of plastic and make them harder to identify.","A further difficulty is contamination. Researchers' clothing, their equipment and even the air in the laboratory constantly shed tiny plastic fibers. Unless strict precautions are taken, a sample may end up containing fibers from the laboratory, as opposed to the seabed. Several early studies were later found to have overestimated the amount of plastic for exactly this reason. Consequently, many laboratories now process 'blank' samples, containers of clean water handled in exactly the same way as the real ones, in order to estimate how much contamination occurs.","Notwithstanding these obstacles, accurate measurements matter. Microplastics on the seafloor may be swallowed by the creatures that live there and passed up the food chain. Some researchers argue that efforts to reduce plastic waste should not wait for precise figures; others caution that without reliable data it will be impossible to judge whether such efforts are working. Both groups agree, however, that standardized methods are needed so that results from different laboratories can be compared."],"qs":[{"q":"The main purpose of the passage is to","o":["argue that microplastics are more harmful in the deep sea than at the surface","describe a new technology for removing plastic from the ocean floor","show that all studies of deep-sea microplastics are unreliable","explain why the amount of microplastics in the deep sea is hard to determine"],"a":3,"ex":"כל הקטע עוסק בקשיים במדידה: המקום רחוק ויקר (פסקה 2), החלקיקים זעירים (פסקה 2), זיהום במעבדה (פסקה 3). הקטע לא משווה כמה הפלסטיק מזיק בכל מקום, ולא אומר שכל המחקרים לא אמינים, רק כמה מחקרים מוקדמים.","w":[["determine","לקבוע, לברר"],["unreliable","לא אמין"]]},{"q":"According to the second paragraph, one reason deep-sea samples may give a misleading picture is that","o":["they are collected from only a small number of places","the chemicals used to treat them add plastic particles","the particles in them are too large to separate from sand","research ships often lose them during long journeys"],"a":0,"ex":"בפסקה 2 כתוב שרוב הדגימות מגיעות מ-«a handful of locations» (מעט מקומות) שאולי לא מייצגים את כל קרקעית האוקיינוס. הכימיקלים לא מוסיפים פלסטיק, הם עלולים לפגוע בו, והחלקיקים זעירים ולא גדולים.","w":[["a handful of","קומץ, מעט"],["represent","לייצג"],["misleading","מטעה"]]},{"q":"In the third paragraph, the word 'shed' could best be replaced by","o":["store","hide","release","collect"],"a":2,"ex":"בגדים, ציוד ואוויר המעבדה «shed» סיבי פלסטיק, כלומר משחררים ומפזרים אותם, וכך הסיבים נכנסים לדגימות. «collect» (לאסוף) הוא כמעט ההפך: אם הם היו אוספים סיבים, לא היה זיהום.","w":[["shed","להשיר, לשחרר"],["release","לשחרר"],["contamination","זיהום"]]},{"q":"The third paragraph mainly serves to","o":["suggest that laboratory research on microplastics should be abandoned","point out a source of error in measurement and how scientists deal with it","compare the amount of plastic in clothing with the amount in the ocean","prove that early estimates of deep-sea plastic were too low"],"a":1,"ex":"פסקה 3 מציגה בעיה (זיהום מהמעבדה שמגדיל את הכמות שנמדדת) ואת הפתרון (דגימות «blank»). המחקרים המוקדמים העריכו יותר מדי (overestimated) ולא פחות מדי, ולכן התשובה האחרונה הפוכה.","w":[["overestimate","להעריך יותר מדי"],["consequently","כתוצאה מכך, לפיכך"],["as opposed to","בניגוד ל..."]]},{"q":"According to the last paragraph, researchers who disagree about when to act","o":["share the view that laboratories need common methods of measurement","agree that the current figures are accurate enough","believe that creatures on the seafloor do not swallow microplastics","argue that plastic waste cannot be reduced"],"a":0,"ex":"בסוף הפסקה: «Both groups agree» שצריך שיטות אחידות (standardized) כדי להשוות בין מעבדות. הם לא מסכימים שהנתונים מדויקים מספיק: קבוצה אחת אומרת במפורש שאין עדיין נתונים אמינים.","w":[["standardized","אחיד, תקני"],["caution","להזהיר"],["notwithstanding","על אף, למרות"]]}]},"s4c3":{"id":"s4c3","tier":2,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"Although the new irrigation method reduced water use on most of the farms that adopted it, researchers caution that it has not yet been tested in regions where rainfall is extremely scarce.","o":["Because the new irrigation method has already been tested in very dry regions, researchers believe that it will reduce water use on all farms.","The new irrigation method cut water use on most farms using it; nevertheless, researchers warn that it has yet to be tried in areas with very little rain.","Researchers warn that the new irrigation method reduced water use on only a few farms, since it was mainly used in regions with very little rainfall each year.","Although researchers have tested the new irrigation method in extremely dry regions, it failed to reduce water use on most of the farms that actually adopted it."],"a":1,"ex":"התשובה הנכונה שומרת על שני החלקים: חיסכון ברוב החוות (most = the majority), ואזהרה שהשיטה עוד לא נבדקה באזורים יבשים (not yet = has yet to). התשובה השלישית משנה «most» ל-«only a few» ומוסיפה סיבה שלא הייתה במקור.","w":[["not yet","עוד לא"],["caution","להזהיר"],["scarce","נדיר, מועט"]]},{"q":"Children who eat breakfast regularly tend to perform better at school, but this does not necessarily mean that eating breakfast is what causes their higher grades, as other factors may be involved.","o":["Since eating breakfast is clearly what improves children's grades, schools should make sure that every student eats a healthy breakfast regularly before class.","Children who eat breakfast regularly do not actually perform any better at school than other children, because other factors determine their grades.","Other factors, rather than breakfast, are certainly what cause some children both to eat breakfast regularly and to get higher grades at school.","Eating breakfast regularly is linked to doing well at school; however, it is possible that something other than breakfast explains the better results."],"a":3,"ex":"המשפט אומר שיש קשר (מתאם) בין ארוחת בוקר לציונים, אבל לא בהכרח שהיא הסיבה. התשובה הנכונה אומרת בדיוק את זה (it is possible). התשובה השלישית מלכודת: היא קובעת בוודאות שגורמים אחרים הם הסיבה, בעוד שבמקור כתוב רק «may».","w":[["tend to","נוטה ל..."],["necessarily","בהכרח"],["account for","להסביר, להיות הגורם ל..."]]},{"q":"The museum's ancient manuscripts are extremely fragile and deteriorate quickly when exposed to light; hence, only a small number of them are displayed to the public at any given time.","o":["Because only a few of the museum's ancient manuscripts are displayed at once, they deteriorate quickly when exposed to light.","Although the museum's ancient manuscripts are very fragile, most of them are displayed to the public, since light hardly affects them.","Since light causes the museum's very delicate ancient manuscripts to decay rapidly, just a few of them are shown to visitors at once.","The museum displays all of its ancient manuscripts to the public, even though light causes a small number of them to deteriorate."],"a":2,"ex":"«hence» = ולכן: הסיבה היא שהאור הורס את כתבי היד, והתוצאה היא שמציגים מעט מהם. התשובה הנכונה שומרת על הכיוון הזה עם «Since». התשובה הראשונה הופכת סיבה ותוצאה.","w":[["hence","מכאן, ולכן"],["deteriorate","להידרדר, להתבלות"],["fragile","שביר, עדין"]]}]},"s4c4":{"id":"s4c4","tier":2,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"The new tax is likely to reduce pollution only insofar as companies find it cheaper to adopt cleaner technologies than to keep paying the tax on their emissions.","o":["The new tax will probably lower pollution only to the extent that switching to cleaner technologies costs companies less than paying the tax.","The new tax will certainly reduce pollution, because companies will always prefer switching to cleaner technologies over paying any tax on their emissions.","Companies will adopt cleaner technologies only if the new tax fails to reduce pollution, regardless of how much the tax costs them.","Since cleaner technologies are already much cheaper than the new tax, most companies have stopped paying the tax on their emissions altogether."],"a":0,"ex":"«insofar as» = במידה ש..., ככל ש... = «to the extent that». המס יוריד זיהום רק בתנאי שטכנולוגיה נקייה זולה יותר מהמס. התשובה השנייה הופכת «likely» (סביר) ל-«certainly» (בוודאות) ומבטלת את התנאי.","w":[["insofar as","במידה ש..., ככל ש..."],["emissions","פליטות"],["adopt","לאמץ"]]},{"q":"The treaty, albeit signed by nearly every country in the region, has had little effect so far, since few of the signatories have passed the laws needed to enforce it.","o":["Because almost every country in the region signed the treaty, it has already had a considerable effect, although a few countries have not yet passed laws to enforce it.","Few countries in the region agreed to sign the treaty, and as a result it has had hardly any effect so far, even though the laws needed to enforce it were passed.","Although almost all the region's countries signed the treaty, it has achieved very little so far, as only a small number of them have enacted the laws required to enforce it.","The treaty has had little effect so far, since nearly every country in the region refused to sign it until the necessary laws were passed."],"a":2,"ex":"«albeit» = אם כי, «little» ו-«few» = מעט, כמעט אין. כמעט כולן חתמו, ובכל זאת להסכם כמעט אין השפעה כי רק מעט מדינות חוקקו חוקים. התשובה הראשונה מלכודת: «a few» (כמה) רומז שרוב המדינות כבר חוקקו, והיא גם הופכת «little effect» להשפעה ניכרת.","w":[["albeit","אם כי"],["few","מעט (כמעט אין)"],["enforce","לאכוף"]]},{"q":"As opposed to earlier surveys, which relied on what people reported about their own diets, the new study used blood tests, thereby providing a more objective measure of what participants actually ate.","o":["Like earlier surveys, the new study relied on participants' own reports of their diets, and therefore its measure of what they ate was more objective.","The new study combined blood tests with what people reported about their own diets, so as to confirm the results that earlier surveys had obtained.","Earlier surveys used blood tests to measure what people actually ate, whereas the new study relied on participants' reports, which are less objective.","Unlike previous surveys, which depended on people's self-reports, the new study used blood tests and in this way measured more objectively what participants really ate."],"a":3,"ex":"«as opposed to» = «unlike» (בניגוד ל...), ו-«thereby» = «in this way» (ובכך). הסקרים הקודמים נשענו על דיווח עצמי, והמחקר החדש על בדיקות דם. התשובה השלישית מחליפה בין הסקרים הישנים למחקר החדש.","w":[["as opposed to","בניגוד ל..."],["thereby","ובכך, על ידי כך"],["objective","אובייקטיבי, לא מוטה"]]}]},"s4c5":{"id":"s4c5","tier":2,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"Since the instructions were ___, half of the participants understood the task one way and the other half understood it in a completely different way.","o":["concise","ambiguous","accurate","compelling"],"a":1,"ex":"«ambiguous» = דו-משמעי. הוראות שאפשר להבין בשתי דרכים גרמו לכל קבוצה להבין אחרת. «accurate» (מדויק) היה מוביל להבנה אחידה, ההפך ממה שקרה.","w":[["ambiguous","דו-משמעי"],["concise","תמציתי"]]},{"q":"The professor's explanation was so ___ that even students with no background in the field could follow it with ease.","o":["lucid","obscure","redundant","hostile"],"a":0,"ex":"«lucid» = ברור, צלול. גם תלמידים בלי רקע הבינו בקלות, ולכן ההסבר היה ברור מאוד. «obscure» (מעורפל, לא ברור) הוא ההפך.","w":[["lucid","ברור, צלול"],["obscure","מעורפל, לא ברור"],["background","רקע"]]},{"q":"During a storm, the flash of lightning always ___ the sound of thunder, because light travels much faster than sound.","o":["follows","imitates","outlasts","precedes"],"a":3,"ex":"«precede» = לבוא לפני. האור מהיר מהקול, ולכן רואים את הברק לפני ששומעים את הרעם. «follows» (בא אחרי) הופך את הסדר ומתנגש עם הסיבה שבסוף המשפט.","w":[["precede","לבוא לפני, להקדים"],["outlast","להחזיק מעמד יותר מ..."]]},{"q":"The plan will succeed ___ the residents are willing to cooperate; without their support, it is likely to fail.","o":["although","unless","insofar as","whereas"],"a":2,"ex":"«insofar as» = במידה ש..., ככל ש... ההצלחה תלויה בשיתוף הפעולה של התושבים, וזה מה שהחלק השני אומר (בלי תמיכה זה ייכשל). «unless» (אלא אם כן) הופך את התנאי: התוכנית תצליח רק אם התושבים לא ישתפו פעולה.","w":[["insofar as","במידה ש..., ככל ש..."],["unless","אלא אם כן"],["cooperate","לשתף פעולה"]]}]},"s5c0":{"id":"s5c0","tier":3,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"The evidence linking the drug to the side effect remains ___ at best: a handful of small studies, none of which took the patients' age into account.","o":["compelling","abundant","tenuous","conclusive"],"a":2,"ex":"«Tenuous» = קלוש, חלש. אחרי הנקודתיים מתוארות ראיות דלות (כמה מחקרים קטנים ולא מבוקרים), ולכן הראיות חלשות. «compelling» ו-«conclusive» אומרות ההפך: ראיות משכנעות וחד-משמעיות.","w":[["tenuous","קלוש, רופף"],["at best","במקרה הטוב"],["conclusive","חד-משמעי, מכריע"]]},{"q":"Researchers stored a second copy of the data on a separate server ___ the original be lost in a power failure.","o":["lest","unless","provided that","so that"],"a":0,"ex":"«Lest» = כדי שלא, פן. שמרו עותק נוסף כדי שהמקור לא יאבד. «so that» היה אומר שהמטרה היא שהמקור יאבד, וזה לא הגיוני.","w":[["lest","פן, שמא, כדי שלא"],["so that","כדי ש..."]]},{"q":"Far from being ___, the senator's position on the issue has shifted at least three times in the past year.","o":["erratic","fickle","controversial","steadfast"],"a":3,"ex":"«Far from being» = רחוק מלהיות. העמדה השתנתה שלוש פעמים, כלומר היא רחוקה מלהיות יציבה: «steadfast» = יציב, נחוש. «erratic» ו-«fickle» (הפכפך) מתארות בדיוק את מה שקרה, ולכן לא מתאימות אחרי «far from».","w":[["steadfast","יציב, איתן, נחוש"],["fickle","הפכפך"],["erratic","לא יציב, הפכפך"]]},{"q":"The committee's report was ___ a full endorsement of the plan; it praised the plan's goals but rejected nearly every one of its proposed methods.","o":["undoubtedly","by no means","above all","in particular"],"a":1,"ex":"«By no means» = בשום אופן לא. הדוח דחה כמעט את כל השיטות, ולכן הוא בשום אופן לא תמיכה מלאה. «undoubtedly» היה אומר שזו ללא ספק תמיכה מלאה, וזה סותר את החלק השני.","w":[["by no means","בשום אופן לא"],["endorsement","תמיכה, אישור"]]}]},"s5c1":{"id":"s5c1","tier":3,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"Although the virus was first detected in a single village, it managed to ___ across the region within weeks, overwhelming local clinics.","o":["proliferate","dwindle","subside","stagnate"],"a":0,"ex":"«Proliferate» = להתרבות, להתפשט במהירות. המרפאות הוצפו, כלומר הנגיף התפשט. «dwindle» ו-«subside» פירושן להצטמצם ולשכוך, ההפך ממה שמתואר.","w":[["proliferate","להתרבות, להתפשט במהירות"],["dwindle","להצטמצם, לפחות"],["subside","לשכוך, לרדת"]]},{"q":"The study's findings are relevant to our school ___ they were based on students of the same age and background as ours.","o":["lest","whereas","inasmuch as","albeit"],"a":2,"ex":"«Inasmuch as» = מאחר ש..., במידה ש.... החלק השני הוא הסיבה לכך שהממצאים רלוונטיים. «whereas» מציין ניגוד, ואין כאן ניגוד בין שני החלקים.","w":[["inasmuch as","מאחר ש..., במידה ש..."],["whereas","בעוד ש..., ואילו"]]},{"q":"Auditors found a striking ___ between the figures the company reported to investors and those it submitted to the tax authorities: the first showed a large profit, the second a loss.","o":["resemblance","consensus","correlation","discrepancy"],"a":3,"ex":"«Discrepancy» = פער, אי-התאמה. סט אחד הראה רווח והשני הפסד, כלומר המספרים לא מתאימים זה לזה. «resemblance» (דמיון) אומרת ההפך.","w":[["discrepancy","פער, אי-התאמה"],["resemblance","דמיון"]]},{"q":"The plan had several obvious flaws; the board, ___, approved it unanimously, hoping to fix the details at a later stage.","o":["accordingly","nonetheless","likewise","namely"],"a":1,"ex":"«Nonetheless» = למרות זאת. לתוכנית היו פגמים ברורים, ובכל זאת הדירקטוריון אישר אותה. «accordingly» (בהתאם לכך) היה אומר שהאישור נבע מהפגמים, וזה לא הגיוני.","w":[["nonetheless","בכל זאת, למרות זאת"],["accordingly","בהתאם לכך, לכן"],["flaw","פגם"]]}]},"s5c2":{"id":"s5c2","tier":3,"type":"rc","title":"The Long Road from Invention to Adoption","text":["It is tempting to assume that a superior technology wins as soon as it appears. History suggests otherwise. The gap between an invention and its widespread use is often measured not in months but in decades, and economists have long tried to explain why tools that seem obviously beneficial in hindsight were, at the time, adopted with remarkable reluctance.","One reason is that a new technology rarely arrives in finished form. Early versions tend to be expensive, unreliable and difficult to repair, and their advantages over existing methods may be modest at first. A farmer who already owns horses and knows how to care for them has little reason to buy an early tractor that breaks down frequently and requires fuel he cannot easily obtain. Only after years of gradual improvement, much of it carried out by people other than the original inventor, does the new tool become clearly worth its price.","A second obstacle lies in what economists call complementary investments. A technology is seldom useful on its own; it depends on other things being in place. Electric motors, for example, offered factories little benefit as long as buildings were designed around a single steam engine that drove every machine through long belts and shafts. The real gains appeared only when owners redesigned entire factories, a costly process that many postponed until their old buildings wore out. In such cases, the delay reflects not ignorance but a reasonable calculation.","Finally, adoption is a social process. People learn about new methods mainly from neighbors, colleagues and competitors, and they tend to trust what they can observe directly. When the benefits of an innovation are hard to see, or appear only after many years, even well-informed individuals may hesitate. Institutions can slow matters further: regulations written for an older technology, or workers whose skills would lose their value, may resist a change that threatens established interests.","None of this means that slow adoption is simply wasteful. Waiting allows a technology to mature and its problems to surface before large sums are committed. Nonetheless, understanding the sources of delay can help governments and firms decide when intervention, such as training programs or shared infrastructure, might shorten a wait that serves no one."],"qs":[{"q":"The passage mainly discusses","o":["why inventors often fail to profit from their own inventions","the reasons that beneficial technologies may take a long time to be widely used","how electricity transformed the design of factories","the ways in which governments and firms can speed up the adoption of new technologies"],"a":1,"ex":"כל הקטע מסביר למה טכנולוגיות מועילות מתפשטות לאט: מוצר לא מוגמר, השקעות משלימות ותהליך חברתי. המנועים החשמליים הם רק דוגמה בפסקה 3, והממשלות מוזכרות רק בסוף.","w":[["adoption","אימוץ"],["widespread","נפוץ, רחב היקף"]]},{"q":"According to the second paragraph, the farmer in the example would probably not buy an early tractor because","o":["he did not trust the people who sold it","the government had restricted its use","it could not do the work of a horse","it often broke down and its fuel was hard to get"],"a":3,"ex":"בפסקה 2 כתוב שהטרקטור המוקדם «breaks down frequently» ודורש דלק שקשה להשיג. אמון במוכרים ותקנות של הממשלה לא מוזכרים בפסקה הזו.","w":[["unreliable","לא אמין"],["obtain","להשיג"]]},{"q":"In the fourth paragraph, the word 'established' could best be replaced by","o":["proven","founded","existing","confirmed"],"a":2,"ex":"«Established interests» = האינטרסים הקיימים והמבוססים, של מי שנהנה מהמצב הנוכחי. לכן «existing». «proven» (מוכח) מפתה, אבל לא מדובר באינטרסים שהוכחו אלא באינטרסים שכבר קיימים.","w":[["established","מבוסס, קיים, מושרש"],["threaten","לאיים על"]]},{"q":"The example of electric motors in the third paragraph is used to show that","o":["the benefit of a new technology may depend on other costly changes","factory owners were generally unaware of the new technologies that could improve their production","steam engines were more efficient than electric motors in most factories of the time","electric motors were adopted more quickly than tractors"],"a":0,"ex":"הפסקה עוסקת ב«complementary investments»: המנוע החשמלי הועיל רק אחרי שתכננו מחדש את כל המפעל, תהליך יקר. הקטע אומר במפורש שהעיכוב «not ignorance», ולכן התשובה על חוסר מודעות שגויה.","w":[["complementary","משלים"],["postpone","לדחות"]]},{"q":"It can be inferred from the last paragraph that the author believes that","o":["some delays in adoption serve a useful purpose, while others might reasonably be shortened","governments should avoid any involvement in the spread of new technologies","every delay in adopting a useful technology is a waste of resources that could have been avoided","most new technologies are adopted too quickly to be properly tested"],"a":0,"ex":"הכותב אומר שהמתנה מאפשרת לטכנולוגיה להבשיל (כלומר יש בה תועלת), ובכל זאת אפשר לקצר המתנה «that serves no one». «every delay is a waste» סותרת את המשפט «None of this means that slow adoption is simply wasteful».","w":[["nonetheless","בכל זאת, למרות זאת"],["mature","להבשיל"],["intervention","התערבות"]]}]},"s5c3":{"id":"s5c3","tier":3,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"Granted that the new vaccine is more expensive than the old one, its far greater effectiveness makes it the better choice for the national health service.","o":["Because the new vaccine is more expensive than the old one, the national health service should continue to prefer the old one, despite its considerably lower effectiveness.","Although the new vaccine costs more than the old one, the national health service would do better to choose it, since it is considerably more effective.","The new vaccine is both cheaper and more effective than the old one, so the national health service should choose it.","Although the new vaccine is more effective than the old one, its higher price makes it the less sensible choice for the national health service."],"a":1,"ex":"«Granted that» = נכון ש..., גם אם נודה ש.... המשפט מודה שהחיסון החדש יקר יותר, ובכל זאת קובע שהוא עדיף כי הוא יעיל בהרבה. התשובה הנכונה שומרת על שני החלקים עם «Although» ו-«since». התשובה האחרונה הופכת את המסקנה (המחיר מכריע).","w":[["granted that","נכון ש..., גם אם נודה ש..."],["although","למרות ש..."],["effectiveness","יעילות"]]},{"q":"The town's economic decline was caused not so much by the closure of the mine as by the failure of local leaders to develop any alternative source of employment in the years that followed.","o":["The closure of the mine was the main reason for the town's economic decline, although local leaders also failed to create any new jobs in the years that followed.","The closure of the mine and the local leaders' failure to create new jobs afterwards contributed in equal measure to the town's economic decline.","Local leaders failed to develop new sources of employment because the closure of the mine had already ruined the town's economy.","It was chiefly the local leaders' failure to create other jobs after the mine closed, rather than the closure itself, that caused the town's economic decline."],"a":3,"ex":"«Not so much X as Y» = לא כל כך X אלא בעיקר Y. הסיבה העיקרית היא כישלון המנהיגים, לא סגירת המכרה. התשובה הראשונה הופכת את הדגש, והשנייה אומרת שהשתיים תרמו באותה מידה.","w":[["not so much X as Y","לא כל כך X אלא Y"],["chiefly","בעיקר"],["rather than","במקום, ולא"]]},{"q":"Officials delayed announcing the results of the inquiry, lest premature disclosure should provoke public panic before the full extent of the water contamination had been established.","o":["Officials held back the inquiry's results, fearing that releasing them too early might cause public panic before the full extent of the water contamination was known.","Because the public had already panicked over the water contamination, officials decided to delay announcing the results of the inquiry until the situation had calmed down.","Officials released the results of the inquiry as early as possible in order to prevent public panic over the extent of the water contamination in the area.","Officials delayed announcing the results of the inquiry until they had confirmed that the water contamination was far too limited to cause any serious public panic."],"a":0,"ex":"«Lest» = מחשש ש..., כדי שלא. הפקידים עיכבו את הפרסום כדי שלא תפרוץ בהלה לפני שהיקף הזיהום ידוע. בתשובה השנייה הבהלה כבר קרתה, והאחרונה מוסיפה טענה שלא נאמרה (שהזיהום מוגבל).","w":[["lest","פן, שמא, כדי שלא"],["premature","מוקדם מדי"],["extent","היקף"]]}]},"s5c4":{"id":"s5c4","tier":3,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"Hardly had the company launched its new smartphone when reports of overheating batteries began to appear, forcing it to recall nearly a quarter of a million devices within a month.","o":["The company recalled nearly a quarter of a million of its new smartphones before any reports of overheating batteries had appeared.","Several years after the company launched its new smartphone, reports of overheating batteries forced it to recall nearly a quarter of a million devices.","Almost as soon as the company's new smartphone went on sale, reports of overheating batteries emerged, and within a month the company had to recall almost 250,000 devices.","Almost as soon as the company's new smartphone went on sale, reports of overheating batteries emerged, but the company refused to recall any of the devices it had sold."],"a":2,"ex":"«Hardly had... when» = אך ורק... וכבר, מיד אחרי ש.... הדיווחים הופיעו מיד אחרי ההשקה והובילו לריקול. התשובה השנייה משנה את הזמן (כמה שנים אחרי), והאחרונה הופכת את התוצאה (סירבה לריקול).","w":[["hardly","כמעט לא"],["recall","להחזיר מוצר מהשוק, ריקול"],["as soon as","ברגע ש..., מיד כש..."]]},{"q":"Inasmuch as the survey relied solely on volunteers, who tend to be more health-conscious than the general population, its conclusions about national eating habits should be treated with considerable caution.","o":["The survey's conclusions about national eating habits are reliable, since its volunteers were more health-conscious than the general population.","Since the survey was based only on volunteers, who are generally more health-conscious than most people, its findings about the nation's eating habits may not be fully trustworthy.","Since the survey was based only on volunteers, who are generally less health-conscious than most people, its findings about the nation's eating habits may not be fully trustworthy.","Since the survey's findings about the nation's eating habits may not be trustworthy, researchers decided to rely only on volunteers."],"a":1,"ex":"«Inasmuch as» = מאחר ש.... מכיוון שהסקר נשען רק על מתנדבים שמקפידים יותר על בריאות, צריך להיזהר במסקנות. התשובה השלישית הופכת את ההשוואה (פחות מקפידים), והרביעית הופכת סיבה ותוצאה.","w":[["inasmuch as","מאחר ש..., במידה ש..."],["solely","אך ורק, בלעדית"],["caution","זהירות"]]},{"q":"The treaty was by no means the first attempt to limit the arms race; it was, nonetheless, the first to include a system for verifying that both sides were actually keeping their commitments.","o":["The treaty was the first attempt ever made to limit the arms race, and it also included a system for checking that both sides actually kept their commitments.","Several earlier agreements had tried to limit the arms race, and, just like the treaty, they included a system for checking that both sides kept their commitments.","Earlier agreements had tried to limit the arms race, but this treaty was the first to provide a way of checking whether both sides honored their commitments.","Since earlier agreements had failed to limit the arms race, the treaty's authors abandoned the idea of checking whether both sides were actually keeping their commitments."],"a":2,"ex":"«By no means the first» = בשום אופן לא הראשון, כלומר היו ניסיונות קודמים. «nonetheless» = ובכל זאת, הוא הראשון עם מנגנון פיקוח. התשובה הראשונה אומרת שזה הניסיון הראשון, והשנייה אומרת שגם להסכמים הקודמים היה פיקוח.","w":[["by no means","בשום אופן לא"],["nonetheless","בכל זאת, למרות זאת"],["verify","לאמת, לוודא"]]}]},"s5c5":{"id":"s5c5","tier":3,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"The government introduced strict measures to ___ water use during the drought, including fines for watering gardens during the day.","o":["boost","subsidize","curtail","justify"],"a":2,"ex":"«Curtail» = לצמצם, לקצץ. קנסות על השקיה בשעות היום נועדו להפחית צריכת מים בזמן בצורת. «boost» ו-«subsidize» היו מעודדות צריכה, ההפך מהמטרה.","w":[["curtail","לצמצם, לקצץ"],["drought","בצורת"],["subsidize","לסבסד"]]},{"q":"The new rules had ___ taken effect when several companies announced they would challenge them in court, so swift was the opposition.","o":["eventually","gradually","long since","hardly"],"a":3,"ex":"«Hardly... when» = רק... וכבר, מיד אחרי ש.... סוף המשפט אומר שההתנגדות הייתה מהירה מאוד, ולכן החברות הודיעו כמעט מיד. «long since» (מזמן) סותרת את המהירות.","w":[["hardly","כמעט לא"],["swift","מהיר"],["take effect","להיכנס לתוקף"]]},{"q":"The scale of the flooding was ___: in more than two centuries of record-keeping, the river had never risen so high.","o":["unprecedented","predictable","negligible","routine"],"a":0,"ex":"«Unprecedented» = חסר תקדים. הנהר מעולם לא עלה כל כך גבוה ב-200 שנות תיעוד, כלומר לא היה כדבר הזה. «routine» ו-«predictable» אומרות שזה רגיל וצפוי, ההפך.","w":[["unprecedented","חסר תקדים"],["negligible","זניח"]]},{"q":"For decades, a reliable treatment for the disease remained ___: each drug that looked promising in early tests failed in later trials.","o":["accessible","elusive","affordable","obsolete"],"a":1,"ex":"«Elusive» = חמקמק, קשה להשגה. כל תרופה נכשלה, כך שטיפול אמין לא נמצא. «accessible» (נגיש) אומרת ההפך, ו-«affordable» עוסקת במחיר, שלא מוזכר כאן.","w":[["elusive","חמקמק, קשה להשגה"],["obsolete","מיושן, שאבד עליו הכלח"]]}]},"s6c0":{"id":"s6c0","tier":0,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"Most of the city's parks are crowded on weekends; ___, on weekday mornings they are almost empty.","o":["however","moreover","therefore","for example"],"a":0,"ex":"«however» = עם זאת. בסופי שבוע הפארקים מלאים, ובבקרים של ימי חול הם כמעט ריקים: זה ניגוד. «therefore» (לכן) היה הופך את החלק השני לתוצאה של הראשון, וזה לא הגיוני.","w":[["however","עם זאת, אולם"],["crowded","צפוף, מלא אנשים"]]},{"q":"The doctor told Maya to drink more water, because her headaches were probably ___ by not drinking enough on hot days.","o":["prevented","solved","caused","ignored"],"a":2,"ex":"«caused by» = נגרם על ידי. הרופא חושב שחוסר שתייה הוא הסיבה לכאבי הראש, ולכן הוא אומר לה לשתות יותר. «prevented» (נמנע) הפוך במשמעות: חוסר שתייה לא מונע כאבי ראש.","w":[["cause","לגרום"],["prevent","למנוע"]]},{"q":"The library stayed open later in the evening ___ students could study there before their exams.","o":["even though","unless","whereas","so that"],"a":3,"ex":"«so that» = כדי ש. הספרייה נשארה פתוחה מאוחר יותר במטרה שהסטודנטים יוכלו ללמוד. «even though» (אף על פי ש) יוצר ניגוד, ואין כאן ניגוד בין שני החלקים.","w":[["so that","כדי ש... (+משפט)"],["even though","אף על פי ש..."]]},{"q":"Vegetables stay fresh for many days in a cool, dry place, but in a warm kitchen they ___ quickly.","o":["freeze","spoil","recover","shine"],"a":1,"ex":"«spoil» = להתקלקל. המשפט מנגיד (but) בין מקום קריר שבו הירקות נשארים טריים לבין מטבח חם, ולכן שם הם מתקלקלים. «freeze» (לקפוא) לא קורה במטבח חם.","w":[["spoil","להתקלקל"],["fresh","טרי"]]}]},"s6c1":{"id":"s6c1","tier":0,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"The outdoor concert was ___ because of the storm, so the band promised to play again next month.","o":["recorded","enjoyed","canceled","repeated"],"a":2,"ex":"«canceled» = בוטל. בגלל הסערה ההופעה בוטלה, ולכן הלהקה הבטיחה לנגן שוב בחודש הבא. «enjoyed» (נהנו ממנו) לא מסביר למה צריך לנגן שוב.","w":[["cancel","לבטל"],["because of","בגלל (+שם עצם)"]]},{"q":"Many teenagers stay up late looking at their phones; ___, some of them sleep only five or six hours a night.","o":["as a result","in contrast","for instance","on the other hand"],"a":0,"ex":"«as a result» = כתוצאה מכך. השינה הקצרה היא התוצאה של השימוש בטלפון עד מאוחר. «in contrast» ו-«on the other hand» יוצרים ניגוד, ואין כאן ניגוד.","w":[["as a result","כתוצאה מכך"],["in contrast","לעומת זאת"]]},{"q":"The teacher gave a clear ___ of the problem, and after that everyone in the class understood how to solve it.","o":["complaint","mistake","question","explanation"],"a":3,"ex":"«explanation» = הסבר. אחרי הסבר ברור כולם הבינו איך לפתור את הבעיה. «mistake» (טעות) לא הייתה עוזרת לכיתה להבין.","w":[["explanation","הסבר"],["solve","לפתור"]]},{"q":"___ Sam had trained for months, he did not finish the race because he hurt his leg.","o":["Since","Even though","So that","As soon as"],"a":1,"ex":"«Even though» = אף על פי ש. הוא התאמן חודשים, ובכל זאת לא סיים את המרוץ: זה ניגוד. «Since» (מכיוון ש) היה אומר שהאימונים הם הסיבה שלא סיים, וזה לא הגיוני.","w":[["even though","אף על פי ש..."],["since","מכיוון ש..."]]}]},"s6c2":{"id":"s6c2","tier":0,"type":"rc","title":"Trees on City Streets","text":["In many cities around the world, local governments plant thousands of trees along streets every year. At first, this may seem like a simple way to make neighborhoods look nicer. However, city planners say that street trees offer much more than beauty. They help people, buildings and even the city budget.","The most obvious benefit is shade. On a hot summer day, a sidewalk under a row of trees can be several degrees cooler than a sidewalk in full sun. Trees also release water through their leaves, and this water cools the air around them. As a result, people who live on green streets often use their air conditioners less, which lowers their electricity bills. In addition, leaves and roots catch rainwater, so less water floods the streets after a storm.","Street trees, however, are not free. A young tree must be watered regularly during its first few years, and older trees need to be cut back so that their branches do not hit buses or power lines. Roots can also cause problems. As they grow, they sometimes push up the sidewalk and damage pipes under the street. For this reason, some cities choose smaller trees for narrow streets, and they plant them in larger holes so that the roots have enough room.","Despite these costs, most studies find that street trees are a good investment. One city calculated that every dollar it spent on caring for its trees returned more than two dollars in savings, mainly from lower energy use and less damage from rainwater. Because of such findings, many cities now plan to plant even more trees in the coming years."],"qs":[{"q":"The passage mainly discusses","o":["how trees release water through their leaves","the benefits and the costs of trees along city streets","why some cities have stopped planting trees","the best kinds of trees for narrow streets"],"a":1,"ex":"הקטע מסביר את היתרונות של עצים ברחוב (צל, אוויר קריר, חיסכון) וגם את הבעיות והעלויות שלהם. שחרור מים דרך העלים הוא רק פרט אחד בפסקה 2, ולא הנושא של כל הקטע.","w":[["benefit","יתרון, תועלת"],["cost","עלות, מחיר"]]},{"q":"According to the second paragraph, people who live on green streets","o":["drive more often than other people","rarely go outside in the summer","must water the trees every day","often pay less for electricity"],"a":3,"ex":"בפסקה 2 כתוב שהם משתמשים פחות במזגן, ולכן חשבונות החשמל שלהם יורדים («lowers their electricity bills»). שאר התשובות לא כתובות בפסקה.","w":[["lower","להוריד, להפחית"],["bill","חשבון (לתשלום)"]]},{"q":"In the third paragraph, the word 'they' in 'As they grow' refers to","o":["branches","buses","roots","power lines"],"a":2,"ex":"המשפט שלפני אומר «Roots can also cause problems», ומיד אחריו «As they grow, they sometimes push up the sidewalk». השורשים הם אלה שגדלים, מרימים את המדרכה ופוגעים בצינורות.","w":[["root","שורש"],["damage","לפגוע, להזיק; נזק"]]},{"q":"The main purpose of the last paragraph is to","o":["show that street trees save more money than they cost","explain how growing roots push up sidewalks and damage pipes under the street","describe the work of watering young trees","suggest that cities should plant fewer trees"],"a":0,"ex":"הפסקה האחרונה אומרת שלמרות העלויות, העצים הם השקעה טובה: כל דולר מחזיר יותר משני דולרים. «plant fewer trees» הפוך ממה שכתוב, כי ערים מתכננות לשתול עוד עצים.","w":[["despite","למרות (+שם עצם)"],["investment","השקעה"]]},{"q":"According to the third paragraph, some cities plant trees in larger holes in order to","o":["keep the branches away from buses","make the trees grow more quickly","use less water for young trees","give the roots enough space"],"a":3,"ex":"בסוף פסקה 3 כתוב שהם שותלים בבורות גדולים יותר «so that the roots have enough room», כלומר כדי שלשורשים יהיה מספיק מקום. הענפים והאוטובוסים מוזכרים בפסקה, אבל קשורים לגיזום ולא לבורות.","w":[["in order to","כדי ל... (+פועל)"],["room","מקום, מרחב"]]}]},"s6c3":{"id":"s6c3","tier":0,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"Although the new phone is cheaper than the old model, most customers prefer the old one because its battery lasts longer.","o":["Most customers prefer the new phone, because it is cheaper and its battery lasts longer.","Since the new phone is cheaper than the old model, its battery also lasts longer than the old model's battery.","Most customers like the old model better since its battery lasts longer, even though the new phone costs less.","Few customers prefer the old model, although its battery lasts longer than the new phone's battery."],"a":2,"ex":"«Although» הוחלף ב-«even though», «prefer» ב-«like better» ו-«cheaper» ב-«costs less». המשמעות זהה: רוב הלקוחות מעדיפים את הדגם הישן בגלל הסוללה. «Few customers» (מעט לקוחות) הופך את «most» (רוב).","w":[["although","למרות ש... (+משפט)"],["even though","אף על פי ש..."],["prefer","להעדיף"]]},{"q":"If students do not hand in their projects by Thursday, they will not be allowed to take part in the science fair.","o":["Students may take part in the science fair only if they hand in their projects by Thursday.","Students who hand in their projects after Thursday will get extra time for the science fair.","Students will be allowed to take part in the science fair even if they hand in their projects late.","Because the science fair is on Thursday, students must hand in their projects before it starts."],"a":0,"ex":"«only if» = רק אם. מי שלא מגיש עד יום חמישי לא משתתף, כלומר משתתפים רק אם מגישים בזמן. «even if they hand in late» אומר את ההפך, והתשובה האחרונה מוסיפה מידע שלא היה (שהיריד ביום חמישי).","w":[["only if","רק אם"],["if","אם"],["hand in","להגיש"]]},{"q":"Fewer tourists visited the island this year, mainly because flights became much more expensive after the airline raised its prices.","o":["More tourists visited the island this year, even though flights became much more expensive after the airline raised its prices.","The main reason for the drop in the number of tourists on the island this year was the airline's higher prices.","The airline raised its prices this year mainly because fewer tourists wanted to fly to the island than in the past.","Flights to the island became much cheaper this year after the airline lowered its prices, so the number of tourists fell."],"a":1,"ex":"«Fewer tourists» הפך ל-«drop in the number of tourists» (ירידה במספר התיירים), ו-«mainly because» הפך ל-«the main reason». התשובה השלישית הופכת סיבה ותוצאה: לפי המקור המחירים גרמו לירידה, ולא להפך.","w":[["mainly","בעיקר"],["because","כי, מפני ש... (+משפט)"],["raise","להעלות"]]}]},"s6c4":{"id":"s6c4","tier":0,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"Many young people hardly ever read newspapers; instead, they get most of their news from short videos on social media.","o":["Many young people often read newspapers, and they also watch short news videos on social media every day.","Short videos on social media have made many young people more interested in reading newspapers than they used to be.","Newspapers are rarely read by older people, who get most of their news from short videos on social media.","Many young people rarely read newspapers; most of the news they receive comes from short videos on social media."],"a":3,"ex":"«hardly ever» = כמעט אף פעם לא, כמו «rarely». המשמעות נשמרת: צעירים כמעט לא קוראים עיתונים ומקבלים חדשות מסרטונים. בתשובה הראשונה «often» (לעיתים קרובות) הופך את המשמעות, ובשלישית מדובר באנשים מבוגרים במקום בצעירים.","w":[["hardly","כמעט לא"],["rarely","לעיתים רחוקות"],["instead","במקום זאת"]]},{"q":"The community center closed for six months so that workers could repair its roof, which had been damaged in a heavy storm.","o":["A heavy storm damaged the community center's roof, but the center stayed open for the whole six months while workers repaired it.","The community center was shut for six months in order to allow workers to fix the roof damaged in a heavy storm.","Workers accidentally damaged the roof of the community center during the six months that it was closed after a heavy storm.","The community center closed for six months because of a heavy storm, but workers will only repair its damaged roof next year."],"a":1,"ex":"«so that workers could repair» הפך ל-«in order to allow workers to fix»: שתיהן מילות מטרה. «closed» הפך ל-«was shut». בתשובה השלישית הפועלים הם שגרמו לנזק, וזה משנה מי עשה מה.","w":[["so that","כדי ש... (+משפט)"],["in order to","כדי ל... (+פועל)"],["repair","לתקן"]]},{"q":"Unlike her older brother, who enjoys cooking, Noa prefers to eat simple meals and rarely spends time in the kitchen.","o":["Noa seldom spends time in the kitchen and likes simple meals, whereas her older brother enjoys cooking.","Like her older brother, Noa enjoys cooking and often spends time in the kitchen.","Noa's older brother prefers simple meals, while Noa enjoys spending time in the kitchen.","Noa rarely spends time in the kitchen because her older brother does all the cooking for her."],"a":0,"ex":"«Unlike» (בניגוד ל) הוחלף ב-«whereas» (ואילו), ו-«rarely» ב-«seldom». שני המשפטים אומרים שאחיה אוהב לבשל והיא לא. התשובה השלישית מחליפה בין נועה לאחיה, והאחרונה מוסיפה סיבה שלא הייתה במקור.","w":[["unlike","בניגוד ל... (+שם עצם)"],["whereas","בעוד ש..., ואילו"],["seldom","לעיתים רחוקות"]]}]},"s6c5":{"id":"s6c5","tier":0,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"Our neighbors are very ___; they often bring us food from their garden and lend us tools without asking for anything.","o":["rude","lazy","generous","careless"],"a":2,"ex":"«generous» = נדיב. השכנים נותנים אוכל ומשאילים כלים בלי לבקש דבר בתמורה. «rude» (גס רוח) סותר את מה שמתואר אחרי הנקודה-פסיק.","w":[["generous","נדיב"],["lend","להשאיל"]]},{"q":"The factory put solar panels on its roof; ___ the sun, it now pays much less for electricity than it did five years ago.","o":["thanks to","instead of","in spite of","except for"],"a":0,"ex":"«thanks to» = הודות ל, בזכות. השמש היא הסיבה הטובה לכך שהמפעל משלם פחות על חשמל. «in spite of» (למרות) היה יוצר ניגוד, אבל השמש עוזרת לחסוך ולא מפריעה.","w":[["thanks to","הודות ל..., בזכות"],["in spite of","למרות (+שם עצם)"]]},{"q":"Before you buy a used car, it is wise to ___ it carefully to make sure that the engine and the brakes work well.","o":["ignore","borrow","paint","examine"],"a":3,"ex":"«examine» = לבדוק היטב. כדי לוודא שהמנוע והבלמים תקינים צריך לבדוק את המכונית. «ignore» (להתעלם) הפוך ממה שצריך לעשות.","w":[["examine","לבדוק, לבחון"],["wise","נבון, חכם"]]},{"q":"Some fruits, ___ bananas and oranges, have a thick skin, so they do not need to be washed before you eat them.","o":["unlike","such as","rather than","instead of"],"a":1,"ex":"«such as» = כגון, כמו. בננות ותפוזים הם דוגמאות לפירות עם קליפה עבה. «unlike» (בניגוד ל) היה אומר שלבננות ולתפוזים אין קליפה עבה, וזה לא נכון.","w":[["such as","כגון, כמו"],["unlike","בניגוד ל... (+שם עצם)"]]}]},"s7c0":{"id":"s7c0","tier":1,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"The committee's report was truly ___: it covered every aspect of the problem and left no important question unanswered.","o":["superficial","comprehensive","ambiguous","premature"],"a":1,"ex":"«comprehensive» = מקיף. אחרי הנקודתיים מוסבר שהדוח כיסה כל היבט ולא השאיר שאלה פתוחה, כלומר הוא מקיף. «superficial» (שטחי) אומר בדיוק את ההפך.","w":[["comprehensive","מקיף"],["superficial","שטחי"],["aspect","היבט"]]},{"q":"Many small shops in the old market have closed in recent years, ___ the rise of large supermarkets on the edge of town.","o":["in spite of","regardless of","instead of","owing to"],"a":3,"ex":"«owing to» = בשל, עקב. עליית הסופרמרקטים הגדולים היא הסיבה לסגירת החנויות הקטנות. «in spite of» (למרות) היה אומר שהחנויות נסגרו למרות הסופרמרקטים, וזה לא הגיוני.","w":[["owing to","בשל, עקב"],["in spite of","למרות (+שם עצם)"]]},{"q":"The ancient manuscript is extremely ___, so visitors are allowed to view it only through a sealed glass case.","o":["fragile","durable","ordinary","accessible"],"a":0,"ex":"«fragile» = שביר, עדין. בגלל שכתב היד עדין, מותר להסתכל עליו רק מבעד לזכוכית. «durable» (עמיד) הוא ההפך, ואז לא הייתה סיבה להגן עליו.","w":[["fragile","שביר, עדין"],["durable","עמיד"],["manuscript","כתב יד"]]},{"q":"The new policy was meant to reduce traffic in the city center; ___, it simply moved the congestion to the surrounding neighborhoods.","o":["likewise","furthermore","accordingly","instead"],"a":3,"ex":"«instead» = במקום זאת. המדיניות הייתה אמורה להפחית את התנועה, ובמקום זה רק העבירה את הפקקים לשכונות אחרות. «accordingly» (בהתאם לכך) מציג תוצאה צפויה, אבל כאן התוצאה הפוכה למטרה.","w":[["instead","במקום זאת"],["congestion","עומס, פקקים"],["accordingly","בהתאם לכך, לכן"]]}]},"s7c1":{"id":"s7c1","tier":1,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"The witness's description of the accident was so ___ that the police could not tell which car had entered the junction first.","o":["precise","vague","detailed","reliable"],"a":1,"ex":"«vague» = מעורפל, לא ברור. בגלל שהעדות הייתה מעורפלת, המשטרה לא הצליחה לקבוע מי נכנס ראשון לצומת. «precise» ו-«detailed» (מדויק, מפורט) היו מאפשרים לקבוע בדיוק את זה.","w":[["vague","מעורפל, לא ברור"],["precise","מדויק"]]},{"q":"Students may submit their essays after the deadline, ___ they inform the lecturer in advance and explain the reason for the delay.","o":["so that","unless","provided that","even though"],"a":2,"ex":"«provided that» = בתנאי ש. מותר להגיש באיחור בתנאי שמודיעים מראש. «unless» (אלא אם כן) היה אומר שמי שמודיע מראש דווקא לא יכול להגיש באיחור, וזה הפוך.","w":[["provided that","בתנאי ש..."],["unless","אלא אם כן"],["in advance","מראש"]]},{"q":"In order to ___ the spread of the disease, the authorities closed schools and banned large public gatherings.","o":["encourage","describe","curb","predict"],"a":2,"ex":"«curb» = לרסן, לבלום. סגירת בתי ספר ואיסור התקהלויות נועדו לבלום את התפשטות המחלה. «encourage» (לעודד) הוא ההפך הגמור.","w":[["curb","לרסן, לבלום"],["in order to","כדי ל... (+פועל)"],["ban","לאסור"]]},{"q":"The professor rarely praises her students' work; ___, when she called one thesis \"excellent\", everyone understood how impressive it must have been.","o":["otherwise","for instance","similarly","hence"],"a":3,"ex":"«hence» = מכאן, ולכן. מכיוון שהיא כמעט אף פעם לא משבחת, כולם הבינו שאם שיבחה, העבודה באמת מצוינת: זו תוצאה. «for instance» (למשל) לא מתאים, כי שבח הוא לא דוגמה לכך שהיא כמעט לא משבחת.","w":[["hence","מכאן, ולכן"],["rarely","לעיתים רחוקות"],["praise","לשבח"]]}]},"s7c2":{"id":"s7c2","tier":1,"type":"rc","title":"The Language of the Hive","text":["For centuries, beekeepers noticed that once a single honeybee discovers a rich patch of flowers, many others from the same hive soon arrive there. How the first bee manages to share this information remained a puzzle, since bees can neither draw maps nor point the way. The answer, it turned out, lay in a series of movements that the returning bee performs on the vertical walls of the hive, in the dark.","The scientist who decoded these movements was the Austrian biologist Karl von Frisch. Beginning in the 1920s, he trained bees to visit dishes of sugar water and watched them through glass-walled hives. He observed that when the food was close to the hive, the returning bee simply ran around in small circles. When the food was farther away, however, she performed what he called a \"waggle dance\": she ran forward in a straight line while shaking her body from side to side, then circled back and repeated the run.","After years of measurement, von Frisch realized that each part of the dance carried a precise message. The angle of the straight run, measured against the vertical, matched the angle between the food source and the sun. A bee running straight upward was telling her sisters to fly directly toward the sun, while a run tilted to the right indicated a direction to the right of it. The length of the waggling, in turn, signaled distance: the longer it lasted, the farther away the flowers were.","Not every scientist accepted these conclusions. In the 1960s, several researchers argued that bees located food mainly by following its smell, and that the dance was merely a sign of excitement. The debate was finally settled decades later, when engineers placed a small dancing robot bee inside a hive. Bees that watched the robot flew in the direction and to the distance it had indicated, even though the robot had never visited any flowers. Von Frisch, who shared the Nobel Prize in 1973, did not live to see this proof that the dancer is, in effect, giving directions."],"qs":[{"q":"Which of the following is the best title for the passage?","o":["How Flowers Attract Honeybees","The Early Life of Karl von Frisch","Cracking the Code of the Honeybee Dance","Why Bees Prefer Sugar Water"],"a":2,"ex":"כל הקטע עוסק בריקוד של הדבורים: מה השאלה, איך פון פריש פענח את המשמעות שלו, ואיך הממצא אושר. «The Early Life of Karl von Frisch» מפתה, אבל הקטע לא מספר על חייו, רק על המחקר שלו.","w":[["decode","לפענח"],["crack a code","לפצח צופן"]]},{"q":"According to paragraph 2, a bee that has found food very close to the hive","o":["runs around in small circles","shakes her body while running in a straight line","leads the other bees to the food herself","does not return to the hive at all"],"a":0,"ex":"בפסקה 2 כתוב שכשהאוכל קרוב לכוורת, הדבורה רק רצה במעגלים קטנים. ריצה בקו ישר עם ניעור הגוף («waggle dance») מתוארת רק כשהאוכל רחוק יותר.","w":[["observe","להבחין, לצפות"],["farther","רחוק יותר"]]},{"q":"Based on paragraph 3, a bee whose straight run points directly downward is most probably indicating food that is","o":["very close to the hive","exactly in the direction of the sun","slightly to the right of the sun","in the opposite direction from the sun"],"a":3,"ex":"לפי פסקה 3, ריצה ישר למעלה פירושה לעוף ישר לכיוון השמש. לכן ריצה ישר למטה (הכיוון ההפוך) פירושה לעוף בכיוון ההפוך לשמש. «exactly in the direction of the sun» מתאים לריצה למעלה, לא למטה.","w":[["indicate","להצביע על, לסמן"],["opposite","הפוך, נגדי"],["tilted","נטוי, מוטה"]]},{"q":"In paragraph 4, the word \"settled\" (in \"The debate was finally settled\") could best be replaced by","o":["started","resolved","ignored","repeated"],"a":1,"ex":"«settled» כאן = הוכרע, נפתר. הוויכוח הוכרע כשניסוי רובוט הדבורה הראה שהריקוד מעביר הוראות. «started» (התחיל) לא נכון, כי הוויכוח התחיל כבר בשנות ה-60.","w":[["settle","להכריע, ליישב (ויכוח)"],["resolve","לפתור, ליישב"],["debate","ויכוח, דיון"]]},{"q":"The main purpose of the last paragraph is to","o":["explain why bees are attracted to the smell of flowers","describe how robots are used to protect beehives","present a challenge to von Frisch's findings and show how it was answered","argue that von Frisch did not deserve to share the Nobel Prize"],"a":2,"ex":"הפסקה האחרונה מציגה חוקרים שפקפקו בממצאים (טענו שהדבורים מוצאות אוכל לפי ריח), ואז מספרת איך ניסוי הרובוט הכריע את הוויכוח. «explain why bees are attracted to the smell» מפתה, אבל הריח מוזכר רק כטענה של המתנגדים.","w":[["challenge","ערעור, אתגר"],["proof","הוכחה"],["merely","רק, לא יותר מ..."]]}]},"s7c3":{"id":"s7c3","tier":1,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"Although the city's population has nearly doubled over the past thirty years, the number of public libraries has remained the same, leaving many neighborhoods without one.","o":["Because the city's population has nearly doubled over the past thirty years, the number of public libraries has also grown, so every neighborhood now has one.","Despite the fact that the city's population has almost doubled in thirty years, no public libraries have been added, so many neighborhoods still have none.","The city's population has hardly changed in thirty years, which explains why no new public libraries have been built in its neighborhoods.","Although many public libraries have opened over the past thirty years, the city's growing population still leaves a few neighborhoods without one."],"a":1,"ex":"במקור: האוכלוסייה כמעט הוכפלה, אבל מספר הספריות לא השתנה, ולכן בהרבה שכונות אין ספרייה. התשובה הנכונה מחליפה «Although» ב-«Despite the fact that». האפשרות הראשונה הופכת את ההיגיון (הספריות גדלו), והשלישית משנה את הכמות («hardly changed»).","w":[["although","למרות ש... (+משפט)"],["despite","למרות (+שם עצם)"],["hardly","כמעט לא"]]},{"q":"The company decided to delay the launch of its new phone in order to fix a battery problem that had been discovered only a week before the planned date.","o":["The company launched its new phone on the planned date as promised, although a serious battery problem had been discovered only a week earlier.","A battery problem in the company's new phone was actually caused by the decision to delay its launch until a week after the planned date.","The company postponed the launch of its new phone for a week because customers in a preview program had complained about its battery.","The company's new phone launch was postponed so that a battery fault found just a week before the due date could be repaired."],"a":3,"ex":"במקור: החברה דחתה את ההשקה כדי לתקן תקלה בסוללה שהתגלתה שבוע לפני המועד. התשובה הנכונה עוברת לסביל («was postponed») ומחליפה «in order to» ב-«so that». האפשרות השנייה הופכת סיבה ותוצאה, והשלישית מוסיפה תלונות של לקוחות שלא מופיעות במקור.","w":[["in order to","כדי ל... (+פועל)"],["so that","כדי ש... (+משפט)"],["postpone","לדחות"]]},{"q":"Only a small minority of the patients who took part in the study reported side effects, and in most of those cases the symptoms disappeared within a few days.","o":["Few of the study's participants said they suffered side effects, and these generally lasted no longer than a few days.","Most of the patients in the study reported side effects, although these usually disappeared within a few days.","A small number of patients reported side effects, and in every case the symptoms lasted for several weeks.","Only a few patients agreed to take part in the study, because most of them were afraid of its side effects."],"a":0,"ex":"במקור: רק מעטים דיווחו על תופעות לוואי, ובדרך כלל הן עברו תוך כמה ימים. «Few» מחליף את «a small minority», ו-«generally» מחליף את «in most of those cases». האפשרות השנייה משנה את הכמות («Most»), והשלישית משנה את משך התסמינים.","w":[["minority","מיעוט"],["few","מעט (כמעט אין)"],["side effects","תופעות לוואי"]]}]},"s7c4":{"id":"s7c4","tier":1,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"Unless the dam is repaired before the rainy season begins, engineers warn, the nearby villages could be flooded, forcing thousands of residents to leave their homes.","o":["Engineers warn that repairing the dam before the rainy season could itself cause flooding in the nearby villages and force thousands of residents to leave.","Because the dam was not repaired before the rainy season began, thousands of residents of the nearby villages have already been forced to leave their homes.","According to engineers, if the dam is not fixed before the rains start, nearby villages may flood and thousands of people may have to leave.","Engineers say that even if the dam is repaired in time, the nearby villages will still be flooded during the rainy season."],"a":2,"ex":"«Unless» = אלא אם כן, כלומר «if ... not». התשובה הנכונה אומרת: אם הסכר לא יתוקן לפני הגשמים, הכפרים עלולים להיות מוצפים. האפשרות השנייה מתארת משהו שכבר קרה, בעוד שבמקור זו רק אזהרה לעתיד, והרביעית («even if») משנה את התנאי.","w":[["unless","אלא אם כן"],["even if","גם אם, אפילו אם"],["resident","תושב"]]},{"q":"Unlike most birds, which build a new nest every year, eagles often return to the same nest for decades, adding fresh material to it each season.","o":["Like most other birds, eagles build a completely new nest every year, often using material taken from the old nests they have abandoned.","Eagles rarely return to the same nest year after year, since most birds, unlike them, add new material to their nests each season.","Most birds return to the same nest for decades and add fresh material to it, whereas eagles prefer to build a new one each year.","Eagles frequently use the same nest for many years, adding new material each season, while most other birds build a new one annually."],"a":3,"ex":"«Unlike» = בניגוד ל. התשובה הנכונה מחליפה אותו ב-«while» ומשנה את סדר החלקים, אבל המשמעות זהה: נשרים חוזרים לאותו קן, ורוב הציפורים בונות קן חדש. האפשרות השלישית מחליפה בין הנשרים לשאר הציפורים, והראשונה הופכת ניגוד לדמיון («Like»).","w":[["unlike","בניגוד ל... (+שם עצם)"],["while","בעוד ש... (ניגוד)"],["annually","מדי שנה"]]},{"q":"The researchers' findings were not published for several years, mainly because the journal's editors doubted whether such a small sample could support such a bold conclusion.","o":["The journal's editors published the researchers' findings immediately, although they privately doubted whether such a small sample could really support so bold a conclusion.","The main reason the researchers' findings remained unpublished for years was that the editors questioned whether so small a sample could justify so bold a conclusion.","The researchers chose to delay publishing their findings for several years because they wanted to collect a much larger sample before drawing such a bold conclusion.","The researchers' findings were finally published after several years, once the journal's editors realized that the sample was much larger than they had thought."],"a":1,"ex":"במקור: המאמר לא פורסם שנים, בעיקר כי העורכים פקפקו אם מדגם קטן יכול לתמוך במסקנה נועזת. התשובה הנכונה מחליפה «mainly because» ב-«The main reason ... was that». האפשרות השלישית משנה מי עשה מה: כאן החוקרים עצמם דחו את הפרסום.","w":[["doubt","לפקפק"],["bold","נועז"],["sample","מדגם"]]}]},"s7c5":{"id":"s7c5","tier":1,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"The two species of frog look almost identical; ___, genetic tests show that they separated from each other millions of years ago.","o":["however","therefore","for example","in addition"],"a":0,"ex":"«however» = עם זאת. הצפרדעים נראות כמעט זהות, אבל הבדיקות הגנטיות מראות שהן נפרדו מזמן: זה ניגוד. «therefore» (לכן) לא מתאים, כי מראה זהה לא מוביל למסקנה שהן רחוקות זו מזו.","w":[["however","עם זאת, אולם"],["identical","זהה"],["species","מין (בביולוגיה)"]]},{"q":"The architect insisted on using local stone ___ imported materials, arguing that it suited the region's hot climate far better.","o":["as well as","rather than","such as","along with"],"a":1,"ex":"«rather than» = במקום, ולא. האדריכל העדיף אבן מקומית על פני חומרים מיובאים, כי לטענתו היא מתאימה יותר לאקלים. «as well as» (וגם) היה אומר שהשתמש בשניהם, וזה סותר את ההעדפה.","w":[["rather than","במקום, ולא"],["insist on","להתעקש על"],["imported","מיובא"]]},{"q":"Although scientists had long ___ that the lakes in the region were shrinking, they lacked clear proof until satellite images became available.","o":["demonstrated","denied","suspected","established"],"a":2,"ex":"«suspected» = חשדו. המדענים חשדו שהאגמים מצטמקים, אבל לא הייתה להם הוכחה. «demonstrated» ו-«established» (הוכיחו, ביססו) סותרים את זה שלא הייתה הוכחה.","w":[["suspect","לחשוד"],["demonstrate","להוכיח, להראות"],["lack","לחסור, להיות חסר"]]},{"q":"The new trade agreement is expected to be ___ beneficial, since both countries will gain access to markets that were previously closed to them.","o":["mutually","hardly","unequally","rarely"],"a":0,"ex":"«mutually» = הדדית. ההסכם מועיל לשני הצדדים, כי שתי המדינות ירוויחו גישה לשווקים חדשים. «hardly» (כמעט לא) סותר את ההסבר שאחרי «since».","w":[["mutually","הדדית"],["beneficial","מועיל"],["previously","קודם לכן, בעבר"]]}]},"s8c0":{"id":"s8c0","tier":1,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"The committee's final report was so ___ that even experts in the field struggled to follow its main argument.","o":["concise","obscure","accessible","entertaining"],"a":1,"ex":"«obscure» = לא ברור, מעורפל. אם אפילו מומחים התקשו לעקוב אחרי הטיעון, הדוח היה לא ברור. «concise» (תמציתי) ו-«accessible» (נגיש) אומרים את ההפך: דוח כזה קל להבנה.","w":[["obscure","לא ברור, מעורפל"],["struggle","להתקשות, להיאבק"],["concise","תמציתי"]]},{"q":"The company did not announce any layoffs this year; ___, it hired two hundred new workers last month.","o":["on the contrary","as a result","for instance","otherwise"],"a":0,"ex":"«on the contrary» = להפך. החברה לא פיטרה, ולהפך: היא אפילו גייסה עובדים חדשים. «as a result» (כתוצאה מכך) לא מתאים, כי היעדר פיטורים לא גורם לגיוס של מאתיים עובדים.","w":[["on the contrary","להפך (דוחה את מה שנאמר)"],["layoff","פיטורים"]]},{"q":"To ___ the spread of the disease, health officials closed schools and banned large public gatherings.","o":["accelerate","document","curb","justify"],"a":2,"ex":"«curb» = לרסן, לבלום. סוגרים בתי ספר ואוסרים התקהלויות כדי לבלום את התפשטות המחלה. «accelerate» (להאיץ) הוא ההפך הגמור ממה שהפקידים רצו.","w":[["curb","לרסן, לבלום"],["spread","התפשטות"],["accelerate","להאיץ"]]},{"q":"The new phone sold out within hours, ___ its unusually high price and a number of poor reviews.","o":["because of","in spite of","in order to","instead of"],"a":1,"ex":"«in spite of» = למרות. מחיר גבוה וביקורות רעות היו אמורים להרחיק קונים, ובכל זאת הטלפון אזל: זה ויתור. «because of» (בגלל) לא הגיוני, כי ביקורות רעות לא גורמות למכירות.","w":[["in spite of","למרות (+שם עצם)"],["sell out","לאזול מהמלאי"]]}]},"s8c1":{"id":"s8c1","tier":1,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"The witness's account was ___ by security camera footage, which showed exactly what she had described.","o":["contradicted","exaggerated","verified","postponed"],"a":2,"ex":"«verified» = אומת. המצלמה הראתה בדיוק את מה שהעדה תיארה, ולכן הסרטון אישר את דבריה. «contradicted» (הוכחש, נסתר) היה מתאים רק אם הסרטון היה מראה משהו אחר.","w":[["verify","לאמת"],["account","תיאור, דיווח"],["contradict","לסתור"]]},{"q":"___ the region's mild climate, it attracts thousands of retirees every winter.","o":["Owing to","Regardless of","Unlike","Apart from"],"a":0,"ex":"«Owing to» = בשל, עקב. האקלים הנוח הוא הסיבה שפנסיונרים מגיעים בחורף. «Regardless of» (בלי קשר ל...) מנתק את הקשר בין האקלים לבין המבקרים, וזה לא הגיוני.","w":[["owing to","בשל, עקב"],["mild","מתון, נוח"],["retiree","פנסיונר"]]},{"q":"Although the two paintings look ___ at first glance, a closer look reveals dozens of small differences.","o":["distinct","ancient","valuable","identical"],"a":3,"ex":"«identical» = זהים. «Although» מראה ניגוד: במבט ראשון הציורים נראים זהים, אבל מקרוב יש הבדלים. «distinct» (שונים זה מזה) לא יוצר ניגוד להבדלים, ולכן לא מתאים ל-«Although».","w":[["identical","זהה"],["although","למרות ש... (+משפט)"],["reveal","לחשוף, לגלות"]]},{"q":"Visitors may enter the nature reserve ___ they stay on the marked trails and do not feed the animals.","o":["unless","provided that","so that","even if"],"a":1,"ex":"«provided that» = בתנאי ש. מותר להיכנס בתנאי שנשארים בשבילים ולא מאכילים את החיות. «unless» (אלא אם כן) הופך את ההיגיון: לפיו אסור להיכנס דווקא כשמתנהגים כמו שצריך.","w":[["provided that","בתנאי ש..."],["unless","אלא אם כן"],["reserve","שמורה"]]}]},"s8c2":{"id":"s8c2","tier":1,"type":"rc","title":"Tomorrow's Problem","text":["Almost everyone has postponed an important task while knowing that the delay would only make things worse. For a long time, procrastination was viewed as a simple matter of laziness or poor time management. Psychologists now regard this explanation as incomplete. Studies suggest that many people who procrastinate are not lazy at all; in fact, they often work hard on other, less urgent tasks while the one that really matters is left waiting. This observation led researchers to look for the causes elsewhere.","According to a growing body of research, procrastination is primarily a problem of managing emotions rather than time. When a task makes us feel anxious, bored or doubtful about our abilities, avoiding it brings immediate relief. That relief, however, is temporary, and it comes at a cost: the unpleasant feelings return, often stronger, as the deadline approaches. Because the brain tends to value an immediate reward more highly than a distant one, the short-term comfort of delay frequently wins over the long-term benefit of finishing the work.","Researchers have also noticed that people tend to think of their future selves almost as strangers. In one study, brain scans showed that when participants imagined themselves ten years from now, their pattern of brain activity resembled the pattern produced when they thought about other people. This may explain why it feels so easy to leave a difficult job for \"tomorrow's me\": it is, in a sense, someone else's problem.","Fortunately, these findings also point to practical solutions. Breaking a large project into small, concrete steps makes it seem less threatening, so getting started requires less emotional effort; writing a single paragraph, for example, feels far easier than writing an entire report. Another useful strategy is to forgive oneself for past delays. In one experiment, students who did so procrastinated less before their next exam, presumably because they felt less guilt and anxiety. Finally, picturing one's future self in vivid detail can make that person feel closer and more worth protecting."],"qs":[{"q":"The passage mainly discusses","o":["how to manage time more efficiently at work","the differences between lazy people and hard-working people","how brain scans are used to study long-term memory in adults and children","why people delay tasks and what can help them do so less"],"a":3,"ex":"הקטע מסביר למה אנשים דוחים משימות (רגשות, תגמול מיידי, ה«אני» העתידי כזר) ובפסקה האחרונה מה עוזר. ניהול זמן מוזכר רק כהסבר הישן שהחוקרים דוחים, ולכן זו לא התשובה.","w":[["procrastinate","לדחות משימות, להתמהמה"],["delay","לדחות; עיכוב"]]},{"q":"According to the second paragraph, people often avoid an unpleasant task because","o":["avoiding it makes them feel better for a short time","they do not know how to plan their schedule in advance","they believe the deadline is still very far away","they prefer to complete tasks together with others"],"a":0,"ex":"בפסקה 2 כתוב שהימנעות מהמשימה נותנת «immediate relief» (הקלה מיידית), אבל זמנית. תכנון לוח זמנים הוא בדיוק ההסבר שהפסקה דוחה: הבעיה היא רגשות, לא זמן.","w":[["relief","הקלה"],["temporary","זמני"],["rather than","במקום, ולא"]]},{"q":"In paragraph 3, the word \"it\" (in \"it is, in a sense, someone else's problem\") refers to","o":["the brain scan","the difficult job","the study","the pattern of activity"],"a":1,"ex":"המשפט אומר שקל להשאיר עבודה קשה ל«אני של מחר», כי היא בעצם הבעיה של מישהו אחר. «it» חוזר אל «a difficult job». סריקת המוח והמחקר הם לא «בעיה» שמשאירים למחר.","w":[["in a sense","במובן מסוים"],["resemble","להיות דומה ל..."]]},{"q":"It can be inferred from paragraph 3 that people procrastinate partly because they","o":["spend too much time thinking about other people","have less brain activity when they plan ahead","do not feel strongly connected to the person they will become","expect to have more free time ten years from now"],"a":2,"ex":"לפי פסקה 3, המוח מתייחס ל«אני» העתידי כמו לאדם זר, ולכן קל להעביר אליו את העבודה. כלומר, אין חיבור חזק לאדם שנהיה בעתיד. הפסקה לא אומרת שהפעילות במוח חלשה יותר, רק שהיא דומה לחשיבה על אחרים.","w":[["infer","להסיק"],["stranger","זר"]]},{"q":"The main purpose of the last paragraph is to","o":["present ways of reducing procrastination that are based on the research","argue that procrastination cannot really be changed","describe in detail an experiment on brain activity","criticize the older view that procrastination is simply a matter of laziness or poor planning"],"a":0,"ex":"הפסקה נפתחת ב-«these findings also point to practical solutions» ומונה שלוש דרכים: לפרק משימה לצעדים, לסלוח לעצמך, ולדמיין את ה«אני» העתידי. הביקורת על ההסבר של עצלות מופיעה בפסקה 1, לא באחרונה.","w":[["strategy","אסטרטגיה, דרך פעולה"],["forgive","לסלוח"],["presumably","ככל הנראה"]]}]},"s8c3":{"id":"s8c3","tier":1,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"Because the factory's machines had become too old to repair, the owners decided to replace them all, although this required a large loan from the bank.","o":["Because the owners took a large loan from the bank, they were able to repair all of the factory's old machines instead of having to replace them with expensive new ones.","The owners replaced only some of the factory's old machines, since the rest could still be repaired cheaply without taking a large loan from the bank.","Since the old machines in the factory could no longer be fixed, the owners chose to replace every one of them, even though this meant borrowing heavily from the bank.","Because the factory's machines were too old to repair, the bank required the owners to replace them all before it would agree to give them a loan."],"a":2,"ex":"במקור: המכונות ישנות מדי לתיקון, ולכן הבעלים החליפו את כולן למרות שנדרשה הלוואה גדולה. בתשובה הנכונה «Because» הופך ל-«Since», «although» ל-«even though», ו-«a large loan» ל-«borrowing heavily». «only some» משנה את הכמות, ובאפשרות האחרונה הבנק הוא שדורש, וזה לא במקור.","w":[["since","מכיוון ש..."],["even though","אף על פי ש..."],["loan","הלוואה"]]},{"q":"Researchers at the university have shown that regular exposure to natural light during the morning can significantly improve the quality of sleep among night-shift workers.","o":["University researchers have shown that night-shift workers actually sleep worse when they are regularly exposed to natural light in the morning hours.","It has been shown by university researchers that night-shift workers may sleep considerably better if regularly exposed to natural light in the morning.","University researchers have shown that regular exposure to natural light in the morning considerably improves the sleep of all workers except those who work at night.","University researchers have shown that night-shift workers need considerably fewer hours of sleep if they regularly spend their mornings outdoors in natural light."],"a":1,"ex":"התשובה הנכונה עוברת לסביל («It has been shown by») ומחליפה «significantly» ב-«considerably». «sleep worse» הופך את התוצאה, והאפשרות השלישית מוציאה דווקא את עובדי הלילה, שהם הנושא של המחקר.","w":[["exposure","חשיפה"],["significantly","באופן משמעותי"],["considerably","במידה ניכרת"]]},{"q":"While the aquarium's shark tank draws thousands of visitors every summer, its exhibit on local river fish is rarely visited, even by people who live nearby.","o":["Both the aquarium's shark tank and its exhibit on local river fish attract thousands of visitors every summer, most of them people who live in the nearby towns.","The aquarium's exhibit on local river fish is popular mostly with residents of the area, while tourists prefer to visit the shark tank in summer.","Because its shark tank is so crowded with thousands of visitors in the summer, the aquarium has decided to close its exhibit on local river fish.","Hardly anyone, not even local residents, visits the aquarium's exhibit on river fish, in contrast to its shark tank, which attracts thousands of visitors each summer."],"a":3,"ex":"התשובה הנכונה מתחילה מהחלק השני של המקור ומחליפה «While» ב-«in contrast to», ו-«rarely» ב-«Hardly anyone». «Both» הופך ניגוד להוספה, והאפשרות השנייה טוענת שתושבי האזור כן מבקרים, בניגוד למקור.","w":[["while","בעוד ש... (ניגוד)"],["rarely","לעיתים רחוקות"],["hardly","כמעט לא"]]}]},"s8c4":{"id":"s8c4","tier":1,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"The study's conclusions should be treated with caution, since the number of participants was small and all of them came from the same neighborhood.","o":["Only a few people took part in the study, and they all lived in the same neighborhood; therefore, its conclusions must be treated carefully.","The researchers were very cautious about choosing participants, so they deliberately selected a small group of people who all came from a single neighborhood.","Although only a few people took part in the study, its conclusions are fully reliable, since all of the participants came from the same neighborhood.","The study included a large number of participants, but only some of them came from the same neighborhood, so its conclusions are uncertain."],"a":0,"ex":"במקור «since» מציג את הסיבה (מעט משתתפים מאותה שכונה) אחרי המסקנה. בתשובה הנכונה הסיבה באה קודם והמסקנה מגיעה עם «therefore». האפשרות השלישית הופכת את המסקנה ל«אמינות», והרביעית משנה את הכמות («large number», «only some»).","w":[["caution","זהירות"],["since","מכיוון ש..."],["therefore","לכן"]]},{"q":"Unless farmers in the region find new sources of water within the next decade, many of them will have to stop growing crops that need heavy irrigation.","o":["Even if farmers in the region find new sources of water in the next decade, most of them will still stop growing crops that need a lot of irrigation.","Farmers in the region have already found new sources of water, so in the next decade they will be able to grow more crops that need heavy irrigation.","If farmers in the region do not find new water sources in the next ten years, many of them will have to stop growing crops that depend on heavy irrigation.","Unless farmers in the region stop growing crops that need heavy irrigation, they will have used up all of the region's available water within the next ten years."],"a":2,"ex":"«Unless» = אלא אם כן, כלומר «if ... not». התשובה הנכונה מחליפה את «Unless» ב-«If ... do not» ושומרת על אותו תנאי ואותה תוצאה. «Even if» מבטל את התנאי, והאפשרות האחרונה הופכת את מה שתלוי במה.","w":[["unless","אלא אם כן"],["if","אם"],["irrigation","השקיה"]]},{"q":"The city planted thousands of trees along its main streets not only to provide shade for pedestrians but also to lower the temperature of the surrounding buildings.","o":["The city planted thousands of trees along its main streets to shade pedestrians from the sun, rather than to lower the temperature of the nearby buildings.","In addition to giving pedestrians shade, the thousands of trees that the city planted along its main streets were meant to cool the nearby buildings.","Since pedestrians had complained about the heat, the city planted a few trees on its main streets to cool the surrounding buildings.","The temperature of the buildings along the city's main streets dropped, so pedestrians began planting thousands of trees themselves to create more shade."],"a":1,"ex":"במקור יש שתי מטרות יחד («not only... but also»). התשובה הנכונה שומרת על שתיהן עם «In addition to». «rather than» משאיר רק מטרה אחת, והאפשרות השלישית משנה את הכמות («a few») ומוסיפה סיבה שלא במקור.","w":[["not only... but also","לא רק... אלא גם"],["in addition to","בנוסף ל... (+שם עצם)"],["pedestrian","הולך רגל"]]}]},"s8c5":{"id":"s8c5","tier":1,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"The scientist's early findings were ___ at best; only later experiments produced clear and reliable results.","o":["conclusive","celebrated","fraudulent","tentative"],"a":3,"ex":"«tentative» = זמני, לא סופי, לא בטוח. רק ניסויים מאוחרים יותר נתנו תוצאות ברורות, ולכן הממצאים הראשונים היו לא חד-משמעיים. «conclusive» (חד-משמעי, מכריע) הוא בדיוק ההפך.","w":[["tentative","זמני, לא ודאי"],["conclusive","חד-משמעי, מכריע"],["reliable","אמין"]]},{"q":"The medicine works quickly, but its effect lasts ___ two hours, which is why some patients must take it as often as ten times a day.","o":["at most","at least","far beyond","no less than"],"a":0,"ex":"«at most» = לכל היותר. ההשפעה קצרה, ולכן צריך לקחת את התרופה הרבה פעמים ביום. «at least» (לפחות) ו-«no less than» מרמזים על השפעה ארוכה, וזה לא מסביר למה צריך עשר מנות ביום.","w":[["at most","לכל היותר"],["at least","לפחות"]]},{"q":"Critics argued that the new law would ___ the rights of workers rather than protect them.","o":["safeguard","expand","clarify","erode"],"a":3,"ex":"«erode» = לשחוק, לכרסם. «rather than protect» מראה שהמבקרים חששו מההפך מהגנה: פגיעה הדרגתית בזכויות. «safeguard» (לשמור על) הוא כמעט מילה נרדפת ל-«protect», ולכן לא יוצר ניגוד.","w":[["erode","לשחוק, לכרסם"],["rather than","במקום, ולא"],["safeguard","לשמור על, להגן"]]},{"q":"The novel was completed in 1920; ___, it remained unpublished until 1965, long after the author's death.","o":["accordingly","likewise","nonetheless","for instance"],"a":2,"ex":"«nonetheless» = בכל זאת, למרות זאת. הרומן היה גמור, ולמרות זאת לא פורסם עשרות שנים: יש כאן ניגוד. «accordingly» (בהתאם לכך) לא מתאים, כי סיום הכתיבה לא גורם לכך שהספר לא יפורסם.","w":[["nonetheless","בכל זאת, למרות זאת"],["accordingly","בהתאם לכך, לכן"]]}]},"s9c0":{"id":"s9c0","tier":2,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"The scientist's early findings were met with doubt, but they were later ___ by several larger studies that reached exactly the same conclusion.","o":["refuted","corroborated","fabricated","overlooked"],"a":1,"ex":"«corroborate» = לאשש, לחזק. מחקרים גדולים שהגיעו בדיוק לאותה מסקנה מאשרים את הממצאים. «refuted» (הופרכו) הוא ההפך: מחקרים שמגיעים לאותה מסקנה לא מפריכים.","w":[["corroborate","לאשש, לחזק"],["refute","להפריך"],["fabricate","לבדות, לזייף"]]},{"q":"The new hiring policy has, ___, caused some confusion among employees; on the whole, though, it has made the process considerably fairer.","o":["consequently","likewise","namely","admittedly"],"a":3,"ex":"«admittedly» = יש להודות ש... הכותב מודה בחיסרון (בלבול), ואחר כך אומר «though» שבסך הכול המדיניות טובה. «consequently» (כתוצאה מכך) דורש סיבה קודמת, ואין כזו במשפט.","w":[["admittedly","יש להודות ש..."],["consequently","כתוצאה מכך, לפיכך"],["considerably","במידה ניכרת"]]},{"q":"Because the ancient poem survives only in a few ___ copies, scholars must often guess at the words that have been lost.","o":["fragmentary","pristine","voluminous","legible"],"a":0,"ex":"«fragmentary» = חלקי, מקוטע. החוקרים צריכים לנחש מילים שאבדו, ולכן ההעתקים חסרים. «pristine» (שמור בשלמותו) הוא ההפך: בהעתק שלם לא היה צורך לנחש.","w":[["fragmentary","חלקי, מקוטע"],["pristine","שמור בשלמותו, כחדש"],["legible","קריא"]]},{"q":"Most residents could barely afford the rising rents, ___ buy a home in the neighborhood where they had grown up.","o":["as well as","rather than","let alone","apart from"],"a":2,"ex":"«let alone» = ובטח שלא, קל וחומר. אם בקושי יכלו לשלם שכירות, בטח שלא יכלו לקנות בית. «as well as» (וגם) היה אומר שהם כן יכלו לקנות בית, וזה סותר את «barely».","w":[["let alone","ובטח שלא, קל וחומר"],["barely","בקושי, כמעט לא"],["as well as","וגם, בנוסף ל..."]]}]},"s9c1":{"id":"s9c1","tier":2,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"Talks between the two unions reached a complete ___ when neither side was willing to make any further concessions.","o":["outset","milestone","impasse","consensus"],"a":2,"ex":"«impasse» = מבוי סתום. כשאף צד לא מוכן לוותר, השיחות נתקעות. «consensus» (הסכמה כללית) הוא ההפך: בלי ויתורים לא מגיעים להסכמה.","w":[["impasse","מבוי סתום"],["concession","ויתור"],["consensus","הסכמה כללית"]]},{"q":"The bridge will reopen to traffic ___ engineers confirm that its supports can bear the weight; until then, it will remain closed.","o":["provided that","even if","lest","whereas"],"a":0,"ex":"«provided that» = בתנאי ש... הגשר ייפתח רק אחרי שהמהנדסים יאשרו, וזה מה שהחלק השני אומר (עד אז הוא סגור). «even if» (גם אם) היה אומר שהאישור לא משנה, וזה סותר את «until then».","w":[["provided that","בתנאי ש..."],["even if","גם אם, אפילו אם"],["bear","לשאת, לעמוד ב..."]]},{"q":"The side effects of the treatment proved ___: in most patients they disappeared completely within a few days.","o":["substantial","permanent","cumulative","transient"],"a":3,"ex":"«transient» = חולף, זמני. מה שבא אחרי הנקודתיים מסביר: תופעות הלוואי נעלמו תוך כמה ימים. «permanent» (קבוע) הוא ההפך הגמור.","w":[["transient","חולף, זמני"],["cumulative","מצטבר"],["permanent","קבוע"]]},{"q":"Emissions from the factory fell sharply after new filters were installed, ___ air quality in the town improved only slightly, since most pollution came from traffic.","o":["thus","whereas","so that","inasmuch as"],"a":1,"ex":"«whereas» = בעוד ש..., ואילו. הפליטות ירדו בחדות, ואילו האוויר השתפר רק מעט: זה ניגוד. «thus» (לפיכך) היה הופך את השיפור הקטן לתוצאה של הירידה, אבל המשפט אומר שהסיבה היא התנועה בכבישים.","w":[["whereas","בעוד ש..., ואילו"],["thus","לפיכך, כך"],["emissions","פליטות"]]}]},"s9c2":{"id":"s9c2","tier":2,"type":"rc","title":"The Price of a Free Ride","text":["Over the past two decades, a growing number of cities have experimented with abolishing fares on buses and trams. The appeal is easy to understand. Supporters argue that free transport benefits low-income residents, who spend a larger share of their earnings on travel, and that it persuades drivers to leave their cars at home, which in turn eases congestion and cuts emissions. Yet the experience of the cities that have actually tried the policy suggests that its effects are more modest, and more complicated, than its advocates often claim.","The first lesson concerns ridership. In almost every case, the number of passengers rose once fares were removed, sometimes considerably. However, surveys of the new riders revealed that relatively few of them had previously driven. Most had formerly walked or cycled, or had simply made fewer trips. In other words, the policy did increase the use of public transport, but it did little to reduce traffic, which was one of its central goals. Some planners concluded that the price of a ticket matters less to drivers than the speed, frequency and reliability of the service.","The second lesson concerns money. Fares rarely cover the full cost of running a transport system, but in many cities they still provide a substantial portion of its budget. Once that income disappears, it must be replaced, usually by raising local taxes or by cutting other public services. Moreover, the additional passengers place further strain on vehicles that may already be crowded, so a city that abolishes fares may soon have to buy more buses and hire more drivers. Critics point out that the same funds could instead be invested in improving the service itself.","None of this means that free transport is necessarily a mistake. In small towns, where ticket sales bring in little revenue and collecting fares is itself costly, eliminating them can make financial sense. Furthermore, some researchers maintain that the policy should be judged by its social benefits, such as greater mobility for elderly and poor residents, rather than by its impact on traffic. The debate, then, is not simply about whether free transport works, but about what, exactly, it is supposed to achieve."],"qs":[{"q":"Which of the following is the best title for the passage?","o":["Why Every City Should Abolish Bus Fares","Free Public Transport: Promises and Results","How Ticket Prices Shape Drivers' Choices","The Rise of the Tram in Small Towns"],"a":1,"ex":"הקטע מציג מה תומכי התחבורה החינמית מבטיחים (פסקה 1) ומה קרה בפועל בערים שניסו (פסקאות 2-4). הוא לא ממליץ לכל עיר לבטל תשלום, ו«מחירי הכרטיסים והנהגים» הוא רק פרט אחד מפסקה 2.","w":[["abolish","לבטל"],["advocate","תומך, חסיד"]]},{"q":"According to the second paragraph, most of the new passengers attracted by free transport","o":["had stopped driving to work","used the service only occasionally","complained that the vehicles were crowded","had not previously traveled by car"],"a":3,"ex":"בפסקה 2 כתוב שמעטים מהנוסעים החדשים נהגו קודם, ורובם הלכו ברגל, רכבו על אופניים או נסעו פחות. לכן רובם לא הגיעו מהרכב. הצפיפות מוזכרת רק בפסקה 3, ולא כתלונה של נוסעים.","w":[["relatively","יחסית"],["formerly","לשעבר, בעבר"],["in other words","במילים אחרות"]]},{"q":"In the third paragraph, 'that income' refers to","o":["the money collected from fares","the money raised through local taxes","the full cost of running a transport system","the funds needed to buy more buses"],"a":0,"ex":"המשפט הקודם מדבר על דמי הנסיעה (fares) שמממנים חלק ניכר מהתקציב. «that income» היא ההכנסה הזו, שנעלמת כשמבטלים את התשלום. המסים המקומיים הם מה שמחליף אותה, לא היא עצמה.","w":[["income","הכנסה"],["substantial","ניכר, משמעותי"],["portion","חלק"]]},{"q":"The last paragraph mainly serves to","o":["argue that free transport should be limited to large cities","show that free transport has failed to achieve its goals in every city that has tried it","suggest that the value of free transport depends partly on what it is meant to achieve","explain why collecting fares costs little in small towns"],"a":2,"ex":"הפסקה האחרונה מאזנת את הביקורת: בעיירות קטנות זה יכול להשתלם, ויש מי שמודד את המדיניות לפי התועלת החברתית. המשפט האחרון אומר שהוויכוח הוא על המטרה. הפסקה מדברת על עיירות קטנות ולא על ערים גדולות, ושם גביית דמי נסיעה דווקא יקרה.","w":[["necessarily","בהכרח"],["maintain","לטעון; לשמר"],["rather than","במקום, ולא"]]},{"q":"It can be inferred from the second paragraph that some planners believe drivers would be more willing to use public transport if","o":["buses and trams came more often and kept to their schedules","fares were reduced rather than abolished completely","more residents chose to walk or cycle instead of driving their own cars","the cities spent less money on new vehicles"],"a":0,"ex":"בסוף פסקה 2 המתכננים אומרים שלנהגים המחיר חשוב פחות מהמהירות, התדירות והאמינות של השירות. מכאן שבשירות תדיר ואמין יותר הם היו עוברים. הוזלה חלקית במקום ביטול לא מוזכרת בכלל, וגם לפי הקטע המחיר הוא לא העיקר.","w":[["infer","להסיק"],["frequency","תדירות"],["reliability","אמינות"]]}]},"s9c3":{"id":"s9c3","tier":2,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"Although the reform was intended to benefit all small businesses, only those with fewer than ten employees saw any meaningful reduction in their administrative costs during its first year.","o":["The reform, which aimed to help every small business, lowered administrative costs for most of them in its first year, particularly for firms with fewer than ten workers.","Only businesses with fewer than ten employees were meant to benefit from the reform, and as a result they alone saw their administrative costs fall in its first year.","Though designed to help every small business, the reform meaningfully cut administrative costs in its first year solely for firms that employed fewer than ten people.","Small businesses with fewer than ten employees benefited from the reform during its first year, yet their administrative costs rose more sharply than those of larger firms."],"a":2,"ex":"במקור: הרפורמה נועדה לעזור לכל העסקים הקטנים, אבל רק עסקים עם פחות מעשרה עובדים נהנו ממנה (only = solely). התשובה הראשונה מלכודת: «most of them» אומר שרוב העסקים נהנו. השנייה משנה את הכוונה: לפי המקור הרפורמה נועדה לכולם.","w":[["solely","אך ורק, בלעדית"],["intend","להתכוון, לייעד"],["meaningful","משמעותי"]]},{"q":"Neighborhoods with more street trees tend to report lower rates of anxiety, but researchers stress that wealthier areas usually have both more trees and better access to health care.","o":["Planting more street trees lowers residents' anxiety, which is why researchers recommend that wealthier neighborhoods should also improve their residents' access to health care.","Lower rates of anxiety are found where street trees are common; however, researchers emphasize that richer areas generally have not only more trees but also better health care.","Researchers stress that street trees reduce anxiety only in wealthier neighborhoods, where residents also tend to enjoy better access to health care than people living elsewhere.","Because wealthier neighborhoods have better access to health care, researchers have concluded that street trees have no effect whatsoever on the anxiety levels of residents."],"a":1,"ex":"המקור מתאר קשר (מתאם) בין עצים לחרדה נמוכה, ומזהיר שבשכונות עשירות יש גם עצים וגם רפואה טובה, כלומר אולי העושר הוא הגורם. התשובה הראשונה הופכת את הקשר לסיבה ותוצאה. האחרונה מגזימה: החוקרים לא קבעו שלעצים אין שום השפעה.","w":[["tend to","נוטה ל..."],["not only... but also","לא רק... אלא גם"],["stress","להדגיש"]]},{"q":"Few of the volunteers who completed the language course became fluent, yet nearly all of them reported that it had made them more confident when speaking with native speakers.","o":["Hardly any of the volunteers who finished the language course achieved fluency; nevertheless, almost all of them said it had increased their confidence with native speakers.","Nearly all the volunteers who finished the language course became fluent, and as a result they reported feeling much more confident when speaking with native speakers.","A few of the volunteers who completed the language course became fluent, which explains why almost all of them felt more confident when speaking with native speakers.","Although most volunteers who completed the language course felt more confident, few of them were actually willing to speak with native speakers once it had ended."],"a":0,"ex":"«few» = מעט (כמעט אין) = «hardly any», ו-«yet» = «nevertheless». מעטים הגיעו לשטף, ובכל זאת כמעט כולם הרגישו בטוחים יותר. התשובה השלישית מלכודת: היא הופכת את השטף של מעטים לסיבה לביטחון של כולם, קשר שאין במקור.","w":[["few","מעט (כמעט אין)"],["nevertheless","למרות זאת, אף על פי כן"],["fluent","שוטף (בשפה)"]]}]},"s9c4":{"id":"s9c4","tier":2,"type":"rs","qs":[{"q":"The newly discovered settlement is not merely older than archaeologists had assumed; it also appears to have been inhabited continuously for several centuries rather than for a few decades.","o":["Archaeologists had assumed that the newly discovered settlement was inhabited for several centuries, but it now turns out to have been occupied for only a few decades.","The newly discovered settlement is somewhat older than archaeologists had assumed, although it was probably abandoned and resettled several times over the centuries.","Because the newly discovered settlement was inhabited continuously for several centuries, archaeologists had correctly assumed that it was older than the other sites nearby.","Besides being older than archaeologists had believed, the newly discovered settlement seems to have been occupied without interruption for centuries, not just for several decades."],"a":3,"ex":"«not merely... also» = לא רק... אלא גם, ולכן «Besides». היישוב עתיק יותר מהצפוי, וגם היה מיושב ברציפות (continuously = without interruption) מאות שנים. התשובה השנייה מלכודת: «abandoned and resettled» סותר את הרציפות.","w":[["merely","רק, לא יותר מ..."],["continuously","ברציפות"],["inhabit","לגור, לאכלס"]]},{"q":"The decline in the lake's fish population was initially blamed on overfishing, but subsequent studies indicated that rising water temperatures were largely responsible for it.","o":["Subsequent studies showed that overfishing, rather than rising water temperatures, was the main reason why the number of fish in the lake had declined.","Later studies indicated that the lake's fish population had shrunk solely because of warmer water, and that overfishing had in fact never taken place there.","At first, overfishing was held responsible for the shrinking number of fish in the lake; later research, however, pointed mainly to warmer water.","Rising water temperatures were partly caused by overfishing, according to the studies that examined why the lake's fish population had declined."],"a":2,"ex":"בהתחלה האשימו את הדיג המופרז, ואחר כך המחקרים הצביעו בעיקר (largely = mainly) על התחממות המים. התשובה השנייה מלכודת: «solely» (אך ורק) חזק מ-«largely», והיא גם מוסיפה שלא היה דיג מופרז בכלל. הראשונה הופכת את המסקנה.","w":[["subsequent","שלאחר מכן, מאוחר יותר"],["largely","במידה רבה, בעיקר"],["solely","אך ורק, בלעדית"]]},{"q":"The new vaccine offers strong protection to adults under sixty, whereas its effectiveness in older patients remains uncertain, since too few of them took part in the clinical trials.","o":["Since few patients over sixty took part in the clinical trials, the new vaccine turned out to be less effective for them than it is for younger adults.","The new vaccine protects adults under sixty well, but how effective it is for older patients is still unclear, as the trials included too few of them.","The new vaccine offers strong protection to adults of all ages, although older patients were somewhat less willing to take part in the clinical trials.","Because the new vaccine proved ineffective in older patients, only a small number of them were included in the trials, which focused on younger adults."],"a":1,"ex":"במקור: החיסון מגן היטב על צעירים מ-60, ואצל מבוגרים יותר פשוט לא יודעים (uncertain = unclear), כי היו מעט מהם בניסויים. התשובה הראשונה מלכודת: היא הופכת «לא ידוע» ל«פחות יעיל». הרביעית הופכת סיבה ותוצאה.","w":[["whereas","בעוד ש..., ואילו"],["uncertain","לא ודאי, לא ידוע"],["take part in","להשתתף ב..."]]}]},"s9c5":{"id":"s9c5","tier":2,"type":"sc","qs":[{"q":"Rather than relying on a single source, the historian ___ evidence from dozens of letters, diaries and official records.","o":["compiled","discarded","concealed","fabricated"],"a":0,"ex":"«compile» = לאסוף ולרכז. במקום מקור אחד, ההיסטוריון אסף ראיות מעשרות מקורות. «discarded» (השליך) הוא ההפך: מי שזורק את המקורות לא מפסיק להסתמך על מקור אחד.","w":[["compile","לאסוף, לרכז"],["discard","להשליך, לזנוח"],["rather than","במקום, ולא"]]},{"q":"The museum's collection, ___ its famous sculptures, includes thousands of ancient coins that are rarely shown to the public.","o":["instead of","by virtue of","aside from","in favor of"],"a":2,"ex":"«aside from» = מלבד. מלבד הפסלים המפורסמים, באוסף יש גם אלפי מטבעות. «instead of» (במקום) היה אומר שאין באוסף פסלים, וזה סותר את «its famous sculptures».","w":[["aside from","מלבד"],["instead of","במקום"],["by virtue of","מתוקף, בזכות"]]},{"q":"To many listeners, the senator's apology sounded ___, since he went on to repeat the very claims he was apologizing for.","o":["heartfelt","hollow","timely","explicit"],"a":1,"ex":"«hollow» = חלול, ריק מתוכן. מי שמתנצל וממשיך לחזור על אותן טענות לא באמת מתכוון. «heartfelt» (כן, מכל הלב) הוא ההפך, וסותר את הסיבה שבסוף המשפט.","w":[["hollow","חלול, ריק מתוכן"],["heartfelt","כן, מכל הלב"],["the very","אותו עצמו, בדיוק אותו"]]},{"q":"Workers are required to wear protective masks at all times, ___ they inhale the toxic dust produced by the machines.","o":["so that","unless","whereas","lest"],"a":3,"ex":"«lest» = פן, כדי שלא. חובשים מסכה כדי שלא ינשמו את האבק הרעיל. «so that» (כדי ש) הופך את המטרה: כאילו המסכה נועדה לגרום להם לנשום אבק.","w":[["lest","פן, שמא, כדי שלא"],["so that","כדי ש..."],["inhale","לשאוף, לנשום פנימה"]]}]}};
